{"turn": 2, "role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call_00_cyAQjTVwicQoVvwuAdWp2573", "tool_name": "read", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/documents/engagement-letter.docx\"}", "result": "**BIRCHWOOD & HALE LLP** **Attorneys at Law --- Real Estate \\| Corporate \\| Litigation** 191 Peachtree Street NE, Suite 4200 Atlanta, GA 30303 Tel: (404) 555-8200 \\| Fax: (404) 555-8201 www.birchwoodhale.com\n\nDecember 5, 2024\n\nMr. Marcus Aldaine Managing Director Galleon Capital Advisors LLC 1200 Peachtree Street NE, Suite 3100 Atlanta, GA 30309\n\n**Re: Engagement for Lease Abstraction and Due Diligence Review --- Acquisition of 12-Property Mixed-Use Portfolio from Thornfield Realty Holdings LP; Purchase Price: \\$187,500,000**\n\nDear Mr. Aldaine:\n\n**[1. Purpose of Engagement]{.underline}**\n\nI am writing on behalf of Birchwood & Hale LLP to confirm the firm\\'s engagement by Galleon Capital Advisors LLC (\\\"Galleon\\\" or \\\"Client\\\") in connection with the lease abstraction and due diligence review of seven (7) key commercial leases within the twelve-property mixed-use portfolio (the \\\"Portfolio\\\") being acquired by Galleon from Thornfield Realty Holdings LP (\\\"Thornfield\\\" or \\\"Seller\\\") for a purchase price of One Hundred Eighty-Seven Million Five Hundred Thousand Dollars (\\$187,500,000) (the \\\"Acquisition\\\"). This engagement arises in connection with the Purchase and Sale Agreement executed by the parties on November 15, 2024 (the \\\"PSA\\\"). We understand that the due diligence period under the PSA commenced on November 16, 2024 and expires on January 31, 2025, a period of seventy-seven (77) days, with a target closing date of March 15, 2025.\n\nGalleon has requested that Birchwood & Hale extract, organize, and analyze the material terms of seven commercial leases across the Portfolio and deliver a comprehensive lease abstraction report (the \\\"Report\\\") that will assist Galleon in evaluating the leased assets, identifying risk items, and informing pre-closing negotiations and decision-making. My colleague Devon Pratt, Senior Associate, will serve as the day-to-day lead attorney on the lease review, and I will provide oversight and be available to address any matters requiring partner-level attention.\n\n**[2. Scope of Engagement]{.underline}**\n\nThe scope of the firm\\'s engagement is defined as follows:\n\n**(a) Lease Abstraction.** Birchwood & Hale will review and abstract the following seven (7) commercial leases across the Portfolio:\n\n> 1\\. **Apex Fulfillment Services Inc.** --- Thornfield Distribution Center, 4200 Logistics Parkway, Charlotte, NC 28214 (approximately 87,500 RSF warehouse/distribution space);\n>\n> 2\\. **Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS, PA** --- Millbrook Medical Plaza, 1585 Millbrook Road, Suite 200, Raleigh, NC 27609 (approximately 3,200 RSF medical/dental office);\n>\n> 3\\. **BrightPath Learning Centers LLC** --- Millbrook Medical Plaza, 1585 Millbrook Road, Suite 100, Raleigh, NC 27609 (approximately 5,800 RSF childcare facility);\n>\n> 4\\. **Southeastern Fire & Safety Equipment Co.** --- Greystone Industrial Park, 770 Greystone Boulevard, Unit 12, Gastonia, NC 28052 (approximately 22,000 RSF industrial/flex space);\n>\n> 5\\. **Verdana Software Solutions Inc.** --- Concord Office Tower, 300 Concord Plaza Drive, 8th Floor, Atlanta, GA 30309 (approximately 18,750 RSF Class A office);\n>\n> 6\\. **The Pint & Platter Restaurant Group LLC** --- Haywood Village Shops, 92 Haywood Street, Unit 4, Asheville, NC 28801 (approximately 4,400 RSF ground-floor retail/restaurant); and\n>\n> 7\\. **United States of America (General Services Administration)**, GSA Lease No. GS-04B-15678 --- Concord Office Tower, 300 Concord Plaza Drive, 5th Floor, Atlanta, GA 30309 (approximately 15,000 RSF government office).\n\n**(b) Rent Roll Cross-Reference.** The firm will cross-reference the lease terms as abstracted against the portfolio rent roll prepared by Thornfield\\'s property manager, Karen Osgood, to identify any inconsistencies between the rent roll and the underlying lease documents.\n\n**(c) Rent Escalation Verification.** The firm will independently verify all rent escalation calculations and financial terms stated in each lease, including base rent schedules, percentage rent calculations (if applicable), CPI adjustment mechanics, and any free rent or abatement provisions.\n\n**(d) Risk Identification.** The firm will identify and flag any mathematical discrepancies, ambiguous provisions, missing documentation or protections, approaching deadlines (including option exercise dates, renewal notice periods, and co-tenancy triggers), holdover situations, and other risk items that may affect Galleon\\'s valuation of the Portfolio or the closing of the Acquisition.\n\n**(e) Standardized Abstraction Report.** The firm will prepare a standardized lease abstraction report covering the following twelve (12) categories of terms for each lease:\n\n> \\(1\\) Tenant and Premises; (2) Term; (3) Rent; (4) Lease Type; (5) Operating Expenses; (6) Renewal Options; (7) Termination Rights; (8) Assignment and Subletting; (9) Security Deposit / Guaranty; (10) Tenant Improvements; (11) Special Provisions; and (12) Risk Flags.\n\n**(f) Executive Summary.** The Report will include an Executive Summary providing portfolio-level analysis, including: aggregate current annual base rent (estimated at approximately \\$2,347,843.50 across the seven leases); weighted average remaining lease term; tenant concentration analysis; a prioritized listing of risk items; and recommended pre-closing actions for Galleon\\'s consideration.\n\nThe seven leases subject to this engagement represent approximately 156,650 RSF of the total Portfolio\\'s 243,650 RSF across all twelve properties. The remaining five properties are being reviewed under separate workstreams outside the scope of this engagement.\n\n**Scope Limitations.** This engagement does not include: title review (which we understand is being handled by Stonebridge Title & Escrow LLC); environmental due diligence (being handled by Hanover Environmental Consultants Inc.); financial or accounting review of Thornfield\\'s books and records (maintained by Crestline Accounting Group LLP); debt placement or financing activities (being handled by Fieldstone Capital Markets LLC); or brokerage matters (listing broker: Ridgeview Realty Brokers Inc.). The firm is not providing tax advice in connection with this engagement, and Galleon is encouraged to consult with its tax advisors as appropriate.\n\n**[3. Deliverables and Timeline]{.underline}**\n\n**Primary Deliverable.** The primary deliverable under this engagement is the comprehensive Lease Abstraction Report (the \\\"Report\\\"), to be delivered in Microsoft Word format. The Report will include: (i) individual lease abstractions for each of the seven leases in the twelve-category format described in Section 2(e) above; (ii) a portfolio rent roll cross-check identifying any discrepancies between the lease documents and the rent roll provided by Thornfield\\'s property manager; (iii) a risk matrix identifying and prioritizing all flagged items by severity and time-sensitivity; and (iv) specific recommended actions for Galleon\\'s consideration prior to the March 15, 2025 target closing date.\n\n**Delivery Deadline.** The firm will use commercially reasonable efforts to deliver the final Report by **December 20, 2024**. This timeline is designed to provide Galleon approximately six (6) weeks within the remaining due diligence period (which expires January 31, 2025) to act on any identified issues, request estoppels or additional documentation from the Seller, and negotiate appropriate protections or purchase price adjustments as warranted.\n\n**Interim Communication.** Devon Pratt will provide weekly status updates to Marcus Aldaine by email regarding the progress of the lease review. In addition, the firm will promptly communicate any material risk items or time-sensitive findings as they arise during the review process and will not wait for delivery of the final Report to flag critical items requiring immediate attention.\n\n**Document Access.** Galleon will arrange for delivery of complete lease files --- including all amendments, exhibits, side letters, subordination, non-disturbance and attornment agreements (SNDAs), estoppel certificates, and guaranties --- to Birchwood & Hale no later than **December 6, 2024**. Delays in the delivery of lease documents or supporting materials may extend the December 20, 2024 delivery timeline, and the firm will notify Galleon promptly if any such delay is anticipated.\n\n**[4. Fee Arrangement]{.underline}**\n\n**Hourly Rates.** Fees for this engagement will be billed on a time-and-materials basis at the following standard hourly rates:\n\n  -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  **Professional**                    **Rate**\n  ----------------------------------- -----------------------------------\n  Lydia Chen, Partner                 \\$575/hour\n\n  Devon Pratt, Senior Associate       \\$385/hour\n\n  Paralegal Support                   \\$195/hour\n  -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**Fee Cap.** Total professional fees for the lease abstraction engagement described herein shall not exceed **Forty-Five Thousand Dollars (\\$45,000)** (the \\\"Fee Cap\\\"), inclusive of all attorney and paralegal time. The Fee Cap does not include out-of-pocket disbursements (e.g., travel expenses, copying, courier services, and database access fees), which will be billed at cost and are estimated not to exceed One Thousand Five Hundred Dollars (\\$1,500).\n\n**Scope Adjustments.** The Fee Cap is predicated on the assumption that the scope of the engagement is limited to the seven (7) leases and the rent roll described in Section 2 above. If Galleon requests that the firm review additional leases from the remaining five portfolio properties, or if the scope of the engagement expands materially (for example, to include lease renegotiations, amendment drafting, or estoppel review beyond what is contained in existing lease files), fees for such additional work will be billed outside the Fee Cap at the standard hourly rates set forth above, subject to prior written approval from Galleon.\n\n**Invoicing and Payment.** The firm will issue monthly invoices containing customary detail of time entries and disbursements. Payment is due within thirty (30) days of the invoice date. No retainer is required for this engagement.\n\n**[5. Client Responsibilities]{.underline}**\n\nGalleon agrees to fulfill the following responsibilities in connection with this engagement:\n\n> \\(a\\) Provide complete and accurate copies of all lease documents, amendments, exhibits, rent rolls, tenant correspondence, and related materials in Galleon\\'s possession or obtainable from the Seller (Thornfield Realty Holdings LP, through Renata Thornfield-Kiess, President, or Karen Osgood, Property Manager) in a timely manner;\n>\n> \\(b\\) Designate Marcus Aldaine as the primary contact for all matters related to the engagement, with authority to provide instructions and approvals on behalf of Galleon;\n>\n> \\(c\\) Respond promptly to requests for additional information, clarification, or direction from the firm\\'s engagement team; and\n>\n> \\(d\\) Acknowledge that the firm\\'s analysis will be based solely on the documents provided to the firm by Galleon or on Galleon\\'s behalf. Birchwood & Hale is not responsible for verifying facts, representations, or conditions beyond the four corners of the lease documents and rent roll unless specifically directed to do so in writing by Galleon.\n\n**[6. Confidentiality]{.underline}**\n\nBirchwood & Hale will maintain the confidentiality of all information provided by or on behalf of Galleon in connection with this engagement. Such information will not be disclosed to third parties without Galleon\\'s prior written consent, except as may be required by applicable law, court order, or professional obligation. The foregoing confidentiality obligation does not extend to information that is or becomes publicly available through no fault of the firm, or that is independently known to the firm from sources unrelated to this engagement.\n\n**[7. Conflicts Check]{.underline}**\n\nThe firm has conducted a conflicts check in connection with this engagement and confirms that Birchwood & Hale does not currently represent Thornfield Realty Holdings LP, Thornfield Management Corp., any of the seven tenants listed in Section 2(a) above, Highpoint National Bank (lender on the Thornfield Distribution Center), or any other party to the Acquisition in a matter adverse to Galleon. Should a conflict of interest arise during the course of the engagement, the firm will promptly notify Galleon and take appropriate steps to address the conflict, which may include withdrawal from the engagement if the conflict cannot be resolved or waived in accordance with applicable rules of professional conduct.\n\n**[8. Limitation of Liability / Disclaimer]{.underline}**\n\nThe Report is prepared for the sole use of Galleon Capital Advisors LLC and its authorized representatives in connection with the evaluation of the Portfolio acquisition described herein. The Report is not intended to be relied upon by any third party, including lenders (including Fieldstone Capital Markets LLC in its capacity as debt placement agent), title companies, insurers, or other advisors, without the prior written consent of Birchwood & Hale LLP. The Report constitutes legal analysis based upon the documents provided to the firm and does not guarantee the enforceability of any lease provision, the creditworthiness or financial condition of any tenant, or the accuracy of any representation made by the Seller or any third party. Galleon is encouraged to independently verify all financial information and conduct such additional due diligence as it deems appropriate in connection with the Acquisition.\n\n**[9. Governing Law and Dispute Resolution]{.underline}**\n\nThis engagement letter shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of Georgia, without regard to its conflicts-of-law principles. Any disputes arising out of or related to this engagement or the services provided hereunder shall be resolved by binding arbitration in Atlanta, Georgia, administered under the Commercial Arbitration Rules of the American Arbitration Association then in effect.\n\n**[10. Acceptance]{.underline}**\n\nPlease confirm Galleon\\'s agreement to the terms of this engagement by signing and returning a copy of this letter to my attention. This engagement letter, once countersigned, supersedes any prior oral or written understandings between Birchwood & Hale LLP and Galleon Capital Advisors LLC regarding the scope of work described herein.\n\nWe look forward to working with you on this important acquisition. Please do not hesitate to contact me or Devon Pratt if you have any questions regarding the terms of this engagement or the lease review process.\n\nVery truly yours,\n\n**BIRCHWOOD & HALE LLP**\n\nBy: **\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_**\n\nName: Lydia Chen\n\nTitle: Partner\n\nDate: **\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_**\n\n**ACKNOWLEDGED AND AGREED:**\n\n**GALLEON CAPITAL ADVISORS LLC**\n\nBy: **\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_**\n\nName: Marcus Aldaine\n\nTitle: Managing Director\n\nDate: **\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_**\n\ncc: Devon Pratt, Senior Associate, Birchwood & Hale LLP\n"}
