{"turn": 5, "role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call_00_JknHLddojhCNUmv4wUIb8848", "tool_name": "read", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/documents/soto-dds-lease.docx\"}", "result": "**[MEDICAL OFFICE LEASE AGREEMENT]{.underline}**\n\n**Millbrook Medical Plaza** **1585 Millbrook Road, Raleigh, North Carolina 27609**\n\nThis Medical Office Lease Agreement (this \\\"Lease\\\") is made and entered into as of September 15, 2021 (the \\\"Lease Date\\\"), by and between **Thornfield Realty Holdings LP**, a North Carolina limited partnership, whose general partner is Thornfield Management Corp., a North Carolina corporation, with its registered office at 500 South Tryon Street, Suite 2200, Charlotte, NC 28202 (\\\"Landlord\\\"), and **Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS, PA**, a North Carolina professional association (\\\"Tenant\\\"). Landlord and Tenant are sometimes referred to herein individually as a \\\"Party\\\" and collectively as the \\\"Parties.\\\"\n\nIn consideration of the mutual covenants and agreements set forth herein, and for other good and valuable consideration, the receipt and sufficiency of which are hereby acknowledged, the Parties agree as follows:\n\n**[ARTICLE 1 --- DEFINITIONS AND BASIC LEASE PROVISIONS]{.underline}**\n\n**Section 1.1 --- Definitions**\n\nAs used in this Lease, the following capitalized terms shall have the meanings set forth below:\n\n**\\\"Additional Rent\\\"** means all sums payable by Tenant to Landlord under this Lease other than Base Rent, including without limitation Tenant\\'s proportionate share of Operating Expense and Real Estate Tax escalations as described in Section 4.2.\n\n**\\\"Base Rent\\\"** means the base rental amounts payable by Tenant as set forth in the Rent Schedule contained in Section 4.1 of this Lease.\n\n**\\\"Base Year\\\"** means calendar year 2022 for purposes of calculating Operating Expense and Real Estate Tax escalations.\n\n**\\\"Building\\\"** means the building known as Millbrook Medical Plaza located at 1585 Millbrook Road, Raleigh, NC 27609, together with all improvements, fixtures, and appurtenances thereto.\n\n**\\\"Commencement Date\\\"** means November 1, 2021.\n\n**\\\"Common Areas\\\"** means all areas within the Building and surrounding property intended for the shared use and benefit of tenants, their employees, patients, and invitees, including without limitation lobbies, corridors, stairwells, restrooms, parking areas, driveways, sidewalks, and landscaped areas.\n\n**\\\"Expiration Date\\\"** means October 31, 2028.\n\n**\\\"Landlord\\\"** means Thornfield Realty Holdings LP, a North Carolina limited partnership.\n\n**\\\"Lease Date\\\"** means September 15, 2021.\n\n**\\\"Lease Term\\\"** or **\\\"Term\\\"** means the period commencing on the Commencement Date and expiring on the Expiration Date, unless earlier terminated or extended as provided herein.\n\n**\\\"Lease Year\\\"** means each successive twelve (12) month period beginning on the Commencement Date. Year 1 shall be the period from November 1, 2021 through October 31, 2022; Year 2 shall be November 1, 2022 through October 31, 2023; and so on for each subsequent Lease Year throughout the Term.\n\n**\\\"Operating Expenses\\\"** means all costs and expenses incurred by Landlord in the operation, management, maintenance, and repair of the Building and Common Areas, including but not limited to insurance premiums, management fees (not to exceed a market-rate percentage), utilities, landscaping, janitorial services for the Common Areas, security, and general administrative expenses, but excluding (i) capital expenditures, except to the extent amortized over their useful life in accordance with generally accepted accounting principles (\\\"GAAP\\\"), (ii) leasing commissions, (iii) costs of tenant improvements for specific tenants, and (iv) depreciation.\n\n**\\\"Permitted Use\\\"** means medical and dental office use only, as further described in Article 5.\n\n**\\\"Premises\\\"** means Suite 200, located on the second (2nd) floor of the Building, containing approximately 3,200 rentable square feet (\\\"RSF\\\"), as more particularly depicted on Exhibit A attached hereto and incorporated herein by reference.\n\n**\\\"Property Manager\\\"** means Karen Osgood, or such other person or entity as Landlord may designate from time to time by written notice to Tenant.\n\n**\\\"Real Estate Taxes\\\"** means all taxes, assessments, special assessments, and governmental charges of every kind and nature levied upon or assessed against the Building and the underlying land, including any tax levied in whole or in part in lieu of or in addition to real property taxes.\n\n**\\\"Rent\\\"** means, collectively, Base Rent and Additional Rent.\n\n**\\\"Rentable Square Feet\\\"** or **\\\"RSF\\\"** means 3,200 RSF for the Premises, as determined in accordance with Section 2.2.\n\n**\\\"Tenant\\\"** means Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS, PA, a North Carolina professional association.\n\n**\\\"Tenant Improvement Allowance\\\"** or **\\\"TI Allowance\\\"** means the allowance of Twelve Dollars (\\$12.00) per RSF provided by Landlord toward the cost of Tenant Improvements, as more particularly described in Article 8.\n\n**Section 1.2 --- Basic Lease Provisions Summary**\n\nThe following is a summary of certain basic terms of this Lease for convenient reference. In the event of any conflict between the provisions of this Section 1.2 and the more detailed provisions of this Lease, the more detailed provisions shall control.\n\n  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  **Item**                            **Description**\n  ----------------------------------- --------------------------------------------------------------\n  Landlord                            Thornfield Realty Holdings LP\n\n  Tenant                              Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS, PA\n\n  Premises                            Suite 200, 2nd Floor, 1585 Millbrook Road, Raleigh, NC 27609\n\n  Rentable Square Feet                3,200 RSF\n\n  Lease Date                          September 15, 2021\n\n  Commencement Date                   November 1, 2021\n\n  Expiration Date                     October 31, 2028\n\n  Lease Term                          Seven (7) years\n\n  Initial Base Rent                   \\$28.00/RSF/year (\\$89,600.00/year; \\$7,466.67/month)\n\n  Rent Escalation                     Fixed increase of \\$0.75/RSF/year\n\n  Lease Type                          Modified Gross (Base Year 2022)\n\n  Permitted Use                       Medical/dental office\n\n  Parking                             12 dedicated spaces\n\n  Security Deposit                    N/A\n\n  Tenant Improvement Allowance        \\$12.00/RSF (\\$38,400.00 total)\n\n  Personal Guaranty                   Dr. Miriam Soto, individually (see Article 21)\n\n  Renewal Option                      One (1) five-year option (see Article 19)\n\n  Early Termination                   End of Lease Year 4 (see Article 20)\n  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**[ARTICLE 2 --- PREMISES]{.underline}**\n\n**Section 2.1 --- Demise of Premises**\n\nLandlord hereby leases to Tenant, and Tenant hereby leases from Landlord, the Premises described as Suite 200, located on the second (2nd) floor of Millbrook Medical Plaza, 1585 Millbrook Road, Raleigh, NC 27609, consisting of approximately 3,200 rentable square feet (RSF), as more particularly shown on the floor plan attached hereto as Exhibit A and incorporated herein by reference. The Premises shall include access to and the non-exclusive right to use the Common Areas in common with other tenants and occupants of the Building.\n\n**Section 2.2 --- Measurement**\n\nThe RSF of the Premises has been determined in accordance with the Building Owners and Managers Association (BOMA) Standard Method of Measurement (ANSI/BOMA Z65.1-2017). Landlord and Tenant agree that the Premises contains 3,200 RSF and such measurement shall be conclusive and binding for all purposes under this Lease, including without limitation the calculation of Base Rent, the TI Allowance, and Tenant\\'s proportionate share of Operating Expenses and Real Estate Taxes.\n\n**Section 2.3 --- Condition of Premises**\n\nTenant accepts the Premises in its \\\"as-is\\\" condition as of the Lease Date, subject to the completion of Tenant Improvements pursuant to Article 8 of this Lease. Landlord makes no representations or warranties regarding the condition of the Premises, including without limitation the suitability of the Premises for Tenant\\'s intended use, except as expressly set forth herein.\n\n**[ARTICLE 3 --- TERM]{.underline}**\n\n**Section 3.1 --- Lease Term**\n\nThe Lease Term shall commence on November 1, 2021 (the \\\"Commencement Date\\\") and shall expire on October 31, 2028 (the \\\"Expiration Date\\\"), for a total initial term of seven (7) Lease Years, unless sooner terminated or extended in accordance with the provisions of this Lease. Tenant\\'s obligation to pay Rent shall commence on the Commencement Date.\n\n**Section 3.2 --- Delivery of Possession**\n\nLandlord shall deliver possession of the Premises to Tenant on the Commencement Date in the condition required by this Lease. If Landlord fails to deliver possession of the Premises to Tenant by the Commencement Date for any reason, Rent shall abate on a per diem basis until possession is delivered to Tenant, but the Expiration Date shall not be extended by reason of such delay. Landlord shall not be liable to Tenant for any damages resulting from any delay in delivery of possession.\n\n**[ARTICLE 4 --- RENT]{.underline}**\n\n**Section 4.1 --- Base Rent**\n\nTenant shall pay Base Rent to Landlord in monthly installments, in advance, on the first day of each calendar month during the Lease Term, without notice, demand, deduction, or setoff. If the Commencement Date falls on a day other than the first day of a calendar month, Base Rent for the first partial month shall be prorated on a per diem basis. All Rent payments shall be made payable to Landlord and delivered to such address or account as Landlord may designate from time to time in writing.\n\nBase Rent shall escalate annually by a fixed increase of \\$0.75 per RSF per year, as set forth in the following Rent Schedule:\n\n  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  **Lease Year**   **Period**                    **\\$/RSF/Year**   **Annual Base Rent**   **Monthly Base Rent**\n  ---------------- ----------------------------- ----------------- ---------------------- -----------------------\n  Year 1           Nov 1, 2021 -- Oct 31, 2022   \\$28.00           \\$89,600.00            \\$7,466.67\n\n  Year 2           Nov 1, 2022 -- Oct 31, 2023   \\$28.75           \\$92,000.00            \\$7,666.67\n\n  Year 3           Nov 1, 2023 -- Oct 31, 2024   \\$29.50           \\$94,400.00            \\$7,866.67\n\n  Year 4           Nov 1, 2024 -- Oct 31, 2025   \\$30.25           \\$96,800.00            \\$8,066.67\n\n  Year 5           Nov 1, 2025 -- Oct 31, 2026   \\$31.00           \\$99,200.00            \\$8,266.67\n\n  Year 6           Nov 1, 2026 -- Oct 31, 2027   \\$31.75           \\$101,600.00           \\$8,466.67\n\n  Year 7           Nov 1, 2027 -- Oct 31, 2028   \\$32.50           \\$104,000.00           \\$8,666.67\n  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nThe current Lease Year is Year 4 (November 1, 2024 through October 31, 2025), during which Base Rent is \\$30.25 per RSF per year (\\$96,800.00 per year, or \\$8,066.67 per month). A duplicate copy of the Rent Schedule is set forth in Exhibit B for ease of reference.\n\n**Section 4.2 --- Additional Rent / Operating Expense Escalations**\n\nThis Lease is a Modified Gross Lease. Landlord shall pay all Operating Expenses and Real Estate Taxes attributable to the Building during the Base Year (calendar year 2022). Beginning in calendar year 2023 and continuing each calendar year thereafter during the Lease Term, Tenant shall pay, as Additional Rent, Tenant\\'s proportionate share of the amount by which actual Operating Expenses and Real Estate Taxes for such calendar year exceed the actual Operating Expenses and Real Estate Taxes incurred during the Base Year.\n\nTenant\\'s proportionate share shall be calculated as a fraction, the numerator of which is the RSF of the Premises (3,200 RSF) and the denominator of which is the total RSF of the Building. Landlord shall provide Tenant with a written estimate of Tenant\\'s proportionate share of the anticipated escalation for each calendar year, and Tenant shall pay one-twelfth (1/12) of such estimated amount monthly, in advance, together with each installment of Base Rent.\n\nWithin one hundred twenty (120) days following the end of each calendar year, Landlord shall provide Tenant with a detailed annual statement of actual Operating Expenses and Real Estate Taxes for such calendar year. If the actual amount due from Tenant exceeds the total estimated payments made by Tenant during such calendar year, Tenant shall pay the deficiency within thirty (30) days of receipt of such statement. If the estimated payments exceed the actual amount due, Landlord shall credit such overpayment against the next installments of Additional Rent due, or if the Lease Term has expired, refund such overpayment within thirty (30) days.\n\nTenant shall have the right, at Tenant\\'s sole cost and expense, to audit Landlord\\'s books and records relating to Operating Expenses and Real Estate Taxes upon thirty (30) days\\' prior written notice, during normal business hours, at Landlord\\'s office. Such audit right must be exercised, if at all, within twelve (12) months following Tenant\\'s receipt of the annual statement for the applicable calendar year.\n\n**Section 4.3 --- Late Charges and Interest**\n\nIf any payment of Rent or other sum due under this Lease is not received by Landlord within five (5) business days of the date on which such payment is due, Tenant shall pay to Landlord a late charge equal to five percent (5%) of the overdue amount. Such late charge is intended to compensate Landlord for the administrative costs associated with handling late payments and is not a penalty. In addition, any amount not paid within thirty (30) days of the date on which such payment is due shall bear interest at the lesser of (a) twelve percent (12%) per annum, or (b) the maximum rate permitted by applicable law, from the due date until paid in full.\n\n**Section 4.4 --- Holdover Rent**\n\nIf Tenant holds over after the Expiration Date or the earlier termination of this Lease without Landlord\\'s prior written consent, Tenant shall pay holdover rent equal to one hundred fifty percent (150%) of the Base Rent in effect during the last month of the Lease Term, plus all Additional Rent, and such holdover tenancy shall be deemed a month-to-month tenancy subject to all other terms and conditions of this Lease. Landlord\\'s acceptance of holdover rent shall not constitute consent to any holdover tenancy nor a waiver of Landlord\\'s right to recover possession of the Premises or to pursue any other remedy available at law or in equity.\n\n**[ARTICLE 5 --- USE]{.underline}**\n\n**Section 5.1 --- Permitted Use**\n\nTenant shall use and occupy the Premises solely for the purpose of operating a medical and dental office (the \\\"Permitted Use\\\") and for no other purpose without Landlord\\'s prior written consent, which consent may be granted or withheld in Landlord\\'s sole discretion. Tenant shall comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws, ordinances, rules, regulations, and orders governing the operation of a dental and medical practice at the Premises, including without limitation all licensing and permitting requirements of the State of North Carolina.\n\n**Section 5.2 --- Hazardous Materials and Biohazardous Waste**\n\nTenant acknowledges that the operation of a dental practice involves the generation of biohazardous waste, dental amalgam waste, and other regulated materials. Tenant shall be solely responsible for the proper handling, storage, transportation, and disposal of all biohazardous materials, dental amalgam waste, sharps, pharmaceutical waste, and any other hazardous or regulated materials generated in connection with Tenant\\'s use and occupancy of the Premises, in strict compliance with all applicable federal, state, and local environmental, health, and safety laws and regulations, including without limitation the Resource Conservation and Recovery Act (RCRA), the Occupational Safety and Health Act (OSHA), and the North Carolina Solid Waste Management Act.\n\nTenant shall not store or dispose of any hazardous or biohazardous materials in the Building\\'s common waste systems, plumbing, or drainage facilities. Tenant shall maintain at all times within the Premises appropriate containers and equipment for the temporary storage of biohazardous and regulated waste and shall contract with a licensed waste disposal service for the regular removal of such materials from the Premises.\n\nLandlord shall have the right, upon reasonable prior notice to Tenant (except in the case of an emergency, in which case no prior notice shall be required), to inspect the Premises to verify Tenant\\'s compliance with this Section 5.2 and all applicable environmental and health laws. If Landlord determines that Tenant\\'s use or disposal of hazardous or biohazardous materials has resulted in contamination of the Premises, the Building, or the surrounding property, Landlord may require Tenant to undertake remediation of any such condition at Tenant\\'s sole cost and expense, in accordance with all applicable laws and to Landlord\\'s reasonable satisfaction.\n\n**[ARTICLE 6 --- UTILITIES AND SERVICES]{.underline}**\n\n**Section 6.1 --- Building Services**\n\nLandlord shall furnish the following services to the Premises during the Lease Term:\n\n> \\(a\\) Heating, ventilation, and air conditioning (\\\"HVAC\\\") during normal business hours, which shall be Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m., and Saturday, 8:00 a.m. to 1:00 p.m., excluding Building holidays as designated by Landlord from time to time. After-hours HVAC service shall be available upon Tenant\\'s written or electronic request submitted to the Property Manager, at a rate established by Landlord from time to time and communicated to Tenant in writing;\n>\n> \\(b\\) Water and sewer service to the Premises;\n>\n> \\(c\\) Elevator service during Building operating hours, and at least one elevator available at all times for after-hours access;\n>\n> \\(d\\) Electricity to the Premises sufficient for normal medical and dental office use, including standard lighting, computers, and dental equipment operating within standard electrical loads.\n\nTenant shall be responsible for all janitorial and cleaning services within the Premises, including the proper sanitization of treatment rooms and clinical areas in compliance with all applicable health and safety regulations. Landlord shall provide janitorial services for the Common Areas only.\n\n**[ARTICLE 7 --- INSURANCE]{.underline}**\n\n**Section 7.1 --- Tenant\\'s Insurance**\n\nThroughout the Lease Term, Tenant shall maintain, at Tenant\\'s sole cost and expense, the following insurance coverage with insurers licensed to do business in the State of North Carolina and rated at least A-VII by A.M. Best:\n\n> \\(a\\) **Commercial General Liability Insurance** with limits of not less than One Million Dollars (\\$1,000,000) per occurrence and Three Million Dollars (\\$3,000,000) in the aggregate, covering bodily injury, personal injury, and property damage arising from Tenant\\'s use and occupancy of the Premises, including contractual liability coverage;\n>\n> \\(b\\) **Professional Liability Insurance** (dental malpractice insurance) with limits of not less than Five Hundred Thousand Dollars (\\$500,000) per occurrence and One Million Dollars (\\$1,000,000) in the aggregate;\n>\n> \\(c\\) **Workers\\' Compensation Insurance** providing statutory benefits as required by the laws of the State of North Carolina, and Employer\\'s Liability Insurance with limits of not less than Five Hundred Thousand Dollars (\\$500,000) per accident;\n>\n> \\(d\\) **Business Personal Property Insurance** covering Tenant\\'s furniture, fixtures, equipment, inventory, dental instruments, and other personal property located within the Premises for their full replacement cost, on a special form (all-risk) basis.\n\nAll policies required under subsections (a) and (d) above shall name Landlord, Thornfield Management Corp., and Landlord\\'s designated Property Manager as additional insureds. Tenant shall deliver certificates of insurance evidencing the required coverages to Landlord prior to the Commencement Date and annually thereafter upon renewal. Each policy shall require the insurer to provide Landlord with at least thirty (30) days\\' prior written notice of cancellation, non-renewal, or material change in coverage.\n\n**Section 7.2 --- Landlord\\'s Insurance**\n\nLandlord shall maintain, at Landlord\\'s cost (included in Operating Expenses), (a) property insurance for the Building and Common Areas providing fire and extended coverage (special form) in an amount not less than the full replacement cost of the Building, and (b) commercial general liability insurance for the Building and Common Areas with limits reasonably determined by Landlord. The cost of Landlord\\'s insurance premiums shall be included in Operating Expenses for purposes of calculating Tenant\\'s proportionate share of escalations.\n\n**Section 7.3 --- Waiver of Subrogation**\n\nEach Party hereby waives all rights of recovery against the other Party for any loss or damage to the extent covered by, or required to be covered by, such Party\\'s insurance policies maintained pursuant to this Article 7. Each Party shall cause its respective insurer to issue a waiver of subrogation endorsement in favor of the other Party and its agents, employees, officers, and partners. This waiver shall be effective regardless of whether or not the applicable insurance policy contains a waiver of subrogation endorsement.\n\n**[ARTICLE 8 --- TENANT IMPROVEMENTS]{.underline}**\n\n**Section 8.1 --- Tenant Improvement Allowance**\n\nLandlord shall provide Tenant with a Tenant Improvement Allowance (\\\"TI Allowance\\\") of Twelve Dollars (\\$12.00) per RSF, for a total of Thirty-Eight Thousand Four Hundred Dollars (\\$38,400.00), calculated as \\$12.00 multiplied by 3,200 RSF. The TI Allowance shall be applied toward the cost of designing, permitting, and constructing Tenant\\'s improvements to the Premises (the \\\"Tenant Improvements\\\") in accordance with plans and specifications approved by Landlord pursuant to Section 8.2.\n\nAny costs of the Tenant Improvements in excess of the TI Allowance shall be Tenant\\'s sole responsibility. Any unused portion of the TI Allowance shall not be refunded or credited against Rent, but shall be forfeited. The TI Allowance shall be deemed amortized on a straight-line basis over the seven (7) year Lease Term for purposes of any early termination recapture calculation as described in Article 20 (amortization of \\$38,400.00 over 7 years = \\$5,485.71 per year).\n\n**Section 8.2 --- Construction and Approval**\n\nTenant shall submit detailed plans and specifications for the Tenant Improvements to Landlord for approval within thirty (30) days of the Lease Date. Landlord\\'s approval shall not be unreasonably withheld, conditioned, or delayed, and Landlord shall respond to Tenant\\'s submission within fifteen (15) business days of receipt. All Tenant Improvements shall be performed by licensed contractors approved by Landlord (such approval not to be unreasonably withheld) and in compliance with all applicable building codes, regulations, and permit requirements.\n\nAll work shall be performed in a good and workmanlike manner and shall not interfere with the operations of other tenants of the Building. Tenant shall obtain all necessary governmental permits and approvals prior to commencing construction. Upon completion, all Tenant Improvements (other than Tenant\\'s trade fixtures, dental equipment, and personal property) shall become the property of the Landlord and shall remain upon and be surrendered with the Premises at the expiration or earlier termination of the Lease.\n\n**[ARTICLE 9 --- MAINTENANCE AND REPAIRS]{.underline}**\n\n**Section 9.1 --- Landlord\\'s Obligations**\n\nLandlord shall maintain and repair the structural elements of the Building, including the roof, foundation, exterior walls, and load-bearing components, the Common Areas, and the Building\\'s mechanical, electrical, plumbing, and HVAC systems serving the Premises and the Building generally, except to the extent damage thereto is caused by the negligence or willful misconduct of Tenant, its agents, employees, contractors, patients, or invitees. The cost of such maintenance and repair shall be included in Operating Expenses, subject to the exclusions set forth in the definition of Operating Expenses in Section 1.1.\n\n**Section 9.2 --- Tenant\\'s Obligations**\n\nTenant shall maintain the interior of the Premises in good order, condition, and repair throughout the Lease Term, including without limitation all non-structural repairs, interior painting, flooring, ceiling tiles, interior doors, light fixtures, plumbing fixtures within the Premises, and all of Tenant\\'s fixtures, equipment, and personal property. Tenant shall keep the Premises in a clean, safe, and sanitary condition consistent with the operation of a medical and dental practice and in compliance with all applicable health and safety regulations.\n\n**[ARTICLE 10 --- PARKING]{.underline}**\n\n**Section 10.1 --- Parking Allocation**\n\nLandlord shall provide Tenant with twelve (12) dedicated parking spaces in the parking garage adjacent to the Building, at no additional charge during the initial Lease Term. The parking ratio provided to Tenant is approximately 3.75 spaces per 1,000 RSF. Tenant\\'s parking spaces shall be identified by signage or pavement markings designated by Landlord, and Landlord shall designate the specific location of such spaces. Tenant shall not use parking spaces in excess of the allocated twelve (12) spaces without Landlord\\'s prior written consent. Tenant shall comply with all parking rules and regulations established by Landlord from time to time and shall ensure that Tenant\\'s employees, patients, and invitees observe such rules.\n\n**[ARTICLE 11 --- ASSIGNMENT AND SUBLETTING]{.underline}**\n\n**Section 11.1 --- Restriction**\n\nTenant shall not assign this Lease or sublet all or any portion of the Premises, nor shall Tenant permit any other person or entity to occupy the Premises or any part thereof, without the prior written consent of Landlord, which consent shall not be unreasonably withheld, conditioned, or delayed. Any purported assignment or subletting without Landlord\\'s prior written consent shall be void and of no force or effect and shall constitute an Event of Default under this Lease.\n\n**Section 11.2 --- Conditions to Consent**\n\nIn connection with any request for Landlord\\'s consent to an assignment or subletting, Tenant shall provide Landlord with the following information at least thirty (30) days prior to the proposed effective date of the assignment or sublease:\n\n> \\(a\\) The identity and financial statements (for the most recent three fiscal years) of the proposed assignee or subtenant;\n>\n> \\(b\\) The terms and conditions of the proposed assignment or sublease, including a complete copy of the proposed instrument;\n>\n> \\(c\\) Evidence satisfactory to Landlord that the proposed assignee or subtenant will use the Premises solely for the Permitted Use and is duly licensed and qualified to operate a medical or dental practice in the State of North Carolina.\n\nLandlord may consider the creditworthiness of the proposed assignee or subtenant, the nature of the proposed use, the experience of the proposed assignee or subtenant in operating a medical or dental practice, and the impact of the proposed assignment or subletting on the Building and its other tenants. No assignment or subletting shall release Tenant from any of its obligations under this Lease unless Landlord expressly agrees to such release in writing. Tenant shall reimburse Landlord for all reasonable out-of-pocket costs and expenses (including attorneys\\' fees) incurred in connection with reviewing any proposed assignment or sublease.\n\n**[ARTICLE 12 --- SUBORDINATION AND ATTORNMENT]{.underline}**\n\n**Section 12.1 --- Subordination**\n\nThis Lease is and shall be subordinate to any mortgage, deed of trust, or ground lease now or hereafter placed upon or encumbering the Building or any part thereof, and to all renewals, modifications, consolidations, replacements, and extensions thereof, provided that the holder of any such mortgage or deed of trust (the \\\"Mortgagee\\\") shall agree not to disturb Tenant\\'s possession of the Premises so long as Tenant is not in default under this Lease beyond any applicable notice and cure period. Landlord shall use commercially reasonable efforts to obtain a subordination, non-disturbance, and attornment agreement (\\\"SNDA\\\") from any current or future Mortgagee, in a form reasonably acceptable to Tenant, within sixty (60) days of the Commencement Date (with respect to any existing mortgage or deed of trust) or within sixty (60) days of the recording of any future mortgage or deed of trust.\n\n**Section 12.2 --- Attornment**\n\nUpon the request of any Mortgagee or any successor to Landlord\\'s interest in the Building, Tenant shall attorn to such party as landlord under this Lease for the balance of the Lease Term upon the same terms and conditions set forth herein, and Tenant shall execute such instruments as may be reasonably required to evidence such attornment.\n\n**[ARTICLE 13 --- INDEMNIFICATION]{.underline}**\n\n**Section 13.1 --- Tenant Indemnification**\n\nTenant shall indemnify, defend, and hold harmless Landlord and its partners, officers, directors, agents, employees, and the Property Manager from and against any and all claims, actions, liabilities, losses, damages, costs, and expenses (including reasonable attorneys\\' fees and court costs) arising from or in connection with (a) Tenant\\'s use and occupancy of the Premises, (b) the conduct of Tenant\\'s business or any activity, work, or thing done, permitted, or suffered by Tenant in or about the Premises, (c) any breach or default by Tenant in the performance of any obligation of Tenant under this Lease, or (d) any negligent or wrongful act or omission of Tenant, its agents, employees, contractors, patients, or invitees, except to the extent caused by the gross negligence or willful misconduct of Landlord.\n\n**Section 13.2 --- Landlord Indemnification**\n\nLandlord shall indemnify, defend, and hold harmless Tenant and its officers, agents, and employees from and against any and all claims, actions, liabilities, losses, damages, costs, and expenses (including reasonable attorneys\\' fees) arising from the negligent or wrongful acts or omissions of Landlord, its agents, or employees in connection with the ownership, operation, and maintenance of the Building and Common Areas, except to the extent caused by the negligence or willful misconduct of Tenant.\n\n**[ARTICLE 14 --- DAMAGE AND DESTRUCTION]{.underline}**\n\nIf the Premises or the Building is damaged by fire or other casualty, Landlord shall, subject to the provisions of this Article, repair and restore the same with reasonable diligence. If Landlord reasonably estimates that repairs can be completed within one hundred eighty (180) days following the date of the casualty, Landlord shall proceed with such repairs, and this Lease shall remain in full force and effect. If Landlord reasonably estimates that repairs will require more than one hundred eighty (180) days, either Party may terminate this Lease upon thirty (30) days\\' prior written notice to the other Party, given within sixty (60) days following the date of the casualty.\n\nIf the Building is damaged to the extent of fifty percent (50%) or more of its replacement cost, Landlord may, at its option, terminate this Lease upon sixty (60) days\\' written notice to Tenant, regardless of the extent of damage to the Premises. Rent shall abate proportionately during any period in which the Premises or a material portion thereof is rendered untenantable as a result of such casualty. Landlord shall not be required to repair or restore Tenant\\'s personal property, trade fixtures, or dental equipment.\n\n**[ARTICLE 15 --- CONDEMNATION]{.underline}**\n\nIf all or a material portion of the Premises is taken by the exercise of the power of eminent domain or by conveyance in lieu thereof (a \\\"Taking\\\"), either Party may terminate this Lease by written notice to the other Party given within thirty (30) days following the date on which title vests in the condemning authority. If a partial Taking does not materially interfere with Tenant\\'s ability to use the Premises for the Permitted Use, this Lease shall continue in full force and effect, and the Base Rent shall be equitably reduced in proportion to the area of the Premises taken.\n\nLandlord shall be entitled to receive the entire condemnation award or payment made in connection with any Taking, except that Tenant shall have the right to file a separate claim (to the extent permitted by law) for compensation for the loss of Tenant\\'s personal property, trade fixtures, dental equipment, relocation expenses, and the unamortized value of any Tenant Improvements paid for by Tenant in excess of the TI Allowance.\n\n**[ARTICLE 16 --- DEFAULT AND REMEDIES]{.underline}**\n\n**Section 16.1 --- Events of Default**\n\nThe occurrence of any one or more of the following events shall constitute an \\\"Event of Default\\\" under this Lease:\n\n> \\(a\\) Failure by Tenant to pay any installment of Rent or any other sum due under this Lease within ten (10) days after written notice from Landlord of such non-payment;\n>\n> \\(b\\) Failure by Tenant to perform or observe any other covenant, term, or condition of this Lease within thirty (30) days after written notice from Landlord specifying such failure; provided, however, that if such failure is of a nature that cannot reasonably be cured within thirty (30) days, Tenant shall not be in default if Tenant commences cure within such thirty (30) day period and thereafter diligently and continuously pursues such cure to completion;\n>\n> \\(c\\) The filing by or against Tenant of a petition in bankruptcy, the appointment of a receiver or trustee for Tenant\\'s assets, or Tenant\\'s making of a general assignment for the benefit of creditors, and such filing, appointment, or assignment is not dismissed or vacated within sixty (60) days;\n>\n> \\(d\\) Abandonment of the Premises by Tenant for a period of fifteen (15) or more consecutive days.\n\n**Section 16.2 --- Remedies**\n\nUpon the occurrence of an Event of Default, Landlord shall have the following remedies, which shall be cumulative and in addition to any other remedies available at law or in equity:\n\n> \\(a\\) Landlord may terminate this Lease by written notice to Tenant, in which case Tenant shall immediately surrender the Premises. If Tenant fails to surrender, Landlord may re-enter the Premises and remove Tenant and Tenant\\'s property in accordance with applicable law;\n>\n> \\(b\\) Landlord may re-enter the Premises without terminating this Lease and may relet the Premises or any part thereof for such term, at such rental, and upon such conditions as Landlord deems appropriate. Tenant shall be liable for the deficiency between the Rent due under this Lease and the net rent collected upon reletting, after deduction of all costs of reletting, including brokers\\' commissions, renovation costs, and reasonable attorneys\\' fees;\n>\n> \\(c\\) Landlord may recover from Tenant all unpaid Rent that has accrued through the date of termination, the cost of recovering possession of the Premises, and damages measured by the difference between the Rent under this Lease and the fair market rental value of the Premises for the remaining Term, discounted to present value at eight percent (8%) per annum.\n\n**[ARTICLE 17 --- SURRENDER AND RESTORATION]{.underline}**\n\nUpon the expiration or earlier termination of this Lease, Tenant shall peaceably surrender the Premises to Landlord in the same condition as received, reasonable wear and tear and damage by fire or other casualty excepted. Tenant shall remove all of its personal property, trade fixtures, dental equipment, and signage from the Premises on or before the Expiration Date or the effective date of termination. Any property of Tenant not removed from the Premises within ten (10) days following the Expiration Date or the effective date of termination shall be deemed abandoned by Tenant, and Landlord may dispose of such property without liability to Tenant. Tenant shall repair all damage to the Premises caused by the removal of Tenant\\'s property, at Tenant\\'s sole cost and expense, and shall leave the Premises in a broom-clean condition.\n\n**[ARTICLE 18 --- NOTICES]{.underline}**\n\nAll notices, demands, consents, approvals, and other communications required or permitted to be given under this Lease shall be in writing and shall be deemed duly given when delivered by any of the following methods:\n\n> \\(a\\) Personal delivery to the Party or to an officer or authorized representative of the Party;\n>\n> \\(b\\) Deposit with a nationally recognized overnight courier service (such as FedEx or UPS), with all charges prepaid, for next-business-day delivery; or\n>\n> \\(c\\) Deposit in the United States mail, certified mail, return receipt requested, with postage prepaid.\n\nNotices shall be addressed as follows:\n\n**To Landlord:**\n\n> Thornfield Realty Holdings LP 500 South Tryon Street, Suite 2200 Charlotte, NC 28202\n>\n> Attn: Renata Thornfield-Kiess, President\n\n**With a copy to the Property Manager:**\n\n> Karen Osgood Thornfield Realty Holdings LP 500 South Tryon Street, Suite 2200 Charlotte, NC 28202\n\n**To Tenant:**\n\n> Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS, PA 1585 Millbrook Road, Suite 200 Raleigh, NC 27609\n>\n> Attn: Dr. Miriam Soto\n\nEither Party may change its notice address by giving written notice thereof to the other Party in accordance with this Article. Notices shall be effective upon receipt if personally delivered, one (1) business day after deposit with a nationally recognized overnight courier, or three (3) business days after deposit in the United States mail in accordance with this Section.\n\n**[ARTICLE 19 --- RENEWAL OPTION]{.underline}**\n\n**Section 19.1 --- Grant of Option**\n\nProvided that (a) Tenant is not in default under this Lease at the time of exercise of the renewal option and (b) no Event of Default exists at the commencement of the Renewal Term, Tenant shall have one (1) option to renew this Lease for an additional period of five (5) years (the \\\"Renewal Term\\\"), commencing on November 1, 2028 and expiring on October 31, 2033, on the same terms and conditions as this Lease, except that (i) Base Rent during the Renewal Term shall be at the then-prevailing fair market rent for comparable medical and dental office space in the Raleigh, North Carolina market, as reasonably determined by Landlord, and (ii) there shall be no further renewal options unless otherwise agreed in writing. Tenant shall exercise this option by delivering written notice to Landlord no later than nine (9) months prior to the Expiration Date (i.e., by no later than January 31, 2028). Time is of the essence with respect to Tenant\\'s exercise of this renewal option.\n\n**Section 19.2 --- Fair Market Rent Determination**\n\nIf Landlord and Tenant are unable to agree on the fair market rent for the Renewal Term within sixty (60) days following Landlord\\'s receipt of Tenant\\'s exercise notice, the fair market rent shall be determined by arbitration as follows. Within thirty (30) days after the expiration of such sixty (60) day negotiation period, each Party shall select and engage, at its own cost, a licensed commercial real estate appraiser with at least ten (10) years of experience in the Raleigh, North Carolina office market. Each appraiser shall independently determine the fair market rent for the Premises within forty-five (45) days of engagement. If the two appraisals differ, the two appraisers shall jointly select a third appraiser meeting the same qualifications. The third appraiser shall, within thirty (30) days of selection, independently determine the fair market rent. The fair market rent shall be the average of the two closest of the three appraisals. The cost of the third appraiser shall be shared equally by the Parties.\n\n**[ARTICLE 20 --- EARLY TERMINATION]{.underline}**\n\n**Section 20.1 --- Tenant\\'s Early Termination Right**\n\nTenant shall have the right to terminate this Lease effective as of the end of Lease Year 4 (October 31, 2025), upon the satisfaction of each of the following conditions:\n\n> \\(a\\) **Notice.** Tenant shall deliver written notice to Landlord of its intent to terminate this Lease no later than six (6) months prior to the effective termination date (i.e., by no later than April 30, 2025). Time is of the essence with respect to delivery of such notice.\n>\n> \\(b\\) **Termination Payment.** Simultaneously with the delivery of the termination notice, Tenant shall pay to Landlord an early termination fee (the \\\"Termination Payment\\\") equal to the sum of the following:\n>\n> \\(i\\) **Unamortized Tenant Improvement Costs:** The unamortized balance of the TI Allowance as of the effective termination date, calculated on a straight-line basis over the seven (7) year Lease Term. The TI Allowance of \\$38,400.00, amortized at \\$5,485.71 per year (\\$38,400.00 divided by 7 years). At the end of Lease Year 4, four (4) years of amortization have elapsed and three (3) years remain. The unamortized balance equals \\$38,400.00 multiplied by 3/7, which equals **\\$16,457.14**.\n>\n> \\(ii\\) **Three (3) Months\\' Base Rent:** Three (3) months of Base Rent at the rate in effect for the Lease Year in which the termination becomes effective. At the end of Lease Year 4, the then-current Base Rent rate is \\$30.25 per RSF per year. Three months\\' Base Rent equals \\$30.25 multiplied by 3,200 RSF, divided by 12, multiplied by 3, which equals \\$96,800.00 divided by 12, multiplied by 3, which equals \\$8,066.67 multiplied by 3, which equals **\\$24,200.00**.\n>\n> **Total Termination Payment: \\$16,457.14 + \\$24,200.00 = \\$40,657.14.**\n>\n> \\(c\\) **Payment Terms.** The Termination Payment shall be paid in full, in immediately available funds (by wire transfer or certified check), at the time the termination notice is delivered to Landlord. Failure to timely pay the Termination Payment in full shall render the termination notice void and of no force or effect, and this Lease shall continue in accordance with its terms.\n>\n> \\(d\\) **Surrender.** Upon the effective date of termination, Tenant shall surrender the Premises to Landlord in accordance with the requirements of Article 17 of this Lease.\n\nA summary worksheet of the early termination fee calculation is set forth in Exhibit D attached hereto for ease of reference.\n\n**[ARTICLE 21 --- PERSONAL GUARANTY]{.underline}**\n\n**Section 21.1 --- Guaranty of Lease Obligations**\n\nAs a material inducement to Landlord\\'s entering into this Lease, Dr. Miriam Soto, individually (the \\\"Guarantor\\\"), unconditionally and irrevocably guarantees to Landlord the full, faithful, and prompt payment and performance of all obligations of Tenant under this Lease, including but not limited to the payment of Base Rent, Additional Rent, the Termination Payment (if applicable), and any and all other sums due hereunder, as well as the full performance of all covenants, terms, and conditions to be performed by Tenant. This Guaranty is a guaranty of payment and performance and not merely of collection. Landlord may proceed directly against Guarantor without first pursuing any remedies against Tenant, any security held by Landlord, or any other person or entity.\n\n**Section 21.2 --- Duration of Guaranty**\n\nThis Guaranty shall remain in full force and effect throughout the initial Lease Term (through October 31, 2028) and, if Tenant exercises the Renewal Option pursuant to Article 19, throughout the Renewal Term (through October 31, 2033). The Guaranty shall not be released, diminished, impaired, or otherwise affected by (a) any amendment, modification, supplement, or extension of this Lease (whether or not Guarantor consents thereto), (b) any subletting or assignment of this Lease (whether or not consented to by Landlord), (c) any forbearance, waiver, or indulgence granted by Landlord to Tenant, (d) the release or discharge of Tenant from any obligation under this Lease by operation of law or otherwise, or (e) any bankruptcy, insolvency, reorganization, or similar proceeding affecting Tenant.\n\n**Section 21.3 --- Waivers**\n\nGuarantor hereby waives each of the following:\n\n> \\(a\\) Notice of acceptance of this Guaranty by Landlord;\n>\n> \\(b\\) Notice of any default or Event of Default by Tenant under this Lease;\n>\n> \\(c\\) Presentment, demand, and protest with respect to any obligation guaranteed hereby;\n>\n> \\(d\\) Any right to require Landlord to proceed against Tenant, to exhaust any security held by Landlord, or to pursue any other remedy before proceeding against Guarantor; and\n>\n> \\(e\\) Any defense arising from the modification, extension, renewal, or alteration of this Lease or any obligation of Tenant hereunder, or from the release of any co-guarantor.\n\n**[ARTICLE 22 --- MISCELLANEOUS PROVISIONS]{.underline}**\n\n**Section 22.1 --- Entire Agreement**\n\nThis Lease, including all Exhibits attached hereto and incorporated herein by reference, constitutes the entire agreement between the Parties with respect to the subject matter hereof and supersedes all prior or contemporaneous agreements, negotiations, representations, and understandings, whether written or oral. No amendment, modification, or supplement to this Lease shall be effective unless set forth in a written instrument executed by both Parties.\n\n**Section 22.2 --- Governing Law**\n\nThis Lease shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of North Carolina, without regard to its conflicts of law principles. Any dispute arising under or in connection with this Lease shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the state and federal courts located in Wake County, North Carolina, and each Party hereby consents to the personal jurisdiction of such courts.\n\n**Section 22.3 --- Successors and Assigns**\n\nThis Lease shall be binding upon and inure to the benefit of the Parties and their respective successors, assigns, heirs, and legal representatives, subject to the restrictions on assignment and subletting set forth in Article 11 of this Lease.\n\n**Section 22.4 --- Severability**\n\nIf any provision of this Lease is held to be invalid, illegal, or unenforceable by a court of competent jurisdiction, such holding shall not affect the validity, legality, or enforceability of the remaining provisions, which shall continue in full force and effect as if such invalid provision had never been included.\n\n**Section 22.5 --- Broker Disclosure**\n\nLandlord and Tenant each represent and warrant to the other that neither Party has dealt with any real estate broker, agent, or finder in connection with this Lease. Each Party shall indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the other Party from and against any claims, liabilities, costs, or expenses (including reasonable attorneys\\' fees) arising from a breach of the foregoing representation by the indemnifying Party.\n\n**Section 22.6 --- Quiet Enjoyment**\n\nLandlord covenants that so long as Tenant pays Rent and performs all of its obligations under this Lease, Tenant shall peaceably and quietly have, hold, and enjoy the Premises for the full Lease Term without hindrance, ejection, or molestation by Landlord or any person lawfully claiming through or under Landlord, subject to the terms and conditions of this Lease.\n\n**Section 22.7 --- Force Majeure**\n\nNeither Party shall be liable for any delay or failure in the performance of any obligation under this Lease (other than the payment of Rent or other monetary obligations) to the extent such delay or failure is caused by acts of God, war, terrorism, civil unrest, fire, flood, earthquake, epidemic, pandemic, strikes, labor disputes, government regulations, shortages of materials or labor, utility interruptions, or other events beyond such Party\\'s reasonable control (each, a \\\"Force Majeure Event\\\"). The time for performance of any obligation affected by a Force Majeure Event shall be extended by a period equal to the duration of such event. This Section shall not excuse Tenant from the timely payment of Rent or any other monetary obligation under this Lease.\n\n**Section 22.8 --- Counterparts**\n\nThis Lease may be executed in one or more counterparts, each of which shall be deemed an original and all of which together shall constitute one and the same instrument. Electronic signatures transmitted by PDF, facsimile, or other electronic means shall be deemed original signatures for all purposes and shall be binding upon the Parties.\n\n**\\[SIGNATURE PAGE FOLLOWS\\]**\n\n**IN WITNESS WHEREOF**, the Parties have executed this Medical Office Lease Agreement as of the Lease Date first written above.\n\n**LANDLORD:**\n\nTHORNFIELD REALTY HOLDINGS LP, a North Carolina limited partnership\n\nBy: Thornfield Management Corp.,\n\nits General Partner\n\nBy: **\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_**\n\nName: Renata Thornfield-Kiess\n\nTitle: President\n\nDate: September 15, 2021\n\n**TENANT:**\n\nDR. MIRIAM SOTO, DDS, PA, a North Carolina professional association\n\nBy: **\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_**\n\nName: Dr. Miriam Soto\n\nTitle: Principal\n\nDate: September 15, 2021\n\n**GUARANTOR** (for purposes of Article 21):\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nDr. Miriam Soto, individually\n\nDate: September 15, 2021\n\n**EXHIBIT A** **FLOOR PLAN OF PREMISES**\n\n**Suite 200, 2nd Floor** **Millbrook Medical Plaza** **1585 Millbrook Road, Raleigh, NC 27609**\n\n\\[Floor plan depicting Suite 200, located on the second (2nd) floor of Millbrook Medical Plaza, 1585 Millbrook Road, Raleigh, NC 27609, showing the Premises consisting of approximately 3,200 rentable square feet. The Premises is outlined in bold and labeled \\\"Suite 200 --- Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS, PA --- Approximately 3,200 RSF.\\\" The floor plan indicates the location of the Premises in relation to the Building\\'s common corridors, elevators, stairwells, and restrooms.\\]\n\nThis Exhibit A is attached to and incorporated by reference into the Medical Office Lease Agreement dated September 15, 2021, between Thornfield Realty Holdings LP (Landlord) and Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS, PA (Tenant).\n\n**EXHIBIT B** **RENT SCHEDULE**\n\nThe following Rent Schedule sets forth the Base Rent payable by Tenant during each Lease Year of the Lease Term, as provided in Section 4.1 of the Lease:\n\n  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  **Lease Year**   **Period**                    **\\$/RSF/Year**   **Annual Base Rent**   **Monthly Base Rent**\n  ---------------- ----------------------------- ----------------- ---------------------- -----------------------\n  Year 1           Nov 1, 2021 -- Oct 31, 2022   \\$28.00           \\$89,600.00            \\$7,466.67\n\n  Year 2           Nov 1, 2022 -- Oct 31, 2023   \\$28.75           \\$92,000.00            \\$7,666.67\n\n  Year 3           Nov 1, 2023 -- Oct 31, 2024   \\$29.50           \\$94,400.00            \\$7,866.67\n\n  Year 4           Nov 1, 2024 -- Oct 31, 2025   \\$30.25           \\$96,800.00            \\$8,066.67\n\n  Year 5           Nov 1, 2025 -- Oct 31, 2026   \\$31.00           \\$99,200.00            \\$8,266.67\n\n  Year 6           Nov 1, 2026 -- Oct 31, 2027   \\$31.75           \\$101,600.00           \\$8,466.67\n\n  Year 7           Nov 1, 2027 -- Oct 31, 2028   \\$32.50           \\$104,000.00           \\$8,666.67\n  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nBase Rent escalates annually by a fixed amount of \\$0.75 per RSF per year. All figures are based on 3,200 rentable square feet.\n\nThis Exhibit B is attached to and incorporated by reference into the Medical Office Lease Agreement dated September 15, 2021, between Thornfield Realty Holdings LP (Landlord) and Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS, PA (Tenant).\n\n**EXHIBIT C** **BUILDING RULES AND REGULATIONS**\n\nThe following rules and regulations apply to all tenants and occupants of Millbrook Medical Plaza, 1585 Millbrook Road, Raleigh, NC 27609, and are incorporated into the Lease by reference:\n\n1\\. **Hours of Operation and Access.** The Building shall be open for normal business operations Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m., and Saturday, 8:00 a.m. to 1:00 p.m. After-hours access shall be available to authorized personnel of each tenant via key card or other access system provided by Landlord.\n\n2\\. **Signage.** All tenant signage shall conform to Landlord\\'s Building signage standards. Each tenant shall be entitled to one listing on the Building directory in the lobby and suite door signage per Landlord\\'s specifications. No signage may be placed on exterior windows, corridors, or common areas without Landlord\\'s prior written approval.\n\n3\\. **Food Preparation.** No cooking or food preparation shall be permitted within the Premises except in designated break room or kitchen areas equipped with appropriate ventilation.\n\n4\\. **Medical and Biohazardous Waste.** All medical, dental, and biohazardous waste shall be handled, stored, and disposed of in strict compliance with all applicable federal, state, and local laws and regulations, and in accordance with Section 5.2 of the Lease. Under no circumstances shall biohazardous materials be disposed of through the Building\\'s common waste systems.\n\n5\\. **ADA and Fire Safety Compliance.** All tenants shall comply with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), applicable fire safety codes, and all other applicable federal, state, and local regulations pertaining to the occupancy and use of the Premises and Common Areas.\n\n6\\. **Animals.** No animals shall be permitted in the Building, except for service animals as required by applicable law.\n\n7\\. **Amendments.** Landlord reserves the right to amend, modify, or supplement these Rules and Regulations upon thirty (30) days\\' prior written notice to tenants. In the event of any conflict between these Rules and Regulations and the provisions of the Lease, the Lease shall control.\n\nThis Exhibit C is attached to and incorporated by reference into the Medical Office Lease Agreement dated September 15, 2021, between Thornfield Realty Holdings LP (Landlord) and Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS, PA (Tenant).\n\n**EXHIBIT D** **EARLY TERMINATION FEE CALCULATION**\n\nThe following summary worksheet sets forth the calculation of the Termination Payment payable by Tenant in connection with the exercise of Tenant\\'s early termination right under Article 20 of the Lease, effective as of the end of Lease Year 4 (October 31, 2025):\n\n**1. Unamortized Tenant Improvement Costs:**\n\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  **Item**                         **Calculation**           **Amount**\n  -------------------------------- ------------------------- -----------------------\n  TI Allowance                     \\$12.00/RSF × 3,200 RSF   \\$38,400.00\n\n  Amortization Period              7 years (straight-line)   ---\n\n  Annual Amortization              \\$38,400.00 / 7           \\$5,485.71/year\n\n  Years Elapsed at End of Year 4   4 years                   ---\n\n  Years Remaining                  3 years                   ---\n\n  Unamortized TI Balance           \\$38,400.00 × (3/7)       **\\$16,457.14**\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**2. Three (3) Months\\' Base Rent at Year 4 Rate:**\n\n  --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  **Item**                   **Calculation**         **Amount**\n  -------------------------- ----------------------- -----------------------\n  Year 4 Base Rent Rate      \\$30.25/RSF/year        ---\n\n  Annual Base Rent           \\$30.25 × 3,200 RSF     \\$96,800.00\n\n  Monthly Base Rent          \\$96,800.00 / 12        \\$8,066.67\n\n  Three Months\\' Base Rent   \\$8,066.67 × 3          **\\$24,200.00**\n  --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**3. Total Termination Payment:**\n\n  -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  **Component**                       **Amount**\n  ----------------------------------- -----------------------------------\n  Unamortized TI Costs                \\$16,457.14\n\n  Three Months\\' Base Rent            \\$24,200.00\n\n  **Total Termination Payment**       **\\$40,657.14**\n  -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**Note:** The Termination Payment of \\$40,657.14 is due and payable simultaneously with delivery of Tenant\\'s written termination notice, which must be delivered to Landlord no later than April 30, 2025 (six months prior to the end of Lease Year 4). Payment must be made in immediately available funds. Failure to timely deliver both the termination notice and the full Termination Payment shall render the termination notice void and of no effect.\n\nThis Exhibit D is attached to and incorporated by reference into the Medical Office Lease Agreement dated September 15, 2021, between Thornfield Realty Holdings LP (Landlord) and Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS, PA (Tenant).\n"}
