{"turn": 9, "role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call_00_nNcYKfrIH5fi708q86Lp9215", "tool_name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd /workspace/documents && python3 -c \\\"\\nimport subprocess\\nout = subprocess.run(['python3','-c','pass'])\\n\\\" ; python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport zipfile,re\\nfor f in ['verdana-software-lease.docx']:\\n    z=zipfile.ZipFile('/workspace/documents/'+f)\\n    x=z.read('word/document.xml').decode('utf8')\\n    t=re.sub(r'<[^>]+>','',x)\\n    print(len(t))\\n    print(t[-3000:])\\nEOF\"}", "result": "63708\n Georgia 30309. Tenant, its employees, agents, and invitees shall comply with these rules and regulations at all times.1. Building Hours. Standard business hours are 8:00 AM to 6:00 PM, Monday through Friday, and 8:00 AM to 1:00 PM, Saturday, excluding the following Building holidays: New Year's Day, Martin Lueger King Jr. Day, Memorial Day, Independence Day, Labor Day, Thanksgiving Day, the day after Thanksgiving, and Christmas Day. The Building shall be accessible to tenants and their authorized personnel twenty-four (24) hours per day, seven (7) days per week, via key card access after standard business hours.2. Common Areas. Tenants and their invitees shall not obstruct sidewalks, entrances, passages, corridors, lobbies, elevators, stairways, or other common areas of the Building. Common areas shall be used only for ingress, egress, and other purposes for which they are designed.3. Solicitation. Canvassing, soliciting, and peddling in the Building are prohibited. Tenants shall cooperate to prevent such activities.4. Animals. No animals shall be brought into the Building, except service animals as required by applicable law.5. Cooking and Food Preparation. Cooking is not permitted within the Premises except in designated kitchen or pantry areas equipped with Landlord-approved appliances (e.g., microwave ovens, coffee makers, and under-counter refrigerators). No open-flame cooking is permitted.6. Smoking. Smoking (including the use of electronic cigarettes or similar devices) is prohibited within the Building and within twenty-five (25) feet of all Building entrances.7. Moving and Deliveries. All moving of furniture, equipment, and supplies, and all deliveries of a bulk nature, shall be conducted via the freight elevator and loading dock only, and shall be scheduled in advance with building management. Landlord reserves the right to designate specific hours for moving and deliveries to minimize disruption.8. Signage. No signs, advertisements, or notices shall be placed in windows, doors, or common areas of the Building without Landlord's prior written consent. Tenant shall be entitled to one (1) listing on the Building directory in the main lobby and suite identification signage at the entrance to the Premises, in Landlord's standard design and at Landlord's expense.9. Trash Removal. Trash and recyclable materials shall be placed in designated receptacles in accordance with the Building's collection schedule. Tenant shall not dispose of any hazardous or regulated materials through the Building's trash removal system.10. Modifications. Landlord reserves the right to modify, amend, or supplement these rules and regulations from time to time upon not less than thirty (30) days' prior written notice to Tenant, provided that all modifications are uniformly applied to all tenants of the Building and do not materially and adversely affect Tenant's use and enjoyment of the Premises for the Permitted Use.[End of Exhibit E][End of Office Lease Agreement]\n"}
