.8)\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"1.2  Portfolio at a glance\\\")\\ncaption(doc, \\\"Table 1 — The seven leases as abstracted (current position, rent roll reference date January 1, 2025)\\\")\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"1\\\",\\\"Apex Fulfillment Services Inc.\\\",\\\"Thornfield Distribution Center, Charlotte, NC\\\",\\\"87,500\\\",\\\"NNN\\\",\\\"6/1/2019\\\",\\\"5/31/2029\\\",\\\"557,375.00\\\",\\\"23.7%\\\"],\\n [\\\"2\\\",\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS, PA\\\",\\\"Millbrook Medical Plaza, Raleigh, NC\\\",\\\"3,200\\\",\\\"Mod. Gross\\\",\\\"11/1/2021\\\",\\\"10/31/2028\\\",\\\"96,800.00\\\",\\\"4.1%\\\"],\\n [\\\"3\\\",\\\"BrightPath Learning Centers LLC\\\",\\\"Millbrook Medical Plaza, Raleigh, NC\\\",\\\"5,800\\\",\\\"NNN\\\",\\\"4/1/2017\\\",\\\"3/31/2032\\\",\\\"150,220.00\\\",\\\"6.4%\\\"],\\n [\\\"4\\\",\\\"Southeastern Fire & Safety Equipment Co.\\\",\\\"Greystone Industrial Park, Gastonia, NC\\\",\\\"22,000\\\",\\\"NNN\\\",\\\"7/1/2014\\\",\\\"6/30/2024 *\\\",\\\"305,250.00\\\",\\\"13.0%\\\"],\\n [\\\"5\\\",\\\"Verdana Software Solutions Inc.\\\",\\\"Concord Office Tower, Atlanta, GA\\\",\\\"18,750\\\",\\\"FSG\\\",\\\"7/1/2022\\\",\\\"6/30/2032\\\",\\\"676,312.50\\\",\\\"28.8%\\\"],\\n [\\\"6\\\",\\\"The Pint & Platter Restaurant Group LLC\\\",\\\"Haywood Village Shops, Asheville, NC\\\",\\\"4,400\\\",\\\"NNN + %\\\",\\\"10/1/2020\\\",\\\"9/30/2030\\\",\\\"89,386.00\\\",\\\"3.8%\\\"],\\n [\\\"7\\\",\\\"United States of America (GSA)\\\",\\\"Concord Office Tower, Atlanta, GA\\\",\\\"15,000\\\",\\\"Gov't\\\",\\\"1/1/2021\\\",\\\"12/31/2030 \\\\u2020\\\",\\\"472,500.00\\\",\\\"20.1%\\\"],\\n [\\\"\\\",\\\"**Aggregate — 7 leases**\\\",\\\"\\\",\\\"**156,650**\\\",\\\"\\\",\\\"\\\",\\\"\\\",\\\"**2,347,843.50**\\\",\\\"**100.0%**\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"#\\\",\\\"Tenant\\\",\\\"Property\\\",\\\"RSF\\\",\\\"Type\\\",\\\"Commence\\\",\\\"Expiry\\\",\\\"Current annual base rent\\\",\\\"% of total\\\"],\\n          rows, [0.28,1.62,1.55,0.52,0.62,0.68,0.68,0.60,0.5],\\n          size=7.8, head_size=7.5, align_center_cols=(0,3,4,5,6,7,8),\\n          row_fills=[None]*7+[\\\"DCE3EC\\\"], keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"* Southeastern Fire & Safety's ten-year term expired 6/30/2024; the tenant holds over month-to-month at 150% of final rent ($305,250 per annum). \\\\u2020 GSA firm term expires 12/31/2025; the balance to 12/31/2030 is soft term terminable by the Government on 120 days' notice. Current annual base rent is the rent roll figure, which for these two tenants reflects at-will rent rather than contractual term rent.\\\")\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"1.3  Headline conclusions\\\")\\nconcl = [\\n \\\"**The Apex right of first refusal is the single largest threat to the transaction (Risk R-01).** Article XIII of the Apex lease gives the tenant a right of first refusal over Building C that is expressly triggered by a bona fide offer made \\\\u201cas part of a multi-property or portfolio transaction in which Building C is included,\\\\u201d and requires the Seller to deliver a ROFR Notice **before** accepting or executing any agreement with the third party. The PSA was executed on November 15, 2024 for a portfolio that includes Building C. Whether the ROFR was waived, expired, or was never triggered (for example because the deal is structured as a transfer of entity interests rather than real property) must be established before closing, and preferably before the January 31, 2025 due diligence expiry. If it was triggered, Apex has a 30-day period to elect to purchase Building C at its allocable price.\\\",\\n \\\"**The GSA lease cannot be assigned and is senior to any mortgage (R-02).** Section 8 prohibits the Lessor from assigning the lease without the Contracting Officer's written consent, and Section 16 provides that the lease is **not** subordinate to any mortgage and that the Lessor may not grant any mortgage taking priority without federal consent. This has two consequences: acquisition financing secured by Concord Office Tower may be unavailable on customary terms, and an asset-level acquisition will require a novation or consent from GSA Region 4 before closing.\\\",\\n \\\"**37.2% of aggregate rent is not firm.** Southeastern Fire & Safety (13.0%) is a month-to-month holdover terminable by either party on 30 days' notice; the GSA lease (20.1%) has twelve months of firm term remaining and then becomes terminable on 120 days' notice with no penalty; and Dr. Soto (4.1%) holds an early termination right exercisable until April 30, 2025. Contractual, firm rent excluding the two at-will tenancies is **$1,570,093.50**, or 66.9% of the aggregate.\\\",\\n \\\"**The Verdana expansion option is a material encumbrance (R-06).** Verdana may, at any time through June 30, 2027, require the Lessor to lease it the entire 9th floor \\\\u2014 approximately 18,500 RSF, or 12.3% of the building \\\\u2014 at the then-current 8th-floor rate ($36.07 per RSF in Year 3, escalating 3% annually thereafter), with a $740,000 allowance, coterminous to June 30, 2032. The option window has already opened and the Lessor has no right to refuse.\\\",\\n \\\"**The Rent Roll's weighted average remaining lease term cannot be reproduced (R-11).** The Rent Roll states approximately 5.7 years, or approximately 4.6 years on a firm-term-only basis. Recomputed on the Rent Roll's own stated method (rent-weighted, measured from January 1, 2025), the correct figures are **5.25 years** and **4.25 years** respectively. Both Rent Roll figures overstate remaining term by roughly 0.4 years.\\\",\\n \\\"**Three lease rent schedules do not follow their own stated escalation formulas (R-12, R-13, R-20).** Apex (Year 5), BrightPath (Year 8) and Southeastern (Year 10) each contain a single year whose rate departs from the stated compounding rate; in the BrightPath lease the error then carries forward to the end of the term. The combined effect on the current-year rent roll is a net overstatement of roughly $6,467 per annum, concentrated in the Southeastern holdover (13.0% of aggregate rent).\\\",\\n \\\"**Estoppel and non-disturbance protection is thin (R-09, R-10).** Only the Apex and Verdana leases oblige the tenant to deliver an estoppel certificate (and both include a deemed-acknowledgment provision). No SNDA is on file for any of the seven leases, and the Apex and Southeastern leases contain self-operative subordination with no non-disturbance obligation at all. Galleon should rely on PSA estoppel conditions, not on the leases.\\\",\\n \\\"**Several documents needed to close the analysis have not been provided (Section 10).** These include the full rent roll and occupancy certificate for Haywood Village Shops (necessary to test Pint & Platter's co-tenancy trigger), the status of Buildings A and B at Thornfield Distribution Center (necessary to test Apex's exclusive-use covenant), the status of the 9th floor at Concord Office Tower (necessary to test the Verdana expansion option), and any ROFR notice delivered to Apex.\\\",\\n]\\nfor c in concl:\\n    p = doc.add_paragraph()\\n    pf = p.paragraph_format\\n    pf.left_indent = Inches(0.2); pf.space_after = Pt(4.5); pf.line_spacing = 1.06\\n    for k,part in enumerate(c.split(\\\"**\\\")):\\n        if not part: continue\\n        r = p.add_run(part); r.font.size=Pt(9.3); r.font.name=\\\"Calibri\\\"; r.bold = (k%2==1)\\n        if k==1 and \\\"R-0\\\" in part: r.font.color.rgb = ACCENT\\nPYEOF\\necho ok\"}", "result": "ok\n"}
{"turn": 22, "role": "assistant", "text": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_DX9CDRNwbwx7nIfOwWCg3364", "name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && cat >> work/build.py <<'PYEOF'\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"1.4  Aggregate rent and rent at risk\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"The aggregate current annual base rent of **$2,347,843.50** ($195,653.63 per month) ties exactly to the Rent Roll's total and to the estimate in the Engagement Letter, and each rent roll line was traced to the tenant's rent schedule in the underlying lease. That aggregate nevertheless overstates durable contractual income, because it includes rent payable under tenancies that are terminable at will or that have only twelve months of firm term remaining.\\\", size=9.8)\\ncaption(doc, \\\"Table 2 — Composition of the aggregate, and duration of the obligation\\\")\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"Contractual rent with firm term beyond 12 months (Apex, BrightPath, Verdana, Pint & Platter, plus Soto absent exercise of its termination right)\\\",\\\"1,570,093.50\\\",\\\"66.9%\\\"],\\n [\\\"GSA shell rent \\\\u2014 firm only to 12/31/2025, then terminable by the Government on 120 days' notice with no penalty\\\",\\\"472,500.00\\\",\\\"20.1%\\\"],\\n [\\\"Southeastern Fire & Safety holdover rent \\\\u2014 month-to-month at 150%; terminable by either party on 30 days' notice\\\",\\\"305,250.00\\\",\\\"13.0%\\\"],\\n [\\\"**Aggregate current annual base rent (Rent Roll)**\\\",\\\"**2,347,843.50**\\\",\\\"**100.0%**\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Component\\\",\\\"Annual amount ($)\\\",\\\"% of aggregate\\\"], rows, [4.5,1.1,1.1],\\n          size=8.3, head_size=8, align_center_cols=(1,2), row_fills=[None,None,None,\\\"DCE3EC\\\"], keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"Amounts computed from the Rent Roll and verified against each lease's rent schedule. The aggregate excludes percentage rent payable by Pint & Platter (not quantifiable without gross sales statements), Verdana's reserved parking income of $16,800 per annum (properly excluded by the Rent Roll), and any recovery of operating expenses, which is additional rent and is not part of base rent.\\\")\\n\\npara(doc, \\\"Two further contingent exposures should be quantified alongside the rent at risk:\\\", size=9.8)\\nbullets(doc, [\\n \\\"**Dr. Soto early termination (R-05).** If the right is exercised, Galleon loses Lease Years 5, 6 and 7 rent of $99,200.00 + $101,600.00 + $104,000.00 = **$304,800.00**, against a termination payment of only **$40,657.14** \\\\u2014 a net exposure of approximately **$264,143**. Notice must be given by April 30, 2025, which is 46 days after the target closing date of March 15, 2025.\\\",\\n \\\"**Apex right of first refusal (R-01).** If Apex validly exercises, Galleon cannot acquire Building C. If the price were allocated across the Portfolio by rentable area, the \\\\u201callocable purchase price\\\\u201d for Building C would be approximately $67.3 million (87,500 \\\\u00f7 243,650 \\\\u00d7 $187,500,000). That figure is illustrative only \\\\u2014 the lease requires the Lessor to determine the allocation in good faith, and the tenant may dispute it before an MAI appraiser \\\\u2014 but it indicates the order of magnitude at stake.\\\",\\n], size=9.3)\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"1.5  Weighted average remaining lease term\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"The Engagement Letter requires a weighted average remaining lease term (\\\\u201cWALT\\\\u201d). We calculated WALT independently, weighting each lease's annual base rent by its remaining term measured from January 1, 2025 \\\\u2014 the same convention and weighting basis stated in the Rent Roll \\\\u2014 and presenting three treatments of the GSA soft term and the Southeastern holdover because those assumptions drive the result.\\\", size=9.8)\\ncaption(doc, \\\"Table 3 — WALT computation (weight = current annual base rent; term measured from January 1, 2025)\\\")\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"Apex Fulfillment\\\",\\\"557,375.00\\\",\\\"5/31/2029\\\",\\\"4.42\\\",\\\"2,463,597\\\"],\\n [\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS\\\",\\\"96,800.00\\\",\\\"10/31/2028\\\",\\\"3.83\\\",\\\"371,067\\\"],\\n [\\\"BrightPath Learning\\\",\\\"150,220.00\\\",\\\"3/31/2032\\\",\\\"7.25\\\",\\\"1,089,095\\\"],\\n [\\\"Southeastern Fire & Safety\\\",\\\"305,250.00\\\",\\\"n/a \\\\u2014 holdover\\\",\\\"0.00\\\",\\\"0\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana Software\\\",\\\"676,312.50\\\",\\\"6/30/2032\\\",\\\"7.50\\\",\\\"5,072,344\\\"],\\n [\\\"The Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"89,386.00\\\",\\\"9/30/2030\\\",\\\"5.75\\\",\\\"513,970\\\"],\\n [\\\"United States of America (GSA)\\\",\\\"472,500.00\\\",\\\"12/31/2030 (soft)  /  12/31/2025 (firm)\\\",\\\"6.00  /  1.00\\\",\\\"2,835,000  /  472,500\\\"],\\n [\\\"**Total / WALT**\\\",\\\"**2,347,843.50**\\\",\\\"\\\",\\\"**5.25 (soft)  /  4.25 (firm)**\\\",\\\"**12,343,233  /  9,980,733**\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Tenant\\\",\\\"Annual rent ($)\\\",\\\"Expiration\\\",\\\"Remaining term (yrs)\\\",\\\"Rent \\\\u00d7 term\\\"], rows,\\n          [1.95,0.95,1.95,1.0,1.15], size=8.2, head_size=7.8, align_center_cols=(1,3,4),\\n          row_fills=[None]*7+[\\\"DCE3EC\\\"], keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"Remaining terms: Apex 4 years 5 months (4.4167); Soto 3 years 10 months (3.8333); BrightPath 7 years 3 months (7.25); Verdana 7 years 6 months (7.5); Pint & Platter 5 years 9 months (5.75); GSA 6.0 years soft / 1.0 year firm; Southeastern treated as 0.00 years because it has no contractual term. If the Southeastern holdover were instead credited with 1.0 year, WALT would be 5.39 years (soft) and 4.38 years (firm) \\\\u2014 still materially below the Rent Roll's figures.\\\")\\nbox(doc, \\\"Reconciliation to the Rent Roll\\\",\\n    [\\\"The Rent Roll's Summary sheet states a WALT of approximately **5.7 years**, reducing to approximately **4.6 years** on a firm-term-only basis. Neither figure can be reproduced from the Rent Roll's own data. Applying the Rent Roll's stated methodology produces **5.25 years** and **4.25 years**. The difference is approximately 0.4 years in both cases and does not appear to arise from a different weighting basis \\\\u2014 weighting by rentable square feet instead of rent produces 4.45 years, and a simple unweighted average produces 4.96 years, so neither alternative convention explains the stated figure.\\\",\\n     \\\"**Consequence.** For valuation purposes Galleon should use a rent-weighted WALT of approximately **5.25 years** on the soft-term basis and **4.25 years** on the firm-term basis. The Rent Roll's presentation is more favourable than the leases support (Risk R-11).\\\"],\\n    fill=AMBER, size=8.8)\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"1.6  Tenant concentration\\\")\\ncaption(doc, \\\"Table 4 — Concentration by annual base rent\\\")\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"Verdana Software Solutions Inc.\\\",\\\"676,312.50\\\",\\\"28.8%\\\",\\\"28.8%\\\",\\\"No security deposit or guaranty; full-floor 8th floor tenancy\\\"],\\n [\\\"Apex Fulfillment Services Inc.\\\",\\\"557,375.00\\\",\\\"23.7%\\\",\\\"52.5%\\\",\\\"No security deposit or guaranty; ROFR over Building C\\\"],\\n [\\\"United States of America (GSA)\\\",\\\"472,500.00\\\",\\\"20.1%\\\",\\\"72.6%\\\",\\\"Full faith and credit; but only 12 months of firm term\\\"],\\n [\\\"Southeastern Fire & Safety Equipment Co.\\\",\\\"305,250.00\\\",\\\"13.0%\\\",\\\"85.6%\\\",\\\"Holdover at will; no deposit or guaranty; AFFF/PFAS on site\\\"],\\n [\\\"BrightPath Learning Centers LLC\\\",\\\"150,220.00\\\",\\\"6.4%\\\",\\\"92.0%\\\",\\\"Security deposit $25,440 (amount to be confirmed)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS, PA\\\",\\\"96,800.00\\\",\\\"4.1%\\\",\\\"96.1%\\\",\\\"Personal guaranty (Dr. Miriam Soto)\\\"],\\n [\\\"The Pint & Platter Restaurant Group LLC\\\",\\\"89,386.00\\\",\\\"3.8%\\\",\\\"100.0%\\\",\\\"Deposit $19,800; personal guaranty burning off\\\"],\\n [\\\"**Total**\\\",\\\"**2,347,843.50**\\\",\\\"**100.0%**\\\",\\\"\\\",\\\"\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Tenant\\\",\\\"Annual rent ($)\\\",\\\"% of total\\\",\\\"Cumulative\\\",\\\"Credit support and concentration comment\\\"], rows,\\n          [1.95,0.9,0.65,0.72,2.48], size=8.0, head_size=7.6, align_center_cols=(1,2,3),\\n          row_fills=[None]*7+[\\\"DCE3EC\\\"], keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"Percentages are the Rent Roll's own and were independently confirmed ($676,312.50 \\\\u00f7 $2,347,843.50 = 28.81%, and so on; the seven shares sum to 100.0%). The top three tenants represent 72.6% of aggregate rent and the top four 85.6%.\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"Concentration is high on any measure, but the more important observation is that the concentration and the absence of credit support coincide. **Apex and Verdana together represent 52.5% of aggregate rent and neither has a security deposit, letter of credit or guaranty**; Southeastern, at 13.0%, is likewise unsecured and is holding over. Only 14.3% of aggregate rent (Soto 4.1% and Pint & Platter 3.8%, together with BrightPath's 6.4% deposit-backed share) carries meaningful credit enhancement. Galleon should obtain current financial statements for Apex, Verdana and Southeastern, and consider a purchase price adjustment or escrow rather than relying on the lease covenant.\\\", size=9.8)\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"1.7  Lease expiration and rollover profile\\\")\\ncaption(doc, \\\"Table 5 — Rollover schedule by trigger date (no renewal options assumed)\\\")\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"At closing\\\",\\\"Southeastern Fire & Safety \\\\u2014 term already expired; at-will\\\",\\\"305,250.00\\\",\\\"13.0%\\\",\\\"13.0%\\\",\\\"At will\\\"],\\n [\\\"31-Oct-2025\\\",\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto \\\\u2014 early termination right (notice by 30-Apr-2025)\\\",\\\"96,800.00\\\",\\\"4.1%\\\",\\\"17.1%\\\",\\\"Tenant option\\\"],\\n [\\\"31-Dec-2025\\\",\\\"GSA \\\\u2014 firm term expires; soft term becomes terminable on 120 days\\\",\\\"472,500.00\\\",\\\"20.1%\\\",\\\"37.2%\\\",\\\"Becomes at will\\\"],\\n [\\\"31-Oct-2028\\\",\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto \\\\u2014 scheduled expiry\\\",\\\"96,800.00\\\",\\\"\\\\u2014\\\",\\\"37.2%\\\",\\\"Firm expiry\\\"],\\n [\\\"31-May-2029\\\",\\\"Apex Fulfillment \\\\u2014 scheduled expiry\\\",\\\"557,375.00\\\",\\\"23.7%\\\",\\\"60.9%\\\",\\\"Firm expiry\\\"],\\n [\\\"30-Sep-2030\\\",\\\"The Pint & Platter \\\\u2014 scheduled expiry\\\",\\\"89,386.00\\\",\\\"3.8%\\\",\\\"64.7%\\\",\\\"Firm expiry\\\"],\\n [\\\"31-Dec-2030\\\",\\\"GSA \\\\u2014 absolute expiry of total term\\\",\\\"\\\\u2014\\\",\\\"\\\\u2014\\\",\\\"64.7%\\\",\\\"Firm expiry\\\"],\\n [\\\"31-Mar-2032\\\",\\\"BrightPath Learning \\\\u2014 scheduled expiry\\\",\\\"150,220.00\\\",\\\"6.4%\\\",\\\"71.1%\\\",\\\"Firm expiry\\\"],\\n [\\\"30-Jun-2032\\\",\\\"Verdana Software \\\\u2014 scheduled expiry\\\",\\\"676,312.50\\\",\\\"28.8%\\\",\\\"100.0%\\\",\\\"Firm expiry\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Trigger date\\\",\\\"Event\\\",\\\"Annual rent ($)\\\",\\\"% of total\\\",\\\"Cumulative\\\",\\\"Nature\\\"], rows,\\n          [0.78,2.55,0.85,0.6,0.68,0.94], size=7.9, head_size=7.5, align_center_cols=(0,2,3,4),\\n          row_fills=[WARN,WARN,WARN,None,None,None,None,None,None], keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"Soto appears once only; its 2028 expiry is shown for completeness but the rent is already treated as at risk from 31 October 2025 if the option is exercised. Shaded rows are the three events that occur on or within twelve months after the target closing date. Cumulative percentages are of the $2,347,843.50 aggregate.\\\")\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"1.8  Priorities for Galleon\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"The following eight items should be actioned immediately. Section 7 contains the full risk register and Section 8 the sequenced action plan with owners and deadlines.\\\", size=9.8)\\npri = [\\n (\\\"1\\\",\\\"Obtain a ROFR waiver or estoppel from Apex, or documentary proof that the ROFR was not triggered, expired or was waived — plus a title search for any recorded memorandum of ROFR.\\\",\\\"Before DD expiry (31 Jan 2025)\\\",\\\"R-01\\\"),\\n (\\\"2\\\",\\\"Establish the acquisition structure (asset vs. equity) and, if asset-level, initiate GSA consent/novation; confirm the lender's position on the GSA lease's anti-subordination clause.\\\",\\\"Immediately (financing commitment)\\\",\\\"R-02\\\"),\\n (\\\"3\\\",\\\"Obtain estoppels from all seven tenants with the certifications listed in Section 9, including option status, ROFR waiver, co-tenancy status and any termination notice.\\\",\\\"Target 17 Jan 2025\\\",\\\"R-09\\\"),\\n (\\\"4\\\",\\\"Require Seller to deliver the Haywood Village Shops full rent roll and an occupancy certificate to test the Pint & Platter co-tenancy trigger.\\\",\\\"Before DD expiry\\\",\\\"R-07\\\"),\\n (\\\"5\\\",\\\"Confirm whether Verdana has exercised the 9th-floor expansion option and whether the 9th floor is available to deliver; price the encumbrance or negotiate a waiver.\\\",\\\"Before DD expiry\\\",\\\"R-06\\\"),\\n (\\\"6\\\",\\\"Address the Southeastern holdover: obtain a new lease or a holdover acknowledgment with a fixed term and rent, and pursue environmental diligence on AFFF/PFAS.\\\",\\\"Before closing\\\",\\\"R-04\\\"),\\n (\\\"7\\\",\\\"Reconcile actual billing ledgers for 2024 against the Rent Roll and the lease schedules, and correct the Apex, BrightPath and Southeastern schedule errors.\\\",\\\"Before closing\\\",\\\"R-12, R-13, R-20\\\"),\\n (\\\"8\\\",\\\"Obtain security deposit ledgers and guaranty originals; confirm the amount actually held for BrightPath and the status of the Pint & Platter guaranty.\\\",\\\"Before closing\\\",\\\"R-15, R-21\\\"),\\n]\\nrows = [[a,b,c,d] for a,b,c,d in pri]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"#\\\",\\\"Action\\\",\\\"Deadline\\\",\\\"Risk\\\"], rows, [0.3,3.85,1.85,0.7], size=8.3, head_size=8,\\n          align_center_cols=(0,3), keep_rows=True)\\nPYEOF\\necho ok\"}"}], "input_tokens": 165955, "output_tokens": 3618, "finish_reason": "completed"}
{"turn": 22, "role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call_00_DX9CDRNwbwx7nIfOwWCg3364", "tool_name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && cat >> work/build.py <<'PYEOF'\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"1.4  Aggregate rent and rent at risk\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"The aggregate current annual base rent of **$2,347,843.50** ($195,653.63 per month) ties exactly to the Rent Roll's total and to the estimate in the Engagement Letter, and each rent roll line was traced to the tenant's rent schedule in the underlying lease. That aggregate nevertheless overstates durable contractual income, because it includes rent payable under tenancies that are terminable at will or that have only twelve months of firm term remaining.\\\", size=9.8)\\ncaption(doc, \\\"Table 2 — Composition of the aggregate, and duration of the obligation\\\")\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"Contractual rent with firm term beyond 12 months (Apex, BrightPath, Verdana, Pint & Platter, plus Soto absent exercise of its termination right)\\\",\\\"1,570,093.50\\\",\\\"66.9%\\\"],\\n [\\\"GSA shell rent \\\\u2014 firm only to 12/31/2025, then terminable by the Government on 120 days' notice with no penalty\\\",\\\"472,500.00\\\",\\\"20.1%\\\"],\\n [\\\"Southeastern Fire & Safety holdover rent \\\\u2014 month-to-month at 150%; terminable by either party on 30 days' notice\\\",\\\"305,250.00\\\",\\\"13.0%\\\"],\\n [\\\"**Aggregate current annual base rent (Rent Roll)**\\\",\\\"**2,347,843.50**\\\",\\\"**100.0%**\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Component\\\",\\\"Annual amount ($)\\\",\\\"% of aggregate\\\"], rows, [4.5,1.1,1.1],\\n          size=8.3, head_size=8, align_center_cols=(1,2), row_fills=[None,None,None,\\\"DCE3EC\\\"], keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"Amounts computed from the Rent Roll and verified against each lease's rent schedule. The aggregate excludes percentage rent payable by Pint & Platter (not quantifiable without gross sales statements), Verdana's reserved parking income of $16,800 per annum (properly excluded by the Rent Roll), and any recovery of operating expenses, which is additional rent and is not part of base rent.\\\")\\n\\npara(doc, \\\"Two further contingent exposures should be quantified alongside the rent at risk:\\\", size=9.8)\\nbullets(doc, [\\n \\\"**Dr. Soto early termination (R-05).** If the right is exercised, Galleon loses Lease Years 5, 6 and 7 rent of $99,200.00 + $101,600.00 + $104,000.00 = **$304,800.00**, against a termination payment of only **$40,657.14** \\\\u2014 a net exposure of approximately **$264,143**. Notice must be given by April 30, 2025, which is 46 days after the target closing date of March 15, 2025.\\\",\\n \\\"**Apex right of first refusal (R-01).** If Apex validly exercises, Galleon cannot acquire Building C. If the price were allocated across the Portfolio by rentable area, the \\\\u201callocable purchase price\\\\u201d for Building C would be approximately $67.3 million (87,500 \\\\u00f7 243,650 \\\\u00d7 $187,500,000). That figure is illustrative only \\\\u2014 the lease requires the Lessor to determine the allocation in good faith, and the tenant may dispute it before an MAI appraiser \\\\u2014 but it indicates the order of magnitude at stake.\\\",\\n], size=9.3)\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"1.5  Weighted average remaining lease term\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"The Engagement Letter requires a weighted average remaining lease term (\\\\u201cWALT\\\\u201d). We calculated WALT independently, weighting each lease's annual base rent by its remaining term measured from January 1, 2025 \\\\u2014 the same convention and weighting basis stated in the Rent Roll \\\\u2014 and presenting three treatments of the GSA soft term and the Southeastern holdover because those assumptions drive the result.\\\", size=9.8)\\ncaption(doc, \\\"Table 3 — WALT computation (weight = current annual base rent; term measured from January 1, 2025)\\\")\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"Apex Fulfillment\\\",\\\"557,375.00\\\",\\\"5/31/2029\\\",\\\"4.42\\\",\\\"2,463,597\\\"],\\n [\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS\\\",\\\"96,800.00\\\",\\\"10/31/2028\\\",\\\"3.83\\\",\\\"371,067\\\"],\\n [\\\"BrightPath Learning\\\",\\\"150,220.00\\\",\\\"3/31/2032\\\",\\\"7.25\\\",\\\"1,089,095\\\"],\\n [\\\"Southeastern Fire & Safety\\\",\\\"305,250.00\\\",\\\"n/a \\\\u2014 holdover\\\",\\\"0.00\\\",\\\"0\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana Software\\\",\\\"676,312.50\\\",\\\"6/30/2032\\\",\\\"7.50\\\",\\\"5,072,344\\\"],\\n [\\\"The Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"89,386.00\\\",\\\"9/30/2030\\\",\\\"5.75\\\",\\\"513,970\\\"],\\n [\\\"United States of America (GSA)\\\",\\\"472,500.00\\\",\\\"12/31/2030 (soft)  /  12/31/2025 (firm)\\\",\\\"6.00  /  1.00\\\",\\\"2,835,000  /  472,500\\\"],\\n [\\\"**Total / WALT**\\\",\\\"**2,347,843.50**\\\",\\\"\\\",\\\"**5.25 (soft)  /  4.25 (firm)**\\\",\\\"**12,343,233  /  9,980,733**\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Tenant\\\",\\\"Annual rent ($)\\\",\\\"Expiration\\\",\\\"Remaining term (yrs)\\\",\\\"Rent \\\\u00d7 term\\\"], rows,\\n          [1.95,0.95,1.95,1.0,1.15], size=8.2, head_size=7.8, align_center_cols=(1,3,4),\\n          row_fills=[None]*7+[\\\"DCE3EC\\\"], keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"Remaining terms: Apex 4 years 5 months (4.4167); Soto 3 years 10 months (3.8333); BrightPath 7 years 3 months (7.25); Verdana 7 years 6 months (7.5); Pint & Platter 5 years 9 months (5.75); GSA 6.0 years soft / 1.0 year firm; Southeastern treated as 0.00 years because it has no contractual term. If the Southeastern holdover were instead credited with 1.0 year, WALT would be 5.39 years (soft) and 4.38 years (firm) \\\\u2014 still materially below the Rent Roll's figures.\\\")\\nbox(doc, \\\"Reconciliation to the Rent Roll\\\",\\n    [\\\"The Rent Roll's Summary sheet states a WALT of approximately **5.7 years**, reducing to approximately **4.6 years** on a firm-term-only basis. Neither figure can be reproduced from the Rent Roll's own data. Applying the Rent Roll's stated methodology produces **5.25 years** and **4.25 years**. The difference is approximately 0.4 years in both cases and does not appear to arise from a different weighting basis \\\\u2014 weighting by rentable square feet instead of rent produces 4.45 years, and a simple unweighted average produces 4.96 years, so neither alternative convention explains the stated figure.\\\",\\n     \\\"**Consequence.** For valuation purposes Galleon should use a rent-weighted WALT of approximately **5.25 years** on the soft-term basis and **4.25 years** on the firm-term basis. The Rent Roll's presentation is more favourable than the leases support (Risk R-11).\\\"],\\n    fill=AMBER, size=8.8)\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"1.6  Tenant concentration\\\")\\ncaption(doc, \\\"Table 4 — Concentration by annual base rent\\\")\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"Verdana Software Solutions Inc.\\\",\\\"676,312.50\\\",\\\"28.8%\\\",\\\"28.8%\\\",\\\"No security deposit or guaranty; full-floor 8th floor tenancy\\\"],\\n [\\\"Apex Fulfillment Services Inc.\\\",\\\"557,375.00\\\",\\\"23.7%\\\",\\\"52.5%\\\",\\\"No security deposit or guaranty; ROFR over Building C\\\"],\\n [\\\"United States of America (GSA)\\\",\\\"472,500.00\\\",\\\"20.1%\\\",\\\"72.6%\\\",\\\"Full faith and credit; but only 12 months of firm term\\\"],\\n [\\\"Southeastern Fire & Safety Equipment Co.\\\",\\\"305,250.00\\\",\\\"13.0%\\\",\\\"85.6%\\\",\\\"Holdover at will; no deposit or guaranty; AFFF/PFAS on site\\\"],\\n [\\\"BrightPath Learning Centers LLC\\\",\\\"150,220.00\\\",\\\"6.4%\\\",\\\"92.0%\\\",\\\"Security deposit $25,440 (amount to be confirmed)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS, PA\\\",\\\"96,800.00\\\",\\\"4.1%\\\",\\\"96.1%\\\",\\\"Personal guaranty (Dr. Miriam Soto)\\\"],\\n [\\\"The Pint & Platter Restaurant Group LLC\\\",\\\"89,386.00\\\",\\\"3.8%\\\",\\\"100.0%\\\",\\\"Deposit $19,800; personal guaranty burning off\\\"],\\n [\\\"**Total**\\\",\\\"**2,347,843.50**\\\",\\\"**100.0%**\\\",\\\"\\\",\\\"\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Tenant\\\",\\\"Annual rent ($)\\\",\\\"% of total\\\",\\\"Cumulative\\\",\\\"Credit support and concentration comment\\\"], rows,\\n          [1.95,0.9,0.65,0.72,2.48], size=8.0, head_size=7.6, align_center_cols=(1,2,3),\\n          row_fills=[None]*7+[\\\"DCE3EC\\\"], keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"Percentages are the Rent Roll's own and were independently confirmed ($676,312.50 \\\\u00f7 $2,347,843.50 = 28.81%, and so on; the seven shares sum to 100.0%). The top three tenants represent 72.6% of aggregate rent and the top four 85.6%.\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"Concentration is high on any measure, but the more important observation is that the concentration and the absence of credit support coincide. **Apex and Verdana together represent 52.5% of aggregate rent and neither has a security deposit, letter of credit or guaranty**; Southeastern, at 13.0%, is likewise unsecured and is holding over. Only 14.3% of aggregate rent (Soto 4.1% and Pint & Platter 3.8%, together with BrightPath's 6.4% deposit-backed share) carries meaningful credit enhancement. Galleon should obtain current financial statements for Apex, Verdana and Southeastern, and consider a purchase price adjustment or escrow rather than relying on the lease covenant.\\\", size=9.8)\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"1.7  Lease expiration and rollover profile\\\")\\ncaption(doc, \\\"Table 5 — Rollover schedule by trigger date (no renewal options assumed)\\\")\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"At closing\\\",\\\"Southeastern Fire & Safety \\\\u2014 term already expired; at-will\\\",\\\"305,250.00\\\",\\\"13.0%\\\",\\\"13.0%\\\",\\\"At will\\\"],\\n [\\\"31-Oct-2025\\\",\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto \\\\u2014 early termination right (notice by 30-Apr-2025)\\\",\\\"96,800.00\\\",\\\"4.1%\\\",\\\"17.1%\\\",\\\"Tenant option\\\"],\\n [\\\"31-Dec-2025\\\",\\\"GSA \\\\u2014 firm term expires; soft term becomes terminable on 120 days\\\",\\\"472,500.00\\\",\\\"20.1%\\\",\\\"37.2%\\\",\\\"Becomes at will\\\"],\\n [\\\"31-Oct-2028\\\",\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto \\\\u2014 scheduled expiry\\\",\\\"96,800.00\\\",\\\"\\\\u2014\\\",\\\"37.2%\\\",\\\"Firm expiry\\\"],\\n [\\\"31-May-2029\\\",\\\"Apex Fulfillment \\\\u2014 scheduled expiry\\\",\\\"557,375.00\\\",\\\"23.7%\\\",\\\"60.9%\\\",\\\"Firm expiry\\\"],\\n [\\\"30-Sep-2030\\\",\\\"The Pint & Platter \\\\u2014 scheduled expiry\\\",\\\"89,386.00\\\",\\\"3.8%\\\",\\\"64.7%\\\",\\\"Firm expiry\\\"],\\n [\\\"31-Dec-2030\\\",\\\"GSA \\\\u2014 absolute expiry of total term\\\",\\\"\\\\u2014\\\",\\\"\\\\u2014\\\",\\\"64.7%\\\",\\\"Firm expiry\\\"],\\n [\\\"31-Mar-2032\\\",\\\"BrightPath Learning \\\\u2014 scheduled expiry\\\",\\\"150,220.00\\\",\\\"6.4%\\\",\\\"71.1%\\\",\\\"Firm expiry\\\"],\\n [\\\"30-Jun-2032\\\",\\\"Verdana Software \\\\u2014 scheduled expiry\\\",\\\"676,312.50\\\",\\\"28.8%\\\",\\\"100.0%\\\",\\\"Firm expiry\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Trigger date\\\",\\\"Event\\\",\\\"Annual rent ($)\\\",\\\"% of total\\\",\\\"Cumulative\\\",\\\"Nature\\\"], rows,\\n          [0.78,2.55,0.85,0.6,0.68,0.94], size=7.9, head_size=7.5, align_center_cols=(0,2,3,4),\\n          row_fills=[WARN,WARN,WARN,None,None,None,None,None,None], keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"Soto appears once only; its 2028 expiry is shown for completeness but the rent is already treated as at risk from 31 October 2025 if the option is exercised. Shaded rows are the three events that occur on or within twelve months after the target closing date. Cumulative percentages are of the $2,347,843.50 aggregate.\\\")\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"1.8  Priorities for Galleon\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"The following eight items should be actioned immediately. Section 7 contains the full risk register and Section 8 the sequenced action plan with owners and deadlines.\\\", size=9.8)\\npri = [\\n (\\\"1\\\",\\\"Obtain a ROFR waiver or estoppel from Apex, or documentary proof that the ROFR was not triggered, expired or was waived — plus a title search for any recorded memorandum of ROFR.\\\",\\\"Before DD expiry (31 Jan 2025)\\\",\\\"R-01\\\"),\\n (\\\"2\\\",\\\"Establish the acquisition structure (asset vs. equity) and, if asset-level, initiate GSA consent/novation; confirm the lender's position on the GSA lease's anti-subordination clause.\\\",\\\"Immediately (financing commitment)\\\",\\\"R-02\\\"),\\n (\\\"3\\\",\\\"Obtain estoppels from all seven tenants with the certifications listed in Section 9, including option status, ROFR waiver, co-tenancy status and any termination notice.\\\",\\\"Target 17 Jan 2025\\\",\\\"R-09\\\"),\\n (\\\"4\\\",\\\"Require Seller to deliver the Haywood Village Shops full rent roll and an occupancy certificate to test the Pint & Platter co-tenancy trigger.\\\",\\\"Before DD expiry\\\",\\\"R-07\\\"),\\n (\\\"5\\\",\\\"Confirm whether Verdana has exercised the 9th-floor expansion option and whether the 9th floor is available to deliver; price the encumbrance or negotiate a waiver.\\\",\\\"Before DD expiry\\\",\\\"R-06\\\"),\\n (\\\"6\\\",\\\"Address the Southeastern holdover: obtain a new lease or a holdover acknowledgment with a fixed term and rent, and pursue environmental diligence on AFFF/PFAS.\\\",\\\"Before closing\\\",\\\"R-04\\\"),\\n (\\\"7\\\",\\\"Reconcile actual billing ledgers for 2024 against the Rent Roll and the lease schedules, and correct the Apex, BrightPath and Southeastern schedule errors.\\\",\\\"Before closing\\\",\\\"R-12, R-13, R-20\\\"),\\n (\\\"8\\\",\\\"Obtain security deposit ledgers and guaranty originals; confirm the amount actually held for BrightPath and the status of the Pint & Platter guaranty.\\\",\\\"Before closing\\\",\\\"R-15, R-21\\\"),\\n]\\nrows = [[a,b,c,d] for a,b,c,d in pri]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"#\\\",\\\"Action\\\",\\\"Deadline\\\",\\\"Risk\\\"], rows, [0.3,3.85,1.85,0.7], size=8.3, head_size=8,\\n          align_center_cols=(0,3), keep_rows=True)\\nPYEOF\\necho ok\"}", "result": "ok\n"}
{"turn": 23, "role": "assistant", "text": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_g0krqgpmkQwHAfXsuQ9A8242", "name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && cat >> work/build.py <<'PYEOF'\\n\\n# ================= 2. SCOPE & METHOD =================\\nh1(doc, \\\"SECTION 2\\\", \\\"Scope, Methodology and Source Inventory\\\")\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"2.1  Engagement basis\\\", space_before=2)\\npara(doc, \\\"This Report is delivered pursuant to the Engagement Letter dated December 5, 2024. Section 2 of the Engagement Letter defines four workstreams, each of which is addressed in a separate section of this Report:\\\", size=9.8)\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"2(a)\\\",\\\"Lease abstraction of the seven specified leases\\\",\\\"Section 4 \\\\u2014 twelve-category abstractions for each lease\\\"],\\n [\\\"2(b)\\\",\\\"Rent roll cross-reference against the underlying leases\\\",\\\"Section 5 \\\\u2014 field-by-field reconciliation\\\"],\\n [\\\"2(c)\\\",\\\"Independent verification of rent escalations and financial terms\\\",\\\"Section 6 and Appendix A\\\"],\\n [\\\"2(d)\\\",\\\"Risk identification: discrepancies, ambiguities, missing documentation, deadlines, holdovers\\\",\\\"Section 7 \\\\u2014 risk register\\\"],\\n [\\\"2(e)\\\",\\\"Standardised twelve-category abstraction format\\\",\\\"Section 4 \\\\u2014 categories (1) to (12) for each lease\\\"],\\n [\\\"2(f)\\\",\\\"Executive summary: aggregate rent, WALT, concentration, prioritised risks, pre-closing actions\\\",\\\"Section 1 and Section 8\\\"],\\n [\\\"3\\\",\\\"Deliverable: individual abstractions, rent roll cross-check, risk matrix by severity and time-sensitivity, recommended actions\\\",\\\"Sections 4, 5, 7, 8\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Engagement Letter \\\\u00a7\\\",\\\"Requirement\\\",\\\"Where addressed in this Report\\\"], rows,\\n          [0.85,3.3,2.55], size=8.3, head_size=8, align_center_cols=(0,), keep_rows=True)\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"2.2  Documents reviewed\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"The Report is based solely on the nine documents listed below, all of which were read in full. A source-to-issue log was maintained throughout so that every proposition, figure and date in this Report can be traced to a document and, where applicable, to an article or section of that document.\\\", size=9.8)\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"D1\\\",\\\"Portfolio Rent Roll\\\",\\\"XLSX\\\",\\\"Karen Osgood, Property Manager, Thornfield Realty Holdings LP\\\",\\\"1 Dec 2024\\\",\\\"Rent Roll + Summary sheets; 7 leases\\\"],\\n [\\\"D2\\\",\\\"Engagement Letter\\\",\\\"DOCX\\\",\\\"Birchwood & Hale LLP to Galleon Capital Advisors LLC\\\",\\\"5 Dec 2024\\\",\\\"Scope, deliverable, fee cap\\\"],\\n [\\\"D3\\\",\\\"Lease Agreement \\\\u2014 Apex Fulfillment Services Inc.\\\",\\\"DOCX\\\",\\\"Thornfield Realty Holdings LP (Landlord)\\\",\\\"1 Mar 2019\\\",\\\"Building C, Thornfield Distribution Center; Ex. A\\\\u2013D\\\"],\\n [\\\"D4\\\",\\\"Medical Office Lease \\\\u2014 Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS, PA\\\",\\\"DOCX\\\",\\\"Thornfield Realty Holdings LP\\\",\\\"15 Sep 2021\\\",\\\"Suite 200, Millbrook Medical Plaza; Ex. A\\\\u2013D\\\"],\\n [\\\"D5\\\",\\\"Lease Agreement \\\\u2014 BrightPath Learning Centers LLC\\\",\\\"DOCX\\\",\\\"Thornfield Realty Holdings LP\\\",\\\"10 Jan 2017\\\",\\\"Suite 100, Millbrook Medical Plaza; Ex. A\\\\u2013D\\\"],\\n [\\\"D6\\\",\\\"Lease Agreement \\\\u2014 Southeastern Fire & Safety Equipment Co.\\\",\\\"DOCX\\\",\\\"Thornfield Realty Holdings LP\\\",\\\"1 Jul 2014\\\",\\\"Unit 12, Greystone Industrial Park; Ex. A\\\\u2013B\\\"],\\n [\\\"D7\\\",\\\"Office Lease Agreement \\\\u2014 Verdana Software Solutions Inc.\\\",\\\"DOCX\\\",\\\"Thornfield Realty Holdings LP\\\",\\\"28 Feb 2022\\\",\\\"8th Floor, Concord Office Tower; Ex. A\\\\u2013E\\\"],\\n [\\\"D8\\\",\\\"Lease Agreement \\\\u2014 The Pint & Platter Restaurant Group LLC\\\",\\\"DOCX\\\",\\\"Thornfield Realty Holdings LP\\\",\\\"15 May 2020\\\",\\\"Unit 4, Haywood Village Shops; Ex. A\\\\u2013D incl. Guaranty\\\"],\\n [\\\"D9\\\",\\\"GSA Lease No. GS-04B-15678 (Form L201D)\\\",\\\"DOCX\\\",\\\"Lessor: Thornfield Realty Holdings LP / Lessee: USA (GSA Region 4)\\\",\\\"30 Sep 2020\\\",\\\"5th Floor, Concord Office Tower; Ex. A\\\\u2013C\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"ID\\\",\\\"Document\\\",\\\"Format\\\",\\\"Parties / addressee\\\",\\\"Date\\\",\\\"Scope of document reviewed\\\"], rows,\\n          [0.32,1.95,0.5,1.55,0.62,1.76], size=7.7, head_size=7.4, align_center_cols=(0,2,4), keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"No amendments, side letters, guaranties (other than the Pint & Platter guaranty at Exhibit D to D8 and the Soto guaranty at Article 21 of D4), SNDAs, estoppel certificates, subleases, commencement date memoranda, or operating expense reconciliations were provided. See Section 10.\\\")\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"2.3  Method\\\")\\nsteps = [\\n \\\"**Inventory and control.** All nine documents were inventoried before analysis and are listed in Section 2.2 and Appendix B. The Engagement Letter was treated as the controlling instruction for the form and content of this Report.\\\",\\n \\\"**Full-text review.** Each lease was read in full, including recitals and exhibits, rather than relying on the Rent Roll's summary. Facts were extracted with section citations and recorded in a source-to-issue log.\\\",\\n \\\"**Independent recomputation.** Every rent schedule was recomputed year by year from the stated starting rent, the stated escalation mechanism and the stated rentable area, and compared with the rate table in the lease and with the Rent Roll (Section 6 and Appendix A). Every percentage share, allowance, amortisation and fee was recomputed from first principles.\\\",\\n \\\"**Date arithmetic.** Commencement and expiration dates, option notice deadlines and notice periods were recomputed from the operative clauses rather than accepted as stated, including the Engagement Letter's own due diligence period.\\\",\\n \\\"**Reconciliation and flagging.** Differences were classified by cause (rounding, drafting error in a single year, error propagating through the term, or a genuine conflict between provisions). Where a conflict exists between two provisions of the same lease, the conflict is described and the probable controlling provision identified; where it cannot be resolved on the documents, it is flagged for follow-up rather than silently resolved.\\\",\\n \\\"**Separation of fact from judgement.** Extracted facts are presented in the abstraction tables; our characterisation and conclusions appear in Sections 1, 3 and 7; open questions are collected in Section 10. Risk ratings are our assessment and are explained in Section 7.1.\\\",\\n]\\nbullets(doc, steps, size=9.3)\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"2.4  Conventions and limitations\\\")\\nconv = [\\n \\\"**Reference date.** Rent, term and option positions are stated as at **January 1, 2025**, consistent with the Rent Roll, unless another date is given. Remaining terms are measured from January 1, 2025.\\\",\\n \\\"**Rent convention.** \\\\u201cCurrent annual base rent\\\\u201d means the contractual base or shell rent for the Lease Year in effect on the reference date, excluding operating expense recoveries, percentage rent and parking income. For Southeastern and GSA it is the Rent Roll figure, which is at-will rent rather than term rent; this is noted wherever it matters.\\\",\\n \\\"**Lease Year convention.** Each lease defines its own Lease Year from its own commencement date; the \\\\u201ccurrent Lease Year\\\\u201d stated for each tenant therefore falls on a different calendar boundary.\\\",\\n \\\"**Rounding.** Per-square-foot rates are quoted as stated in the leases. Where we recompute a rate, we round to the nearest $0.001 per RSF per annum for the Apex and BrightPath leases (which use that convention) and to the nearest cent elsewhere, matching each lease's own stated convention. Annual and monthly amounts are rounded to the nearest cent.\\\",\\n \\\"**Area convention.** Rentable square footage is taken as stipulated in each lease. Neither Millbrook lease, the Greystone lease nor the GSA lease states the building or park denominator used for the tenant's proportionate share, so the recovery percentage for those four leases could not be verified (R-19).\\\",\\n \\\"**Not a title, environmental or financial review.** Title, survey, environmental, structural, zoning and tenant credit review are outside scope (Engagement Letter \\\\u00a7 2, scope limitations) and are being handled by Stonebridge Title & Escrow LLC, Hanover Environmental Consultants Inc. and Crestline Accounting Group LLP respectively. Where this Report touches on those matters it does so only to identify a lease-based issue that requires referral.\\\",\\n \\\"**No verification of tenant assertions.** Nothing in this Report verifies any fact stated in a lease by a tenant, or the truth of any representation made by the Seller or the Rent Roll. See Section 11.\\\",\\n]\\nbullets(doc, conv, size=9.3)\\nPYEOF\\necho ok\"}"}], "input_tokens": 169587, "output_tokens": 2045, "finish_reason": "completed"}
{"turn": 23, "role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call_00_g0krqgpmkQwHAfXsuQ9A8242", "tool_name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && cat >> work/build.py <<'PYEOF'\\n\\n# ================= 2. SCOPE & METHOD =================\\nh1(doc, \\\"SECTION 2\\\", \\\"Scope, Methodology and Source Inventory\\\")\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"2.1  Engagement basis\\\", space_before=2)\\npara(doc, \\\"This Report is delivered pursuant to the Engagement Letter dated December 5, 2024. Section 2 of the Engagement Letter defines four workstreams, each of which is addressed in a separate section of this Report:\\\", size=9.8)\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"2(a)\\\",\\\"Lease abstraction of the seven specified leases\\\",\\\"Section 4 \\\\u2014 twelve-category abstractions for each lease\\\"],\\n [\\\"2(b)\\\",\\\"Rent roll cross-reference against the underlying leases\\\",\\\"Section 5 \\\\u2014 field-by-field reconciliation\\\"],\\n [\\\"2(c)\\\",\\\"Independent verification of rent escalations and financial terms\\\",\\\"Section 6 and Appendix A\\\"],\\n [\\\"2(d)\\\",\\\"Risk identification: discrepancies, ambiguities, missing documentation, deadlines, holdovers\\\",\\\"Section 7 \\\\u2014 risk register\\\"],\\n [\\\"2(e)\\\",\\\"Standardised twelve-category abstraction format\\\",\\\"Section 4 \\\\u2014 categories (1) to (12) for each lease\\\"],\\n [\\\"2(f)\\\",\\\"Executive summary: aggregate rent, WALT, concentration, prioritised risks, pre-closing actions\\\",\\\"Section 1 and Section 8\\\"],\\n [\\\"3\\\",\\\"Deliverable: individual abstractions, rent roll cross-check, risk matrix by severity and time-sensitivity, recommended actions\\\",\\\"Sections 4, 5, 7, 8\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Engagement Letter \\\\u00a7\\\",\\\"Requirement\\\",\\\"Where addressed in this Report\\\"], rows,\\n          [0.85,3.3,2.55], size=8.3, head_size=8, align_center_cols=(0,), keep_rows=True)\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"2.2  Documents reviewed\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"The Report is based solely on the nine documents listed below, all of which were read in full. A source-to-issue log was maintained throughout so that every proposition, figure and date in this Report can be traced to a document and, where applicable, to an article or section of that document.\\\", size=9.8)\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"D1\\\",\\\"Portfolio Rent Roll\\\",\\\"XLSX\\\",\\\"Karen Osgood, Property Manager, Thornfield Realty Holdings LP\\\",\\\"1 Dec 2024\\\",\\\"Rent Roll + Summary sheets; 7 leases\\\"],\\n [\\\"D2\\\",\\\"Engagement Letter\\\",\\\"DOCX\\\",\\\"Birchwood & Hale LLP to Galleon Capital Advisors LLC\\\",\\\"5 Dec 2024\\\",\\\"Scope, deliverable, fee cap\\\"],\\n [\\\"D3\\\",\\\"Lease Agreement \\\\u2014 Apex Fulfillment Services Inc.\\\",\\\"DOCX\\\",\\\"Thornfield Realty Holdings LP (Landlord)\\\",\\\"1 Mar 2019\\\",\\\"Building C, Thornfield Distribution Center; Ex. A\\\\u2013D\\\"],\\n [\\\"D4\\\",\\\"Medical Office Lease \\\\u2014 Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS, PA\\\",\\\"DOCX\\\",\\\"Thornfield Realty Holdings LP\\\",\\\"15 Sep 2021\\\",\\\"Suite 200, Millbrook Medical Plaza; Ex. A\\\\u2013D\\\"],\\n [\\\"D5\\\",\\\"Lease Agreement \\\\u2014 BrightPath Learning Centers LLC\\\",\\\"DOCX\\\",\\\"Thornfield Realty Holdings LP\\\",\\\"10 Jan 2017\\\",\\\"Suite 100, Millbrook Medical Plaza; Ex. A\\\\u2013D\\\"],\\n [\\\"D6\\\",\\\"Lease Agreement \\\\u2014 Southeastern Fire & Safety Equipment Co.\\\",\\\"DOCX\\\",\\\"Thornfield Realty Holdings LP\\\",\\\"1 Jul 2014\\\",\\\"Unit 12, Greystone Industrial Park; Ex. A\\\\u2013B\\\"],\\n [\\\"D7\\\",\\\"Office Lease Agreement \\\\u2014 Verdana Software Solutions Inc.\\\",\\\"DOCX\\\",\\\"Thornfield Realty Holdings LP\\\",\\\"28 Feb 2022\\\",\\\"8th Floor, Concord Office Tower; Ex. A\\\\u2013E\\\"],\\n [\\\"D8\\\",\\\"Lease Agreement \\\\u2014 The Pint & Platter Restaurant Group LLC\\\",\\\"DOCX\\\",\\\"Thornfield Realty Holdings LP\\\",\\\"15 May 2020\\\",\\\"Unit 4, Haywood Village Shops; Ex. A\\\\u2013D incl. Guaranty\\\"],\\n [\\\"D9\\\",\\\"GSA Lease No. GS-04B-15678 (Form L201D)\\\",\\\"DOCX\\\",\\\"Lessor: Thornfield Realty Holdings LP / Lessee: USA (GSA Region 4)\\\",\\\"30 Sep 2020\\\",\\\"5th Floor, Concord Office Tower; Ex. A\\\\u2013C\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"ID\\\",\\\"Document\\\",\\\"Format\\\",\\\"Parties / addressee\\\",\\\"Date\\\",\\\"Scope of document reviewed\\\"], rows,\\n          [0.32,1.95,0.5,1.55,0.62,1.76], size=7.7, head_size=7.4, align_center_cols=(0,2,4), keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"No amendments, side letters, guaranties (other than the Pint & Platter guaranty at Exhibit D to D8 and the Soto guaranty at Article 21 of D4), SNDAs, estoppel certificates, subleases, commencement date memoranda, or operating expense reconciliations were provided. See Section 10.\\\")\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"2.3  Method\\\")\\nsteps = [\\n \\\"**Inventory and control.** All nine documents were inventoried before analysis and are listed in Section 2.2 and Appendix B. The Engagement Letter was treated as the controlling instruction for the form and content of this Report.\\\",\\n \\\"**Full-text review.** Each lease was read in full, including recitals and exhibits, rather than relying on the Rent Roll's summary. Facts were extracted with section citations and recorded in a source-to-issue log.\\\",\\n \\\"**Independent recomputation.** Every rent schedule was recomputed year by year from the stated starting rent, the stated escalation mechanism and the stated rentable area, and compared with the rate table in the lease and with the Rent Roll (Section 6 and Appendix A). Every percentage share, allowance, amortisation and fee was recomputed from first principles.\\\",\\n \\\"**Date arithmetic.** Commencement and expiration dates, option notice deadlines and notice periods were recomputed from the operative clauses rather than accepted as stated, including the Engagement Letter's own due diligence period.\\\",\\n \\\"**Reconciliation and flagging.** Differences were classified by cause (rounding, drafting error in a single year, error propagating through the term, or a genuine conflict between provisions). Where a conflict exists between two provisions of the same lease, the conflict is described and the probable controlling provision identified; where it cannot be resolved on the documents, it is flagged for follow-up rather than silently resolved.\\\",\\n \\\"**Separation of fact from judgement.** Extracted facts are presented in the abstraction tables; our characterisation and conclusions appear in Sections 1, 3 and 7; open questions are collected in Section 10. Risk ratings are our assessment and are explained in Section 7.1.\\\",\\n]\\nbullets(doc, steps, size=9.3)\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"2.4  Conventions and limitations\\\")\\nconv = [\\n \\\"**Reference date.** Rent, term and option positions are stated as at **January 1, 2025**, consistent with the Rent Roll, unless another date is given. Remaining terms are measured from January 1, 2025.\\\",\\n \\\"**Rent convention.** \\\\u201cCurrent annual base rent\\\\u201d means the contractual base or shell rent for the Lease Year in effect on the reference date, excluding operating expense recoveries, percentage rent and parking income. For Southeastern and GSA it is the Rent Roll figure, which is at-will rent rather than term rent; this is noted wherever it matters.\\\",\\n \\\"**Lease Year convention.** Each lease defines its own Lease Year from its own commencement date; the \\\\u201ccurrent Lease Year\\\\u201d stated for each tenant therefore falls on a different calendar boundary.\\\",\\n \\\"**Rounding.** Per-square-foot rates are quoted as stated in the leases. Where we recompute a rate, we round to the nearest $0.001 per RSF per annum for the Apex and BrightPath leases (which use that convention) and to the nearest cent elsewhere, matching each lease's own stated convention. Annual and monthly amounts are rounded to the nearest cent.\\\",\\n \\\"**Area convention.** Rentable square footage is taken as stipulated in each lease. Neither Millbrook lease, the Greystone lease nor the GSA lease states the building or park denominator used for the tenant's proportionate share, so the recovery percentage for those four leases could not be verified (R-19).\\\",\\n \\\"**Not a title, environmental or financial review.** Title, survey, environmental, structural, zoning and tenant credit review are outside scope (Engagement Letter \\\\u00a7 2, scope limitations) and are being handled by Stonebridge Title & Escrow LLC, Hanover Environmental Consultants Inc. and Crestline Accounting Group LLP respectively. Where this Report touches on those matters it does so only to identify a lease-based issue that requires referral.\\\",\\n \\\"**No verification of tenant assertions.** Nothing in this Report verifies any fact stated in a lease by a tenant, or the truth of any representation made by the Seller or the Rent Roll. See Section 11.\\\",\\n]\\nbullets(doc, conv, size=9.3)\\nPYEOF\\necho ok\"}", "result": "ok\n"}
{"turn": 24, "role": "assistant", "text": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_HoUuChzsOdhASs8XedRZ4879", "name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && cat >> work/build.py <<'PYEOF'\\n\\n# ================= 3. PORTFOLIO ANALYSIS =================\\nh1(doc, \\\"SECTION 3\\\", \\\"Portfolio-Level Analysis\\\")\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"3.1  Rent-at-risk: what is and is not firm\\\", space_before=2)\\npara(doc, \\\"Three of the seven tenancies are not firm beyond twelve months. Each fails in a different way, and each requires a different remedy, so they are analysed separately rather than aggregated.\\\", size=9.8)\\nh3(doc, \\\"Southeastern Fire & Safety \\\\u2014 expired lease, at-will holdover\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"The ten-year term expired on June 30, 2024. The tenant's single five-year renewal option required written notice by April 1, 2024 and lapsed unexercised, so **no renewal right remains**. Since July 1, 2024 the tenant has occupied month-to-month at 150% of the final month's rent \\\\u2014 $25,437.50 per month, $305,250 per annum \\\\u2014 and either party may terminate on 30 days' written notice (Article 13). There is no security deposit, no guaranty and no letter of credit. The tenant is therefore paying a 50% premium but can leave at any time, and the Landlord can require it to leave at any time on 30 days' notice. For a purchaser this is 13.0% of aggregate rent that is both terminable at will by the tenant and unsupported by credit enhancement. It is also the tenancy that carries the most significant environmental exposure in the portfolio, since the permitted use expressly includes storage and handling of aqueous film-forming foam, foam concentrates and PFAS-containing materials (Article 14).\\\", size=9.8)\\nh3(doc, \\\"GSA \\\\u2014 twelve months of firm term, then terminable at will\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"The firm term runs from January 1, 2021 to December 31, 2025. After the firm term expiration date the lease continues for a five-year soft term during which the Government may terminate at any time on not less than 120 calendar days' written notice, with **no termination fee, penalty or liquidated damages** (\\\\u00a7 3.2). The lease states expressly that soft-term rent is \\\\u201ccontingent upon the Government's continued occupancy and is not guaranteed beyond the Firm Term Expiration Date\\\\u201d. The Rent Roll nonetheless includes the full $472,500 in the aggregate. In substance Galleon is buying twelve months of government rent with an option over the following five years at the Government's sole election.\\\", size=9.8)\\nh3(doc, \\\"Dr. Miriam Soto \\\\u2014 contractual but terminable on payment of a modest fee\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"The term runs to October 31, 2028, but Article 20 gives the tenant a right to terminate effective October 31, 2025 on 60 days' notice (deliverable by April 30, 2025) and payment of $40,657.14. We recomputed the fee: unamortised TI allowance of $38,400 \\\\u00d7 3/7 = $16,457.14, plus three months' base rent of $96,800 \\\\u00f7 4 = $24,200.00, total $40,657.14 \\\\u2014 consistent with the lease and with Exhibit D. Because the fee is roughly five months' rent and the tenant would otherwise owe three further years, the right is economically attractive to the tenant and the exposure is material relative to a 3,200 RSF suite: net exposure approximately $264,143.\\\", size=9.8)\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"3.2  Encumbrances on leasing and value\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"Four lease provisions constrain what Galleon can do with the properties after closing, independently of rent. They are the items most likely to be missed in a rent-roll-based valuation.\\\", size=9.8)\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"Right of first refusal over Building C, expressly including portfolio transactions (Art. XIII)\\\",\\\"Prevents sale of Building C to Galleon on the PSA terms if validly triggered; 30-day exercise period; allocable price mechanism; reinstatement if Seller does not close within 180 days.\\\",\\\"R-01\\\"],\\n [\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"Exclusive use for fulfillment, logistics, distribution and warehousing across **all three buildings** (A, B and C) (\\\\u00a7 6.2)\\\",\\\"Buildings A and B cannot be leased to any logistics, distribution or warehouse user for the balance of the term (to 5/31/2029 plus renewals). If A or B is presently occupied by such a user the Landlord is already in breach.\\\",\\\"R-08\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"Expansion option over the entire 9th floor, ~18,500 RSF, at the then-current 8th-floor rate plus $40/RSF allowance, coterminous to 6/30/2032 (Art. XIII)\\\",\\\"9th-floor space (12.3% of the building) is effectively pre-let at a 2022 rent schedule; the Lessor cannot lease it at market and must fund $740,000 of allowance if exercised.\\\",\\\"R-06\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"Co-tenancy right: 70% occupancy test on the whole 62,000 RSF centre (Art. 10)\\\",\\\"If centre occupancy falls below 70% for more than 180 consecutive days, tenant may cut rent to 75% or terminate on 60 days' notice. Trigger status cannot be verified on the documents provided.\\\",\\\"R-07\\\"],\\n [\\\"BrightPath\\\",\\\"Exclusive use for childcare/daycare/early education in Millbrook Medical Plaza (\\\\u00a7 7.2)\\\",\\\"Precludes leasing any other suite at Millbrook to a childcare or daycare operator; relevant to re-letting Suite 200 if Soto terminates.\\\",\\\"R-08\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"Exclusive use for a full-service restaurant, with QSR carve-out below 2,000 RSF (\\\\u00a7 5.2)\\\",\\\"Limits re-letting options at Haywood Village Shops to food users below 2,000 RSF or non-food uses; breach gives rent abatement as well as injunctive relief.\\\",\\\"R-08\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Lease\\\",\\\"Provision\\\",\\\"Effect on Galleon\\\",\\\"Risk\\\"], rows, [0.72,1.85,3.6,0.53], size=7.9, head_size=7.6,\\n          align_center_cols=(0,3), keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"The Rent Roll's Notes column refers to the Apex ROFR (\\\\u201cROFR on Building C\\\\u201d) and the Verdana expansion and contraction options, but does not describe the portfolio-transaction trigger in the Apex ROFR, the Apex exclusive-use covenant, or either of the other exclusive-use covenants. See Section 5.4.\\\")\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"3.3  Operating expense mechanics\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"The seven leases use five different recovery structures. That matters for value because base rent is only part of the revenue, and because Galleon will inherit seven different recovery calculations, five different audit regimes and four leases with no stated building denominator.\\\", size=9.8)\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"NNN\\\",\\\"Pro rata 36.46% (87,500 / 240,000)\\\",\\\"None \\\\u2014 \\\\u00a7 5.3 states expressly that there is no cap\\\",\\\"5% of gross rental revenues\\\",\\\"Annual, 30 days' notice; >5% overcharge: landlord pays audit\\\"],\\n [\\\"Soto\\\",\\\"Modified gross\\\",\\\"Base year 2022; increases above base year only\\\",\\\"None stated\\\",\\\"\\\\u201cNot to exceed a market-rate percentage\\\\u201d \\\\u2014 no figure\\\",\\\"Annual; 12-month limit; no overcharge cost-shift\\\"],\\n [\\\"BrightPath\\\",\\\"NNN\\\",\\\"Pro rata 5,800 / Building RSF (**denominator not stated**)\\\",\\\"None; capex limited to law-mandated post-commencement items amortised at \\\\u22648%\\\",\\\"5% of gross revenues from Building\\\",\\\"Annual, 30 days' notice; >5% overcharge: landlord pays audit\\\"],\\n [\\\"Southeastern\\\",\\\"NNN (absolutely net)\\\",\\\"Pro rata 22,000 / Building or Park RSF (**not stated**)\\\",\\\"None\\\",\\\"5% of gross rental income\\\",\\\"Annual, 90 days; **no tenant audit right**\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"Full-service gross\\\",\\\"Base year 2022 expense stop; pro rata 12.50% (18,750 / 150,000)\\\",\\\"**Yes** \\\\u2014 controllable expenses capped at 5% p.a. compounding; gross-up to 95% occupancy\\\",\\\"4% of Building gross revenues\\\",\\\"Annual, 30 days' notice; >5% overcharge: landlord pays audit\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"NNN + percentage rent\\\",\\\"Pro rata 7.10% (4,400 / 62,000)\\\",\\\"None; capex excluded except law-required/reducing, amortised\\\",\\\"4% of gross rental revenue (CAM)\\\",\\\"Annual, 30 days' notice\\\"],\\n [\\\"GSA\\\",\\\"Government full service\\\",\\\"Base year 2021; increases above base year only; pro rata 15,000 / Building RSF (**not stated**)\\\",\\\"None\\\",\\\"Not capped in the lease\\\",\\\"Annual, 90 days; Government may audit during term and for 3 years after\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Lease\\\",\\\"Structure\\\",\\\"Recovery share\\\",\\\"Cap on recoveries\\\",\\\"Management fee\\\",\\\"Reconciliation and audit\\\"], rows,\\n          [0.72,1.02,1.62,1.55,1.02,1.77], size=7.4, head_size=7.3, keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"Denominators: the Apex, Verdana and Pint & Platter leases state the building or centre area, so their shares were verified. The Soto, BrightPath, Southeastern and GSA leases do not state the denominator. Verdana's lease states the building area as approximately 150,000 RSF; applying that figure to the GSA lease (same building) would give the Government a 10.00% share, but the GSA lease itself does not fix the percentage.\\\")\\nbox(doc, \\\"Observation \\\\u2014 two base years in one building\\\",\\n    [\\\"The Verdana lease uses **calendar year 2022** as its expense stop and the GSA lease (same building) uses **calendar year 2021**. Two tenants in Concord Office Tower therefore reimburse operating expense increases on different bases, and Verdana's recoveries benefit from an additional cap that GSA does not have. Galleon will need both base-year expense statements to reconcile 2025 recoveries, and should obtain the certified 2021 statement that the GSA lease required the Lessor to deliver by March 31, 2022 (Exhibit C).\\\"],\\n    fill=BOX, size=8.8)\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"3.4  Credit support\\\")\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"23.7%\\\",\\\"None\\\",\\\"No deposit, no guaranty, no letter of credit in the lease\\\",\\\"R-21\\\"],\\n [\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto\\\",\\\"4.1%\\\",\\\"Personal guaranty\\\",\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto, individually \\\\u2014 payment and performance, not merely collection; survives amendments; runs through any renewal term (to 10/31/2033)\\\",\\\"\\\"],\\n [\\\"BrightPath\\\",\\\"6.4%\\\",\\\"Security deposit $25,440\\\",\\\"Described as \\\\u201ctwo (2) months of Base Rent\\\\u201d \\\\u2014 but two months of current rent is $25,036.67; amount to be confirmed and transferred\\\",\\\"R-15\\\"],\\n [\\\"Southeastern\\\",\\\"13.0%\\\",\\\"None\\\",\\\"No deposit, no guaranty; at-will holdover\\\",\\\"R-21\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"28.8%\\\",\\\"None\\\",\\\"Lease states \\\\u201cSecurity Deposit: None\\\\u201d\\\",\\\"R-21\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"3.8%\\\",\\\"Deposit $19,800 + personal guaranty\\\",\\\"Deposit equals three months of Lease Year 1 rent (verified). Guaranty by Lance Whitford **burns off at the earlier of 9/30/2025 or $2,000,000 trailing-12-month gross sales**\\\",\\\"R-21\\\"],\\n [\\\"United States (GSA)\\\",\\\"20.1%\\\",\\\"None required\\\",\\\"Government self-insured; full faith and credit of the United States\\\",\\\"\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Lease\\\",\\\"% of rent\\\",\\\"Instrument\\\",\\\"Terms and verification\\\",\\\"Risk\\\"], rows, [1.05,0.6,1.25,3.25,0.55],\\n          size=7.9, head_size=7.6, align_center_cols=(1,4), keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"Two deposits are held and both should be dealt with as closing prorations: either transferred to Galleon with a Seller credit, or credited to Galleon against the purchase price. The Pint & Platter guaranty may already have burned off; Seller should provide the certified gross sales reports and any release executed under Exhibit D \\\\u00a7 2.\\\")\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"3.5  Consents, estoppels and non-disturbance\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"The lease documents give Galleon limited ability to compel the documentation a purchaser or lender will require. The position is summarised below and the required certifications are set out in Section 9.\\\", size=9.8)\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"**Yes** \\\\u2014 within 10 business days of request (\\\\u00a7 17.1)\\\",\\\"Yes \\\\u2014 failure to deliver is an irrevocable acknowledgment of the landlord's form (\\\\u00a7 17.2)\\\",\\\"Self-operative subordination; **no non-disturbance obligation**; failure to execute attornment documents is a default (\\\\u00a7 8.4)\\\",\\\"None on file\\\"],\\n [\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto\\\",\\\"No estoppel provision in the lease\\\",\\\"\\\\u2014\\\",\\\"Landlord to use \\\\u201ccommercially reasonable efforts\\\\u201d to obtain SNDA within 60 days of commencement (\\\\u00a7 12.1)\\\",\\\"None on file\\\"],\\n [\\\"BrightPath\\\",\\\"No estoppel provision in the lease\\\",\\\"\\\\u2014\\\",\\\"Landlord to use commercially reasonable efforts; deliver to tenant within 30 days of request (Art. 17)\\\",\\\"None on file\\\"],\\n [\\\"Southeastern\\\",\\\"No estoppel provision in the lease\\\",\\\"\\\\u2014\\\",\\\"Self-operative subordination; **no non-disturbance**; tenant appoints Landlord attorney-in-fact to sign (Art. 16)\\\",\\\"None on file\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"**Yes** \\\\u2014 within 15 business days (Art. XXIV)\\\",\\\"Yes \\\\u2014 deemed acknowledgment applies to either party\\\",\\\"Subordination expressly conditioned on a commercially reasonable SNDA (17.01); landlord represented no mortgage on the building as at 2/28/2022 (17.02)\\\",\\\"None on file\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"No estoppel provision in the lease\\\",\\\"\\\\u2014\\\",\\\"Landlord to use commercially reasonable efforts (Art. 12)\\\",\\\"None on file\\\"],\\n [\\\"United States (GSA)\\\",\\\"No estoppel provision; certificates of lease status are arranged through the Contracting Officer\\\",\\\"\\\\u2014\\\",\\\"**Lease is senior** \\\\u2014 not subordinate to any mortgage; lessor may not grant a priority mortgage without consent; SNDA only if the Government requests (Art. 16)\\\",\\\"Not applicable\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Lease\\\",\\\"Tenant estoppel obligation\\\",\\\"Deemed acknowledgment\\\",\\\"Subordination / SNDA posture\\\",\\\"SNDA on file\\\"], rows,\\n          [0.88,1.5,1.32,2.3,0.7], size=7.4, head_size=7.3, keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"Consequence: for five of the seven leases Galleon has no contractual right to an estoppel at all, and for none of the seven is there a non-disturbance agreement in place. The PSA should therefore carry an express estoppel condition covering each tenant, and the lender's SNDA requirements should be tested against the Apex, Southeastern and GSA provisions before the financing commitment is finalised.\\\")\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"3.6  Option and notice deadlines\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"The following dates are computed from the operative notice provisions. Dates marked \\\\u200b\\\\u201copen now\\\\u201d have already begun to run and require immediate attention.\\\", size=9.8)\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"ROFR over Building C\\\",\\\"30 days from delivery of a ROFR Notice\\\",\\\"On any triggering offer \\\\u2014 **may have been triggered by the PSA (15 Nov 2024)**\\\",\\\"R-01\\\"],\\n [\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"Renewal option 1 / option 2\\\",\\\"12 months before expiry\\\",\\\"31 May 2028  /  31 May 2033\\\",\\\"R-18\\\"],\\n [\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto\\\",\\\"Early termination notice\\\",\\\"6 months before effective date\\\",\\\"**30 April 2025** \\\\u2014 46 days after target closing\\\",\\\"R-05\\\"],\\n [\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto\\\",\\\"Renewal option\\\",\\\"9 months before expiry\\\",\\\"31 January 2028\\\",\\\"\\\"],\\n [\\\"BrightPath\\\",\\\"Renewal option 1\\\",\\\"12 months before expiry\\\",\\\"31 March 2031\\\",\\\"\\\"],\\n [\\\"Southeastern\\\",\\\"Renewal option\\\",\\\"90 days before expiry\\\",\\\"**Lapsed** \\\\u2014 1 April 2024; no renewal right remains\\\",\\\"R-04\\\"],\\n [\\\"Southeastern\\\",\\\"Termination of holdover\\\",\\\"30 days' notice\\\",\\\"Either party, at any time\\\",\\\"R-04\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"Expansion option (9th floor)\\\",\\\"6 months before desired commencement\\\",\\\"Window **1 July 2024 \\\\u2013 30 June 2027 \\\\u2014 open now**\\\",\\\"R-06\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"Contraction notice\\\",\\\"9 months before contraction date\\\",\\\"First available 1 July 2027 (earliest contraction 1 April 2028)\\\",\\\"R-17\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"Renewal option 1\\\",\\\"12 months before expiry\\\",\\\"30 June 2031\\\",\\\"\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"Co-tenancy right\\\",\\\"Rolling \\\\u2014 180 consecutive days below 70%\\\",\\\"**Status unknown \\\\u2014 may already be running**\\\",\\\"R-07\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"Renewal option 1\\\",\\\"9 months before expiry\\\",\\\"31 December 2029\\\",\\\"\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"Guaranty burn-off\\\",\\\"Earlier of fixed date or sales test\\\",\\\"**30 September 2025** or $2,000,000 trailing-12-month sales\\\",\\\"R-21\\\"],\\n [\\\"United States (GSA)\\\",\\\"Firm term expiry\\\",\\\"\\\\u2014\\\",\\\"**31 December 2025**\\\",\\\"R-03\\\"],\\n [\\\"United States (GSA)\\\",\\\"Government termination (soft term)\\\",\\\"120 calendar days' notice\\\",\\\"Any time after 31 December 2025\\\",\\\"R-03\\\"],\\n [\\\"All\\\",\\\"Estoppel delivery\\\",\\\"10 business days (Apex); 15 business days (Verdana)\\\",\\\"On Galleon's request \\\\u2014 action now\\\",\\\"R-09\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Lease\\\",\\\"Right or obligation\\\",\\\"Notice period\\\",\\\"Key date\\\",\\\"Risk\\\"], rows, [0.85,1.55,1.5,2.25,0.55],\\n          size=7.6, head_size=7.4, align_center_cols=(4,), keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"Deadlines recomputed from each lease's operative clause and cross-checked against the expiry date. The Rent Roll does not state any option or notice deadline other than the Southeastern lapse; the Soto early termination deadline of 30 April 2025 is the most time-critical omission because it falls within seven weeks of the target closing date (Risk R-09).\\\")\\nPYEOF\\necho ok\"}"}], "input_tokens": 171646, "output_tokens": 4508, "finish_reason": "completed"}
{"turn": 24, "role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call_00_HoUuChzsOdhASs8XedRZ4879", "tool_name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && cat >> work/build.py <<'PYEOF'\\n\\n# ================= 3. PORTFOLIO ANALYSIS =================\\nh1(doc, \\\"SECTION 3\\\", \\\"Portfolio-Level Analysis\\\")\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"3.1  Rent-at-risk: what is and is not firm\\\", space_before=2)\\npara(doc, \\\"Three of the seven tenancies are not firm beyond twelve months. Each fails in a different way, and each requires a different remedy, so they are analysed separately rather than aggregated.\\\", size=9.8)\\nh3(doc, \\\"Southeastern Fire & Safety \\\\u2014 expired lease, at-will holdover\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"The ten-year term expired on June 30, 2024. The tenant's single five-year renewal option required written notice by April 1, 2024 and lapsed unexercised, so **no renewal right remains**. Since July 1, 2024 the tenant has occupied month-to-month at 150% of the final month's rent \\\\u2014 $25,437.50 per month, $305,250 per annum \\\\u2014 and either party may terminate on 30 days' written notice (Article 13). There is no security deposit, no guaranty and no letter of credit. The tenant is therefore paying a 50% premium but can leave at any time, and the Landlord can require it to leave at any time on 30 days' notice. For a purchaser this is 13.0% of aggregate rent that is both terminable at will by the tenant and unsupported by credit enhancement. It is also the tenancy that carries the most significant environmental exposure in the portfolio, since the permitted use expressly includes storage and handling of aqueous film-forming foam, foam concentrates and PFAS-containing materials (Article 14).\\\", size=9.8)\\nh3(doc, \\\"GSA \\\\u2014 twelve months of firm term, then terminable at will\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"The firm term runs from January 1, 2021 to December 31, 2025. After the firm term expiration date the lease continues for a five-year soft term during which the Government may terminate at any time on not less than 120 calendar days' written notice, with **no termination fee, penalty or liquidated damages** (\\\\u00a7 3.2). The lease states expressly that soft-term rent is \\\\u201ccontingent upon the Government's continued occupancy and is not guaranteed beyond the Firm Term Expiration Date\\\\u201d. The Rent Roll nonetheless includes the full $472,500 in the aggregate. In substance Galleon is buying twelve months of government rent with an option over the following five years at the Government's sole election.\\\", size=9.8)\\nh3(doc, \\\"Dr. Miriam Soto \\\\u2014 contractual but terminable on payment of a modest fee\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"The term runs to October 31, 2028, but Article 20 gives the tenant a right to terminate effective October 31, 2025 on 60 days' notice (deliverable by April 30, 2025) and payment of $40,657.14. We recomputed the fee: unamortised TI allowance of $38,400 \\\\u00d7 3/7 = $16,457.14, plus three months' base rent of $96,800 \\\\u00f7 4 = $24,200.00, total $40,657.14 \\\\u2014 consistent with the lease and with Exhibit D. Because the fee is roughly five months' rent and the tenant would otherwise owe three further years, the right is economically attractive to the tenant and the exposure is material relative to a 3,200 RSF suite: net exposure approximately $264,143.\\\", size=9.8)\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"3.2  Encumbrances on leasing and value\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"Four lease provisions constrain what Galleon can do with the properties after closing, independently of rent. They are the items most likely to be missed in a rent-roll-based valuation.\\\", size=9.8)\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"Right of first refusal over Building C, expressly including portfolio transactions (Art. XIII)\\\",\\\"Prevents sale of Building C to Galleon on the PSA terms if validly triggered; 30-day exercise period; allocable price mechanism; reinstatement if Seller does not close within 180 days.\\\",\\\"R-01\\\"],\\n [\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"Exclusive use for fulfillment, logistics, distribution and warehousing across **all three buildings** (A, B and C) (\\\\u00a7 6.2)\\\",\\\"Buildings A and B cannot be leased to any logistics, distribution or warehouse user for the balance of the term (to 5/31/2029 plus renewals). If A or B is presently occupied by such a user the Landlord is already in breach.\\\",\\\"R-08\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"Expansion option over the entire 9th floor, ~18,500 RSF, at the then-current 8th-floor rate plus $40/RSF allowance, coterminous to 6/30/2032 (Art. XIII)\\\",\\\"9th-floor space (12.3% of the building) is effectively pre-let at a 2022 rent schedule; the Lessor cannot lease it at market and must fund $740,000 of allowance if exercised.\\\",\\\"R-06\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"Co-tenancy right: 70% occupancy test on the whole 62,000 RSF centre (Art. 10)\\\",\\\"If centre occupancy falls below 70% for more than 180 consecutive days, tenant may cut rent to 75% or terminate on 60 days' notice. Trigger status cannot be verified on the documents provided.\\\",\\\"R-07\\\"],\\n [\\\"BrightPath\\\",\\\"Exclusive use for childcare/daycare/early education in Millbrook Medical Plaza (\\\\u00a7 7.2)\\\",\\\"Precludes leasing any other suite at Millbrook to a childcare or daycare operator; relevant to re-letting Suite 200 if Soto terminates.\\\",\\\"R-08\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"Exclusive use for a full-service restaurant, with QSR carve-out below 2,000 RSF (\\\\u00a7 5.2)\\\",\\\"Limits re-letting options at Haywood Village Shops to food users below 2,000 RSF or non-food uses; breach gives rent abatement as well as injunctive relief.\\\",\\\"R-08\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Lease\\\",\\\"Provision\\\",\\\"Effect on Galleon\\\",\\\"Risk\\\"], rows, [0.72,1.85,3.6,0.53], size=7.9, head_size=7.6,\\n          align_center_cols=(0,3), keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"The Rent Roll's Notes column refers to the Apex ROFR (\\\\u201cROFR on Building C\\\\u201d) and the Verdana expansion and contraction options, but does not describe the portfolio-transaction trigger in the Apex ROFR, the Apex exclusive-use covenant, or either of the other exclusive-use covenants. See Section 5.4.\\\")\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"3.3  Operating expense mechanics\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"The seven leases use five different recovery structures. That matters for value because base rent is only part of the revenue, and because Galleon will inherit seven different recovery calculations, five different audit regimes and four leases with no stated building denominator.\\\", size=9.8)\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"NNN\\\",\\\"Pro rata 36.46% (87,500 / 240,000)\\\",\\\"None \\\\u2014 \\\\u00a7 5.3 states expressly that there is no cap\\\",\\\"5% of gross rental revenues\\\",\\\"Annual, 30 days' notice; >5% overcharge: landlord pays audit\\\"],\\n [\\\"Soto\\\",\\\"Modified gross\\\",\\\"Base year 2022; increases above base year only\\\",\\\"None stated\\\",\\\"\\\\u201cNot to exceed a market-rate percentage\\\\u201d \\\\u2014 no figure\\\",\\\"Annual; 12-month limit; no overcharge cost-shift\\\"],\\n [\\\"BrightPath\\\",\\\"NNN\\\",\\\"Pro rata 5,800 / Building RSF (**denominator not stated**)\\\",\\\"None; capex limited to law-mandated post-commencement items amortised at \\\\u22648%\\\",\\\"5% of gross revenues from Building\\\",\\\"Annual, 30 days' notice; >5% overcharge: landlord pays audit\\\"],\\n [\\\"Southeastern\\\",\\\"NNN (absolutely net)\\\",\\\"Pro rata 22,000 / Building or Park RSF (**not stated**)\\\",\\\"None\\\",\\\"5% of gross rental income\\\",\\\"Annual, 90 days; **no tenant audit right**\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"Full-service gross\\\",\\\"Base year 2022 expense stop; pro rata 12.50% (18,750 / 150,000)\\\",\\\"**Yes** \\\\u2014 controllable expenses capped at 5% p.a. compounding; gross-up to 95% occupancy\\\",\\\"4% of Building gross revenues\\\",\\\"Annual, 30 days' notice; >5% overcharge: landlord pays audit\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"NNN + percentage rent\\\",\\\"Pro rata 7.10% (4,400 / 62,000)\\\",\\\"None; capex excluded except law-required/reducing, amortised\\\",\\\"4% of gross rental revenue (CAM)\\\",\\\"Annual, 30 days' notice\\\"],\\n [\\\"GSA\\\",\\\"Government full service\\\",\\\"Base year 2021; increases above base year only; pro rata 15,000 / Building RSF (**not stated**)\\\",\\\"None\\\",\\\"Not capped in the lease\\\",\\\"Annual, 90 days; Government may audit during term and for 3 years after\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Lease\\\",\\\"Structure\\\",\\\"Recovery share\\\",\\\"Cap on recoveries\\\",\\\"Management fee\\\",\\\"Reconciliation and audit\\\"], rows,\\n          [0.72,1.02,1.62,1.55,1.02,1.77], size=7.4, head_size=7.3, keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"Denominators: the Apex, Verdana and Pint & Platter leases state the building or centre area, so their shares were verified. The Soto, BrightPath, Southeastern and GSA leases do not state the denominator. Verdana's lease states the building area as approximately 150,000 RSF; applying that figure to the GSA lease (same building) would give the Government a 10.00% share, but the GSA lease itself does not fix the percentage.\\\")\\nbox(doc, \\\"Observation \\\\u2014 two base years in one building\\\",\\n    [\\\"The Verdana lease uses **calendar year 2022** as its expense stop and the GSA lease (same building) uses **calendar year 2021**. Two tenants in Concord Office Tower therefore reimburse operating expense increases on different bases, and Verdana's recoveries benefit from an additional cap that GSA does not have. Galleon will need both base-year expense statements to reconcile 2025 recoveries, and should obtain the certified 2021 statement that the GSA lease required the Lessor to deliver by March 31, 2022 (Exhibit C).\\\"],\\n    fill=BOX, size=8.8)\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"3.4  Credit support\\\")\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"23.7%\\\",\\\"None\\\",\\\"No deposit, no guaranty, no letter of credit in the lease\\\",\\\"R-21\\\"],\\n [\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto\\\",\\\"4.1%\\\",\\\"Personal guaranty\\\",\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto, individually \\\\u2014 payment and performance, not merely collection; survives amendments; runs through any renewal term (to 10/31/2033)\\\",\\\"\\\"],\\n [\\\"BrightPath\\\",\\\"6.4%\\\",\\\"Security deposit $25,440\\\",\\\"Described as \\\\u201ctwo (2) months of Base Rent\\\\u201d \\\\u2014 but two months of current rent is $25,036.67; amount to be confirmed and transferred\\\",\\\"R-15\\\"],\\n [\\\"Southeastern\\\",\\\"13.0%\\\",\\\"None\\\",\\\"No deposit, no guaranty; at-will holdover\\\",\\\"R-21\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"28.8%\\\",\\\"None\\\",\\\"Lease states \\\\u201cSecurity Deposit: None\\\\u201d\\\",\\\"R-21\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"3.8%\\\",\\\"Deposit $19,800 + personal guaranty\\\",\\\"Deposit equals three months of Lease Year 1 rent (verified). Guaranty by Lance Whitford **burns off at the earlier of 9/30/2025 or $2,000,000 trailing-12-month gross sales**\\\",\\\"R-21\\\"],\\n [\\\"United States (GSA)\\\",\\\"20.1%\\\",\\\"None required\\\",\\\"Government self-insured; full faith and credit of the United States\\\",\\\"\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Lease\\\",\\\"% of rent\\\",\\\"Instrument\\\",\\\"Terms and verification\\\",\\\"Risk\\\"], rows, [1.05,0.6,1.25,3.25,0.55],\\n          size=7.9, head_size=7.6, align_center_cols=(1,4), keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"Two deposits are held and both should be dealt with as closing prorations: either transferred to Galleon with a Seller credit, or credited to Galleon against the purchase price. The Pint & Platter guaranty may already have burned off; Seller should provide the certified gross sales reports and any release executed under Exhibit D \\\\u00a7 2.\\\")\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"3.5  Consents, estoppels and non-disturbance\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"The lease documents give Galleon limited ability to compel the documentation a purchaser or lender will require. The position is summarised below and the required certifications are set out in Section 9.\\\", size=9.8)\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"**Yes** \\\\u2014 within 10 business days of request (\\\\u00a7 17.1)\\\",\\\"Yes \\\\u2014 failure to deliver is an irrevocable acknowledgment of the landlord's form (\\\\u00a7 17.2)\\\",\\\"Self-operative subordination; **no non-disturbance obligation**; failure to execute attornment documents is a default (\\\\u00a7 8.4)\\\",\\\"None on file\\\"],\\n [\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto\\\",\\\"No estoppel provision in the lease\\\",\\\"\\\\u2014\\\",\\\"Landlord to use \\\\u201ccommercially reasonable efforts\\\\u201d to obtain SNDA within 60 days of commencement (\\\\u00a7 12.1)\\\",\\\"None on file\\\"],\\n [\\\"BrightPath\\\",\\\"No estoppel provision in the lease\\\",\\\"\\\\u2014\\\",\\\"Landlord to use commercially reasonable efforts; deliver to tenant within 30 days of request (Art. 17)\\\",\\\"None on file\\\"],\\n [\\\"Southeastern\\\",\\\"No estoppel provision in the lease\\\",\\\"\\\\u2014\\\",\\\"Self-operative subordination; **no non-disturbance**; tenant appoints Landlord attorney-in-fact to sign (Art. 16)\\\",\\\"None on file\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"**Yes** \\\\u2014 within 15 business days (Art. XXIV)\\\",\\\"Yes \\\\u2014 deemed acknowledgment applies to either party\\\",\\\"Subordination expressly conditioned on a commercially reasonable SNDA (17.01); landlord represented no mortgage on the building as at 2/28/2022 (17.02)\\\",\\\"None on file\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"No estoppel provision in the lease\\\",\\\"\\\\u2014\\\",\\\"Landlord to use commercially reasonable efforts (Art. 12)\\\",\\\"None on file\\\"],\\n [\\\"United States (GSA)\\\",\\\"No estoppel provision; certificates of lease status are arranged through the Contracting Officer\\\",\\\"\\\\u2014\\\",\\\"**Lease is senior** \\\\u2014 not subordinate to any mortgage; lessor may not grant a priority mortgage without consent; SNDA only if the Government requests (Art. 16)\\\",\\\"Not applicable\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Lease\\\",\\\"Tenant estoppel obligation\\\",\\\"Deemed acknowledgment\\\",\\\"Subordination / SNDA posture\\\",\\\"SNDA on file\\\"], rows,\\n          [0.88,1.5,1.32,2.3,0.7], size=7.4, head_size=7.3, keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"Consequence: for five of the seven leases Galleon has no contractual right to an estoppel at all, and for none of the seven is there a non-disturbance agreement in place. The PSA should therefore carry an express estoppel condition covering each tenant, and the lender's SNDA requirements should be tested against the Apex, Southeastern and GSA provisions before the financing commitment is finalised.\\\")\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"3.6  Option and notice deadlines\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"The following dates are computed from the operative notice provisions. Dates marked \\\\u200b\\\\u201copen now\\\\u201d have already begun to run and require immediate attention.\\\", size=9.8)\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"ROFR over Building C\\\",\\\"30 days from delivery of a ROFR Notice\\\",\\\"On any triggering offer \\\\u2014 **may have been triggered by the PSA (15 Nov 2024)**\\\",\\\"R-01\\\"],\\n [\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"Renewal option 1 / option 2\\\",\\\"12 months before expiry\\\",\\\"31 May 2028  /  31 May 2033\\\",\\\"R-18\\\"],\\n [\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto\\\",\\\"Early termination notice\\\",\\\"6 months before effective date\\\",\\\"**30 April 2025** \\\\u2014 46 days after target closing\\\",\\\"R-05\\\"],\\n [\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto\\\",\\\"Renewal option\\\",\\\"9 months before expiry\\\",\\\"31 January 2028\\\",\\\"\\\"],\\n [\\\"BrightPath\\\",\\\"Renewal option 1\\\",\\\"12 months before expiry\\\",\\\"31 March 2031\\\",\\\"\\\"],\\n [\\\"Southeastern\\\",\\\"Renewal option\\\",\\\"90 days before expiry\\\",\\\"**Lapsed** \\\\u2014 1 April 2024; no renewal right remains\\\",\\\"R-04\\\"],\\n [\\\"Southeastern\\\",\\\"Termination of holdover\\\",\\\"30 days' notice\\\",\\\"Either party, at any time\\\",\\\"R-04\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"Expansion option (9th floor)\\\",\\\"6 months before desired commencement\\\",\\\"Window **1 July 2024 \\\\u2013 30 June 2027 \\\\u2014 open now**\\\",\\\"R-06\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"Contraction notice\\\",\\\"9 months before contraction date\\\",\\\"First available 1 July 2027 (earliest contraction 1 April 2028)\\\",\\\"R-17\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"Renewal option 1\\\",\\\"12 months before expiry\\\",\\\"30 June 2031\\\",\\\"\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"Co-tenancy right\\\",\\\"Rolling \\\\u2014 180 consecutive days below 70%\\\",\\\"**Status unknown \\\\u2014 may already be running**\\\",\\\"R-07\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"Renewal option 1\\\",\\\"9 months before expiry\\\",\\\"31 December 2029\\\",\\\"\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"Guaranty burn-off\\\",\\\"Earlier of fixed date or sales test\\\",\\\"**30 September 2025** or $2,000,000 trailing-12-month sales\\\",\\\"R-21\\\"],\\n [\\\"United States (GSA)\\\",\\\"Firm term expiry\\\",\\\"\\\\u2014\\\",\\\"**31 December 2025**\\\",\\\"R-03\\\"],\\n [\\\"United States (GSA)\\\",\\\"Government termination (soft term)\\\",\\\"120 calendar days' notice\\\",\\\"Any time after 31 December 2025\\\",\\\"R-03\\\"],\\n [\\\"All\\\",\\\"Estoppel delivery\\\",\\\"10 business days (Apex); 15 business days (Verdana)\\\",\\\"On Galleon's request \\\\u2014 action now\\\",\\\"R-09\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Lease\\\",\\\"Right or obligation\\\",\\\"Notice period\\\",\\\"Key date\\\",\\\"Risk\\\"], rows, [0.85,1.55,1.5,2.25,0.55],\\n          size=7.6, head_size=7.4, align_center_cols=(4,), keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"Deadlines recomputed from each lease's operative clause and cross-checked against the expiry date. The Rent Roll does not state any option or notice deadline other than the Southeastern lapse; the Soto early termination deadline of 30 April 2025 is the most time-critical omission because it falls within seven weeks of the target closing date (Risk R-09).\\\")\\nPYEOF\\necho ok\"}", "result": "ok\n"}
{"turn": 25, "role": "assistant", "text": "Now the core: the seven twelve-category lease abstractions.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_TLrfv6xBvldYWII5DImO4664", "name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && cat >> work/build.py <<'PYEOF'\\n\\n# ================= 4. LEASE ABSTRACTIONS =================\\ndef snapshot(doc, pairs):\\n    rows = []\\n    for i in range(0, len(pairs), 2):\\n        a = pairs[i]; b = pairs[i+1] if i+1 < len(pairs) else (\\\"\\\",\\\"\\\")\\n        rows.append([a[0], a[1], b[0], b[1]])\\n    t = doc.add_table(rows=0, cols=4)\\n    set_borders(t, sz=4, color=\\\"BFC5CE\\\"); set_cell_margins(t, 45, 45, 80, 80)\\n    for r in rows:\\n        row = t.add_row(); cant_split(row)\\n        write_cell(row.cells[0], r[0], size=7.6, bold=True, color=NAVY); shade(row.cells[0], \\\"EDF0F4\\\")\\n        write_cell(row.cells[1], r[1], size=8.0)\\n        write_cell(row.cells[2], r[2], size=7.6, bold=True, color=NAVY); shade(row.cells[2], \\\"EDF0F4\\\")\\n        write_cell(row.cells[3], r[3], size=8.0)\\n    set_widths(t, [1.12, 2.23, 1.12, 2.23])\\n    doc.add_paragraph().paragraph_format.space_after = Pt(1)\\n\\ndef abstraction(doc, cats, notes=None, risk_line=None):\\n    t = doc.add_table(rows=0, cols=2)\\n    set_borders(t, sz=4, color=\\\"BFC5CE\\\"); set_cell_margins(t, 55, 55, 85, 85)\\n    for i,(cat,txt) in enumerate(cats):\\n        row = t.add_row()\\n        write_cell(row.cells[0], cat, size=7.9, bold=True, color=NAVY)\\n        shade(row.cells[0], \\\"EDF0F4\\\")\\n        write_cell(row.cells[1], txt, size=8.2)\\n        if i % 2 == 1: shade(row.cells[1], \\\"FAFBFC\\\")\\n    set_widths(t, [1.28, 5.42])\\n    doc.add_paragraph().paragraph_format.space_after = Pt(1)\\n    if notes:\\n        p = doc.add_paragraph(); pf = p.paragraph_format\\n        pf.space_before = Pt(4); pf.space_after = Pt(2); pf.keep_with_next = True\\n        r = p.add_run(\\\"Verification and drafting notes\\\"); r.bold=True; r.font.size=Pt(8.3); r.font.color.rgb = ACCENT; r.font.name=\\\"Calibri\\\"\\n        for n in notes:\\n            pp = doc.add_paragraph(); pf = pp.paragraph_format\\n            pf.left_indent = Inches(0.2); pf.first_line_indent = Inches(-0.13)\\n            pf.space_after = Pt(1.5); pf.line_spacing = 1.04\\n            r = pp.add_run(\\\"\\\\u2013 \\\"); r.font.size=Pt(8); r.font.color.rgb = LGREY\\n            for k,part in enumerate(n.split(\\\"**\\\")):\\n                if not part: continue\\n                rr = pp.add_run(part); rr.font.size=Pt(8); rr.font.name=\\\"Calibri\\\"; rr.bold=(k%2==1)\\n    if risk_line:\\n        p = doc.add_paragraph(); pf = p.paragraph_format\\n        pf.space_before = Pt(5); pf.space_after = Pt(8)\\n        r = p.add_run(\\\"Risk flags: \\\"); r.bold=True; r.font.size=Pt(8.3); r.font.color.rgb = ACCENT; r.font.name=\\\"Calibri\\\"\\n        r = p.add_run(risk_line); r.font.size=Pt(8.3); r.font.name=\\\"Calibri\\\"\\n\\nh1(doc, \\\"SECTION 4\\\", \\\"Lease Abstractions\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"Each lease is abstracted below in the twelve categories required by Section 2(e) of the Engagement Letter. Category (12), Risk Flags, cross-refers to the numbered entries in the Risk Register at Section 7, where each item is rated and an action is assigned. Figures are verified as described in Section 6; verification notes specific to each lease follow its abstraction table.\\\", size=9.8)\\n\\n# ---------- 4.1 APEX ----------\\nh2(doc, \\\"4.1  Apex Fulfillment Services Inc. \\\\u2014 Thornfield Distribution Center, Building C\\\")\\nsnapshot(doc, [\\n (\\\"Tenant\\\",\\\"Apex Fulfillment Services Inc., a Delaware corporation\\\"),\\n (\\\"Premises\\\",\\\"Building C (entire), 87,500 RSF warehouse / distribution\\\"),\\n (\\\"Landlord\\\",\\\"Thornfield Realty Holdings LP\\\"),\\n (\\\"Property\\\",\\\"4200 Logistics Parkway, Charlotte, Mecklenburg Co., NC 28214\\\"),\\n (\\\"Lease date\\\",\\\"March 1, 2019\\\"),\\n (\\\"Source\\\",\\\"D3 \\\\u2014 Lease Agreement dated March 1, 2019\\\"),\\n (\\\"Current annual rent\\\",\\\"$557,375.00  ($46,447.92 / month)\\\"),\\n (\\\"Share of portfolio\\\",\\\"23.7%\\\"),\\n])\\nabstraction(doc, [\\n (\\\"(1) Tenant and premises\\\",\\n  \\\"Apex Fulfillment Services Inc., a Delaware corporation, qualified to do business in North Carolina, whose principal office is the leased premises. Premises are the entirety of **Building C**, approximately **87,500 RSF** of warehouse and distribution space, in Thornfield Distribution Center, a three-building park of approximately 240,000 RSF on approximately 25 acres. Building C includes 12 dock-high doors, 2 drive-in doors and approximately 50 adjacent surface spaces including tractor-trailer staging. Tenant's pro rata share is **36.46%** (87,500 \\\\u00f7 240,000) and adjusts on remeasurement or addition/demolition. Permitted use: third-party logistics, fulfillment, distribution and warehousing, with ancillary office.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(2) Term\\\",\\n  \\\"Lease Date 1 March 2019; Commencement **1 June 2019**; Expiration **31 May 2029**; ten Lease Years measured from the Commencement Date. Pre-commencement period 1 March \\\\u2013 31 May 2019 during which tenant had access to build out with no Base Rent payable. If the first renewal option is exercised, the Renewal Term runs 1 June 2029 \\\\u2013 31 May 2034; the second, 1 June 2034 \\\\u2013 31 May 2039.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(3) Rent\\\",\\n  \\\"Year 1: **$5.500/RSF** = $481,250.00 per annum ($40,104.17 per month). Escalation **3% per annum compounded annually**, each year's rate derived from the prior year and rounded to the nearest $0.001/RSF. Current Lease Year 6 (1 June 2024 \\\\u2013 31 May 2025): **$6.370/RSF = $557,375.00 per annum ($46,447.92 per month)**. Year 10: $7.170/RSF = $627,375.00. Late fee 5% after 5 business days; default interest 1.5% per month. No free rent after commencement.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(4) Lease type\\\",\\n  \\\"**Triple net (NNN)** \\\\u2014 Article V. Base Rent is in addition to all Operating Expenses.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(5) Operating expenses\\\",\\n  \\\"Tenant pays its 36.46% pro rata share of all Operating Expenses (taxes, insurance, CAM, utilities, landscaping, security, management fees and capital reserves). Management fee capped at 5% of gross rental revenues collected from the Property. **No cap, ceiling or limitation** on year-over-year increases \\\\u2014 \\\\u00a7 5.3 states this expressly. Estimated monthly payments with a 120-day annual reconciliation. Audit right once per calendar year on 30 days' notice; if the audit shows an overcharge exceeding 5%, Landlord bears the audit cost.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(6) Renewal options\\\",\\n  \\\"**Two consecutive five-year options** at **95% of fair market rent**. Notice **not less than 12 months** before the then-current Expiration Date \\\\u2014 first option by **31 May 2028**, second by **31 May 2033**. Time is of the essence; failure to give timely notice causes the applicable option **and all subsequent options** to lapse irrevocably. Options are personal to Apex, non-assignable to any assignee or subtenant, and conditional on no default and on occupancy. FMR by agreement, failing which a three-appraiser process with the FMR set at the average of the two closest appraisals.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(7) Termination rights\\\",\\n  \\\"**None in favour of the tenant** \\\\u2014 there is no early termination right. Landlord may terminate on default (Article XV), with damages including the present value (at 6%) of the rent differential and recapture of unamortised TI. Holdover is month-to-month at **150%** of final rent (Article XIV). **The lease contains no casualty or condemnation article**: there is no express rent abatement on damage or taking, no repair obligation and no termination right on destruction, so those matters would fall back on North Carolina law.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(8) Assignment and subletting\\\",\\n  \\\"Landlord's prior written consent required, **not to be unreasonably withheld** (\\\\u00a7 7.1). **Affiliate transfers permitted without consent** (50%+ voting control), on 10 business days' notice and written assumption (\\\\u00a7 7.2). **No release of tenant** on any assignment \\\\u2014 Apex remains jointly and severally liable (\\\\u00a7 7.3). No landlord recapture right and no profit-sharing on assignment.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(9) Security deposit / guaranty\\\",\\n  \\\"**None.** The lease provides for no security deposit, no letter of credit and no guaranty. Galleon's credit exposure to Apex (23.7% of aggregate rent) is entirely unsecured by any lease instrument.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(10) Tenant improvements\\\",\\n  \\\"TI Allowance **$15.00/RSF = $1,312,500.00** (Exhibit C), disbursed in up to three draws against paid invoices, architect's certificate and lien waivers. Amortised straight-line at $131,250.00 per Lease Year. Recapture of the unamortised balance applied only on a default before the end of Lease Year 5 and **terminated automatically on 31 May 2024** \\\\u2014 there is no current recapture exposure. Improvements become Landlord's property on installation and are removable only at Landlord's direction.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(11) Special provisions\\\",\\n  \\\"**Exclusive use (\\\\u00a7 6.2):** Landlord may not lease, permit or suffer any space in **Buildings A, B or C** to be used for fulfillment, logistics, distribution or warehousing by anyone other than Apex, binding on successors and assigns. **Right of first refusal to purchase Building C (Article XIII):** triggered by any bona fide third-party offer, **expressly including a multi-property or portfolio transaction in which Building C is included**; Landlord must deliver a ROFR Notice before accepting or executing any agreement; tenant has 30 days to elect; the allocable price in a portfolio deal is set by Landlord in good faith and may be disputed before an MAI appraiser; the ROFR reinstates if Landlord does not close within 180 days or improves the terms. Personal to Apex; a memorandum may be recorded (\\\\u00a7 13.8). **Parking:** minimum 50 spaces, no charge during the initial term; prevailing rates permitted in a Renewal Term. **Estoppel:** 10 business days, with deemed acknowledgment (\\\\u00a7 17.2). **Subordination:** self-operative, with no non-disturbance obligation; failure to deliver attornment documents within 10 business days is an Event of Default (\\\\u00a7 8.4). Governing law: North Carolina.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(12) Risk flags\\\",\\n  \\\"**R-01** ROFR may have been triggered by this transaction (critical). **R-08** exclusive use across Buildings A, B and C. **R-18** renewal options lapse together if the first notice is missed. **R-20** Year 5 rate in Exhibit B inconsistent with the stated 3% escalation. **R-10** self-operative subordination with no non-disturbance. **R-21** no credit support for 23.7% of aggregate rent. **R-24** no casualty or condemnation provisions.\\\"),\\n], notes=[\\n \\\"Exhibit B Year 5 is stated as **$6.180/RSF**. Applying the lease's own 3% compounding formula to the Year 4 rate of $6.010 gives **$6.190**. The schedule appears to have been built from the erroneous Year 5 figure, so Years 6 to 10 are each approximately $0.006/RSF low. Current-year understatement: $557,900.65 \\\\u2212 $557,375.00 = **$525.65**; cumulative over the term $3,616.92. Immaterial in amount, but it confirms that Exhibit B was not generated from the operative formula.\\\",\\n \\\"Pro rata share recomputed: 87,500 \\\\u00f7 240,000 = 36.4583%, stated as 36.46% \\\\u2014 correct.\\\",\\n \\\"TI allowance and amortisation recomputed: 87,500 \\\\u00d7 $15.00 = $1,312,500.00; \\\\u00f7 10 = $131,250.00 \\\\u2014 correct.\\\",\\n \\\"Exhibit B is described as rounded \\\\u201cto the nearest dollar for annual and monthly figures\\\\u201d, but every amount is stated to the cent. Cosmetic only.\\\",\\n \\\"The lease contains no casualty or condemnation article, and no estoppel-related obligation on the Landlord. The absence of a casualty article is unusual for an NNN industrial lease of this size and should be raised with Seller as a document-completeness point.\\\",\\n],\\nrisk_line=\\\"R-01 (critical), R-08, R-10, R-18, R-20, R-21, R-24.\\\")\\nPYEOF\\necho ok\"}"}], "input_tokens": 176168, "output_tokens": 3526, "finish_reason": "completed"}
