0%+ voting control), on 10 business days' notice and written assumption (\\\\u00a7 7.2). **No release of tenant** on any assignment \\\\u2014 Apex remains jointly and severally liable (\\\\u00a7 7.3). No landlord recapture right and no profit-sharing on assignment.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(9) Security deposit / guaranty\\\",\\n  \\\"**None.** The lease provides for no security deposit, no letter of credit and no guaranty. Galleon's credit exposure to Apex (23.7% of aggregate rent) is entirely unsecured by any lease instrument.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(10) Tenant improvements\\\",\\n  \\\"TI Allowance **$15.00/RSF = $1,312,500.00** (Exhibit C), disbursed in up to three draws against paid invoices, architect's certificate and lien waivers. Amortised straight-line at $131,250.00 per Lease Year. Recapture of the unamortised balance applied only on a default before the end of Lease Year 5 and **terminated automatically on 31 May 2024** \\\\u2014 there is no current recapture exposure. Improvements become Landlord's property on installation and are removable only at Landlord's direction.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(11) Special provisions\\\",\\n  \\\"**Exclusive use (\\\\u00a7 6.2):** Landlord may not lease, permit or suffer any space in **Buildings A, B or C** to be used for fulfillment, logistics, distribution or warehousing by anyone other than Apex, binding on successors and assigns. **Right of first refusal to purchase Building C (Article XIII):** triggered by any bona fide third-party offer, **expressly including a multi-property or portfolio transaction in which Building C is included**; Landlord must deliver a ROFR Notice before accepting or executing any agreement; tenant has 30 days to elect; the allocable price in a portfolio deal is set by Landlord in good faith and may be disputed before an MAI appraiser; the ROFR reinstates if Landlord does not close within 180 days or improves the terms. Personal to Apex; a memorandum may be recorded (\\\\u00a7 13.8). **Parking:** minimum 50 spaces, no charge during the initial term; prevailing rates permitted in a Renewal Term. **Estoppel:** 10 business days, with deemed acknowledgment (\\\\u00a7 17.2). **Subordination:** self-operative, with no non-disturbance obligation; failure to deliver attornment documents within 10 business days is an Event of Default (\\\\u00a7 8.4). Governing law: North Carolina.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(12) Risk flags\\\",\\n  \\\"**R-01** ROFR may have been triggered by this transaction (critical). **R-08** exclusive use across Buildings A, B and C. **R-18** renewal options lapse together if the first notice is missed. **R-20** Year 5 rate in Exhibit B inconsistent with the stated 3% escalation. **R-10** self-operative subordination with no non-disturbance. **R-21** no credit support for 23.7% of aggregate rent. **R-24** no casualty or condemnation provisions.\\\"),\\n], notes=[\\n \\\"Exhibit B Year 5 is stated as **$6.180/RSF**. Applying the lease's own 3% compounding formula to the Year 4 rate of $6.010 gives **$6.190**. The schedule appears to have been built from the erroneous Year 5 figure, so Years 6 to 10 are each approximately $0.006/RSF low. Current-year understatement: $557,900.65 \\\\u2212 $557,375.00 = **$525.65**; cumulative over the term $3,616.92. Immaterial in amount, but it confirms that Exhibit B was not generated from the operative formula.\\\",\\n \\\"Pro rata share recomputed: 87,500 \\\\u00f7 240,000 = 36.4583%, stated as 36.46% \\\\u2014 correct.\\\",\\n \\\"TI allowance and amortisation recomputed: 87,500 \\\\u00d7 $15.00 = $1,312,500.00; \\\\u00f7 10 = $131,250.00 \\\\u2014 correct.\\\",\\n \\\"Exhibit B is described as rounded \\\\u201cto the nearest dollar for annual and monthly figures\\\\u201d, but every amount is stated to the cent. Cosmetic only.\\\",\\n \\\"The lease contains no casualty or condemnation article, and no estoppel-related obligation on the Landlord. The absence of a casualty article is unusual for an NNN industrial lease of this size and should be raised with Seller as a document-completeness point.\\\",\\n],\\nrisk_line=\\\"R-01 (critical), R-08, R-10, R-18, R-20, R-21, R-24.\\\")\\nPYEOF\\necho ok\"}", "result": "ok\n"}
{"turn": 26, "role": "assistant", "text": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_ET_Ns6fPBebKSMKnaT7oCpW8976", "name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && cat >> work/build.py <<'PYEOF'\\n\\n# ---------- 4.2 SOTO ----------\\nh2(doc, \\\"4.2  Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS, PA \\\\u2014 Millbrook Medical Plaza, Suite 200\\\")\\nsnapshot(doc, [\\n (\\\"Tenant\\\",\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS, PA, a North Carolina professional association\\\"),\\n (\\\"Premises\\\",\\\"Suite 200, 2nd floor, 3,200 RSF medical / dental office\\\"),\\n (\\\"Landlord\\\",\\\"Thornfield Realty Holdings LP\\\"),\\n (\\\"Property\\\",\\\"1585 Millbrook Road, Raleigh, Wake Co., NC 27609\\\"),\\n (\\\"Lease date\\\",\\\"September 15, 2021\\\"),\\n (\\\"Source\\\",\\\"D4 \\\\u2014 Medical Office Lease Agreement dated September 15, 2021\\\"),\\n (\\\"Current annual rent\\\",\\\"$96,800.00  ($8,066.67 / month)\\\"),\\n (\\\"Share of portfolio\\\",\\\"4.1%\\\"),\\n])\\nabstraction(doc, [\\n (\\\"(1) Tenant and premises\\\",\\n  \\\"Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS, PA, a North Carolina professional association. **Suite 200**, second floor, approximately **3,200 RSF** of medical and dental office space in Millbrook Medical Plaza. Measured under **BOMA Z65.1-2017**, and the measurement is stated to be conclusive and binding for all purposes including Base Rent, the TI allowance and the pro rata share (\\\\u00a7 2.2). Pro rata share is 3,200 divided by the total RSF of the Building \\\\u2014 **the Building area is not stated**. Parking: 12 dedicated garage spaces at no charge during the initial term (3.75 per 1,000 RSF). Permitted use is medical and dental office only, with detailed biohazardous waste obligations (\\\\u00a7 5.2).\\\"),\\n (\\\"(2) Term\\\",\\n  \\\"Lease Date 15 September 2021; Commencement **1 November 2021**; Expiration **31 October 2028**; **seven Lease Years**. Renewal Term, if exercised, 1 November 2028 \\\\u2013 31 October 2033. If Landlord fails to deliver possession on time, rent abates per diem but the Expiration Date is **not** extended and Landlord is not liable for damages (\\\\u00a7 3.2).\\\"),\\n (\\\"(3) Rent\\\",\\n  \\\"Year 1: **$28.00/RSF** = $89,600.00 per annum ($7,466.67 per month). Escalation is a **fixed increase of $0.75 per RSF per year** (not compounding, not CPI). Current Lease Year 4 (1 November 2024 \\\\u2013 31 October 2025): **$30.25/RSF = $96,800.00 per annum ($8,066.67 per month)**. Year 7: $32.50/RSF = $104,000.00. Late charge 5%; interest at the lesser of 12% per annum or the legal maximum on amounts unpaid after 30 days.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(4) Lease type\\\",\\n  \\\"**Modified gross with a Base Year 2022 expense stop** \\\\u2014 \\\\u00a7 1.2 and \\\\u00a7 4.2.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(5) Operating expenses\\\",\\n  \\\"Landlord pays all Operating Expenses and Real Estate Taxes attributable to the Building for the **Base Year (calendar 2022)**. From calendar 2023 the tenant pays, as Additional Rent, its proportionate share of the **increase** over 2022 actuals, by monthly estimate with a 120-day annual statement. Operating Expenses exclude capital (except as amortised under GAAP), leasing commissions, tenant-specific improvements and depreciation. Management fee is \\\\u201cnot to exceed a market-rate percentage\\\\u201d \\\\u2014 **no figure is given**. No cap on escalations. Tenant audit right, exercisable within 12 months of the annual statement; unlike the other commercial leases, there is no overcharge cost-shift in the tenant's favour.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(6) Renewal options\\\",\\n  \\\"**One** five-year option at **fair market rent \\\\u201cas reasonably determined by Landlord\\\\u201d**, with a three-appraiser arbitration fallback (average of the two closest). Notice **by 31 January 2028** (nine months before expiry); time of the essence. No further options. There is **no floor** and no reference to the final-year rent, so the Landlord's determination governs subject only to the arbitration right.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(7) Termination rights\\\",\\n  \\\"**Tenant early termination effective 31 October 2025** (end of Lease Year 4) on satisfaction of three conditions (\\\\u00a7 20.1): (a) written notice by **30 April 2025** (six months, time of the essence); (b) payment of a termination fee of **$40,657.14**, simultaneously with the notice \\\\u2014 comprising unamortised TI of $16,457.14 plus three months' Base Rent of $24,200.00; and (c) surrender under Article 17. Failure to deliver both notice and full payment renders the notice void. Landlord may terminate on default (Article 16), with damages discounted at 8%. Holdover **150%** of final rent, month-to-month. Casualty: if repair is estimated to exceed 180 days either party may terminate; if damage exceeds 50% of replacement cost Landlord may terminate regardless; rent abates proportionately. Condemnation: either party may terminate on a material taking; the award belongs to Landlord, with a separate claim available to the tenant for personal property, dental equipment, relocation and its own TI excess.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(8) Assignment and subletting\\\",\\n  \\\"Landlord's prior written consent required, **not to be unreasonably withheld, conditioned or delayed** (\\\\u00a7 11.1). Conditions: 30 days' prior notice, three years' financial statements, full copy of the proposed instrument, and evidence that the assignee is licensed and qualified to practise in North Carolina and will use the premises only for the Permitted Use. **No release** absent an express written release. Tenant reimburses Landlord's review costs including legal fees. Unconsented transfer is void **and an Event of Default**. No recapture right; no profit share.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(9) Security deposit / guaranty\\\",\\n  \\\"**No security deposit** (\\\\u201cSecurity Deposit: N/A\\\\u201d). Instead, a **continuing personal guaranty from Dr. Miriam Soto, individually** (Article 21): unconditional and irrevocable, a guaranty of payment and performance and not merely of collection, enforceable directly without first pursuing the tenant, and expressly unaffected by amendments, assignments, forbearance, release of the tenant or the tenant's bankruptcy. It runs throughout the initial term and **any Renewal Term, i.e. to 31 October 2033**.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(10) Tenant improvements\\\",\\n  \\\"TI Allowance **$12.00/RSF = $38,400.00**. Unused allowance is forfeited, not credited. Amortised straight-line over seven years at $5,485.71 per year, used only to compute the early-termination recapture. Improvements become Landlord's property on completion, other than trade fixtures, dental equipment and personal property. **No allowance in any Renewal Term.**\\\"),\\n (\\\"(11) Special provisions\\\",\\n  \\\"**Base Year 2022 falls inside the lease term** (commencement November 2021), so the tenant's recovery obligation starts from a base that already includes a full year of its own occupancy \\\\u2014 favourable to the tenant and a drag on recoveries. **Building area not stated**, so the recovery share cannot be verified. **SNDA:** Landlord to use commercially reasonable efforts to obtain an SNDA from any current or future mortgagee within 60 days of commencement or recording (\\\\u00a7 12.1) \\\\u2014 none on file. **Parking:** 12 dedicated spaces, no charge during the initial term. **Biohazard regime** with Landlord inspection and remediation rights (\\\\u00a7 5.2). Broker representation: \\\\u00a7 22.5 states that neither party dealt with a broker, which is inconsistent with Ridgeview Realty Brokers Inc. acting as listing broker on the other portfolio leases. Governing law: North Carolina, venue Wake County.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(12) Risk flags\\\",\\n  \\\"**R-05** early termination right with a 30 April 2025 notice deadline (high). **R-19** building area and therefore the recovery share cannot be verified. **R-09** no estoppel obligation in the lease. **R-10** SNDA only on commercially reasonable efforts. **R-26** Base Year 2022 falls within the term, depressing recoveries.\\\"),\\n], notes=[\\n \\\"Early-termination fee recomputed: $38,400.00 \\\\u00d7 3/7 = $16,457.14; $96,800.00 \\\\u00f7 12 \\\\u00d7 3 = $24,200.00; total **$40,657.14** \\\\u2014 agrees to the lease and to Exhibit D.\\\",\\n \\\"Rent schedule recomputed on a $0.75/RSF step: 28.00 / 28.75 / 29.50 / 30.25 / 31.00 / 31.75 / 32.50, all seven years agree, as do the annual amounts ($89,600 to $104,000) and monthly amounts.\\\",\\n \\\"Parking ratio recomputed: 3,200 \\\\u00d7 3.75 \\\\u00f7 1,000 = 12 spaces \\\\u2014 agrees.\\\",\\n \\\"**Deadline conflict to note:** the tenant's notice deadline of 30 April 2025 is 46 days after the target closing date of 15 March 2025, so Galleon inherits the right unexpired. The 2025 Lease Year base rent of $99,200.00 is also the rate used to compute the termination fee, which is only about five months' rent against three further years of term.\\\",\\n],\\nrisk_line=\\\"R-05 (high), R-09, R-10, R-19, R-26.\\\")\\n\\n# ---------- 4.3 BRIGHTPATH ----------\\nh2(doc, \\\"4.3  BrightPath Learning Centers LLC \\\\u2014 Millbrook Medical Plaza, Suite 100\\\")\\nsnapshot(doc, [\\n (\\\"Tenant\\\",\\\"BrightPath Learning Centers LLC, a North Carolina LLC\\\"),\\n (\\\"Premises\\\",\\\"Suite 100, ground floor, 5,800 RSF childcare facility\\\"),\\n (\\\"Landlord\\\",\\\"Thornfield Realty Holdings LP\\\"),\\n (\\\"Property\\\",\\\"1585 Millbrook Road, Raleigh, Wake Co., NC 27609\\\"),\\n (\\\"Lease date\\\",\\\"January 10, 2017\\\"),\\n (\\\"Source\\\",\\\"D5 \\\\u2014 Lease Agreement dated January 10, 2017\\\"),\\n (\\\"Current annual rent\\\",\\\"$150,220.00  ($12,518.33 / month)\\\"),\\n (\\\"Share of portfolio\\\",\\\"6.4%\\\"),\\n])\\nabstraction(doc, [\\n (\\\"(1) Tenant and premises\\\",\\n  \\\"BrightPath Learning Centers LLC, a North Carolina limited liability company. **Suite 100**, ground floor, approximately **5,800 RSF** childcare and early childhood education facility, with direct access to a ground-level courtyard and patio used as an outdoor play area. Measured under **BOMA 2010**, stipulated and expressly **not subject to remeasurement**. Pro rata share is 5,800 divided by total Building RSF \\\\u201cas reasonably determined by Landlord\\\\u201d, with Landlord to notify the share within 30 days of commencement \\\\u2014 **the Building area is not stated in the lease**. Permitted use: childcare, daycare and early childhood education, with licensing obligations to the NC Division of Child Development and Early Education.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(2) Term\\\",\\n  \\\"Lease Date 10 January 2017; Commencement **1 April 2017**; Expiration **31 March 2032**; **fifteen years**. Early access from 1 February 2017 for installation of fixtures and build-out, with no Base Rent or Additional Rent during that period. Three consecutive renewal terms of five years each, so the lease could run to 31 March 2047 if all options are exercised.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(3) Rent\\\",\\n  \\\"Year 1: **$22.00/RSF** = $127,600.00 per annum ($10,633.33 per month). Escalation **2.5% per annum compounded annually** on each anniversary of the Commencement Date. Current Lease Year 8 (1 April 2024 \\\\u2013 31 March 2025): **$25.90/RSF = $150,220.00 per annum ($12,518.33 per month)**. Year 15: $30.79/RSF = $178,582.00. Late charge 5%; interest 1.5% per month (18% per annum).\\\"),\\n (\\\"(4) Lease type\\\",\\n  \\\"**Triple net (NNN)** \\\\u2014 Article 5; tenant pays pro rata shares of Operating Expenses, Real Estate Taxes and Insurance Costs as Additional Rent.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(5) Operating expenses\\\",\\n  \\\"Tenant pays its pro rata share of Operating Expenses, Real Estate Taxes and Insurance Costs, by monthly estimate with a 90-day annual reconciliation statement and an audit right (commenced within 12 months). Excluded from Operating Expenses: capital expenditure (except law-mandated post-commencement capex, amortised over useful life with interest not exceeding 8%), leasing commissions, TI for other tenants, income and franchise taxes, depreciation, correction of original construction defects, and costs recovered from insurance, condemnation or other tenants. **Management fee capped at 5% of gross revenues from the Building.** Tax protest savings are credited through to the tenant. **No cap on controllable expenses.**\\\"),\\n (\\\"(6) Renewal options\\\",\\n  \\\"**Three consecutive five-year options** (to 2047). Notice **not less than 12 months** before expiry of the then-current term; failure to give timely notice waives that option **and all subsequent unexercised options**. Options are personal to BrightPath except in favour of a permitted affiliate. **First Renewal Term rent is the lesser of fair market rent and the Year 15 rent escalated at 3% per annum compounded** \\\\u2014 an effective cap in the tenant's favour. Second and Third Renewal Terms at fair market rent. FMR by agreement or a three-appraiser process using the average of the two closest appraisals; interim rent at the prior rate pending determination.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(7) Termination rights\\\",\\n  \\\"**No general early termination right for the tenant.** Landlord has a **recapture right** exercisable within 30 days of a request for consent to assign or sublet, which operates as a termination right in respect of the affected space (see category 8). Landlord may terminate on default (Article 16), including where the tenant's childcare licence is revoked, suspended or ineffective for more than 60 consecutive days. **Casualty:** Landlord to commence restoration within 60 days and complete within 180 days; if it determines restoration cannot be completed within 180 days, either party may terminate on 30 days' notice. Rent abates proportionately while untenantable. **Condemnation:** either party may terminate on a taking of 25% or more of the RSF; the award belongs to Landlord with a separate claim available to the tenant for trade fixtures, personal property, moving and business interruption. Holdover **150%**.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(8) Assignment and subletting\\\",\\n  \\\"Landlord's prior written consent required, on a reasonableness standard tied to the assignee's financial condition, creditworthiness, reputation, intended use and compatibility (\\\\u00a7 11.1). **Landlord recapture right:** within 30 days of receiving a complete request, Landlord may terminate the lease as to the proposed space (or the whole premises for an assignment) and re-let it to anyone on any terms with no liability to the tenant (\\\\u00a7 11.2). Conditions of consent include that the tenant remains primarily liable, 30 days' notice with audited financial statements, a business plan and references, and **payment to Landlord of 50% of any consideration above the rent payable under the lease**, net of the tenant's reasonable costs (\\\\u00a7 11.3(e)). **Affiliate transfers** permitted without consent on 15 days' notice, with assumption and continuing tenant liability (\\\\u00a7 11.4).\\\"),\\n (\\\"(9) Security deposit / guaranty\\\",\\n  \\\"**Security deposit of $25,440.00**, described in Article 1 and Article 6 as \\\\u201cequal to two (2) months of Base Rent\\\\u201d. Non-interest-bearing, need not be segregated, with a ten-day replenishment obligation and return within 30 days after expiry and surrender. **No guaranty.**\\\"),\\n (\\\"(10) Tenant improvements\\\",\\n  \\\"**No TI allowance** \\\\u2014 \\\\u201cTenant's Work shall be entirely self-funded by Tenant\\\\u201d (Exhibit D \\\\u00a7 3). Landlord delivers shell condition, including slab, exterior walls, MEP stubbed to the boundary, sprinklers and one ADA restroom. Improvements become Landlord's property except trade fixtures, personal property and movable equipment; Landlord may require removal of designated improvements on 60 days' notice before expiry, with restoration at the tenant's cost.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(11) Special provisions\\\",\\n  \\\"**Exclusive use (\\\\u00a7 7.2):** Landlord may not lease any space in Millbrook Medical Plaza for a childcare, daycare or early childhood education facility; the covenant runs with the property and binds successors; the tenant's remedy is injunctive relief plus actual damages. **Childcare licence revocation** for more than 60 consecutive days is an Event of Default (\\\\u00a7 16.1(e)). **Phase I ESA** prepared by Hanover Environmental Consultants Inc. dated 15 November 2016, with no RECs, CRECs or HRECs, and a Landlord representation of continued accuracy (\\\\u00a7 10.2). Access protocols coordinated with the on-site manager given the presence of children (\\\\u00a7 13). Outdoor play-area rights acknowledged (Exhibit C \\\\u00b6 8) and hours of operation 6:30 a.m. to 6:30 p.m. acknowledged. Governing law: North Carolina.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(12) Risk flags\\\",\\n  \\\"**R-13** Year 8 rate departs from the stated 2.5% escalation and the error propagates to the end of the term. **R-15** security deposit amount inconsistent with \\\\u201ctwo months of Base Rent\\\\u201d. **R-19** building area not stated. **R-09** no estoppel obligation in the lease. **R-16** landlord-favourable recapture and 50% profit share (not a risk to Galleon, noted for completeness).\\\"),\\n], notes=[\\n \\\"**Escalation integrity.** The Year 7 rate is $25.51. Applying 2.5% gives **$26.1477 \\\\u2192 $26.15** for Year 8, but Exhibit B states **$25.90**. The schedule then compounds from the erroneous figure ($25.90 \\\\u00d7 1.025 = $26.55, which is the stated Year 9 rate), so the shortfall carries through to Year 15 ($30.79 stated against $31.09 computed). Current-year understatement **$1,456.30**; cumulative over Years 8\\\\u201315 **$12,773.84**.\\\",\\n \\\"**Security deposit.** Two months of the current (Year 8) Base Rent is $150,220.00 \\\\u00f7 12 \\\\u00d7 2 = **$25,036.67**; two months of Year 1 rent would be $21,266.67. The stated $25,440.00 equals two months at $26.317/RSF, a rate that appears nowhere in the schedule. The amount held should be confirmed against the ledger and, if $25,440.00 is correct, treated as a closing proration.\\\",\\n \\\"Years 1 to 7 of the schedule agree with 2.5% compounding to the nearest cent; only Year 8 breaks the chain.\\\",\\n \\\"The document retains an unremoved Word field placeholder (\\\\u201cRight-click to update Table of Contents\\\\u201d) on the cover page \\\\u2014 an indicator that the lease was assembled from a template and that the remaining text should not be assumed to have been checked against a signed original.\\\",\\n],\\nrisk_line=\\\"R-13 (medium), R-15, R-19, R-09.\\\")\\nPYEOF\\necho ok\"}"}], "input_tokens": 179708, "output_tokens": 4570, "finish_reason": "completed"}
{"turn": 26, "role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call_00_ET_Ns6fPBebKSMKnaT7oCpW8976", "tool_name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && cat >> work/build.py <<'PYEOF'\\n\\n# ---------- 4.2 SOTO ----------\\nh2(doc, \\\"4.2  Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS, PA \\\\u2014 Millbrook Medical Plaza, Suite 200\\\")\\nsnapshot(doc, [\\n (\\\"Tenant\\\",\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS, PA, a North Carolina professional association\\\"),\\n (\\\"Premises\\\",\\\"Suite 200, 2nd floor, 3,200 RSF medical / dental office\\\"),\\n (\\\"Landlord\\\",\\\"Thornfield Realty Holdings LP\\\"),\\n (\\\"Property\\\",\\\"1585 Millbrook Road, Raleigh, Wake Co., NC 27609\\\"),\\n (\\\"Lease date\\\",\\\"September 15, 2021\\\"),\\n (\\\"Source\\\",\\\"D4 \\\\u2014 Medical Office Lease Agreement dated September 15, 2021\\\"),\\n (\\\"Current annual rent\\\",\\\"$96,800.00  ($8,066.67 / month)\\\"),\\n (\\\"Share of portfolio\\\",\\\"4.1%\\\"),\\n])\\nabstraction(doc, [\\n (\\\"(1) Tenant and premises\\\",\\n  \\\"Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS, PA, a North Carolina professional association. **Suite 200**, second floor, approximately **3,200 RSF** of medical and dental office space in Millbrook Medical Plaza. Measured under **BOMA Z65.1-2017**, and the measurement is stated to be conclusive and binding for all purposes including Base Rent, the TI allowance and the pro rata share (\\\\u00a7 2.2). Pro rata share is 3,200 divided by the total RSF of the Building \\\\u2014 **the Building area is not stated**. Parking: 12 dedicated garage spaces at no charge during the initial term (3.75 per 1,000 RSF). Permitted use is medical and dental office only, with detailed biohazardous waste obligations (\\\\u00a7 5.2).\\\"),\\n (\\\"(2) Term\\\",\\n  \\\"Lease Date 15 September 2021; Commencement **1 November 2021**; Expiration **31 October 2028**; **seven Lease Years**. Renewal Term, if exercised, 1 November 2028 \\\\u2013 31 October 2033. If Landlord fails to deliver possession on time, rent abates per diem but the Expiration Date is **not** extended and Landlord is not liable for damages (\\\\u00a7 3.2).\\\"),\\n (\\\"(3) Rent\\\",\\n  \\\"Year 1: **$28.00/RSF** = $89,600.00 per annum ($7,466.67 per month). Escalation is a **fixed increase of $0.75 per RSF per year** (not compounding, not CPI). Current Lease Year 4 (1 November 2024 \\\\u2013 31 October 2025): **$30.25/RSF = $96,800.00 per annum ($8,066.67 per month)**. Year 7: $32.50/RSF = $104,000.00. Late charge 5%; interest at the lesser of 12% per annum or the legal maximum on amounts unpaid after 30 days.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(4) Lease type\\\",\\n  \\\"**Modified gross with a Base Year 2022 expense stop** \\\\u2014 \\\\u00a7 1.2 and \\\\u00a7 4.2.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(5) Operating expenses\\\",\\n  \\\"Landlord pays all Operating Expenses and Real Estate Taxes attributable to the Building for the **Base Year (calendar 2022)**. From calendar 2023 the tenant pays, as Additional Rent, its proportionate share of the **increase** over 2022 actuals, by monthly estimate with a 120-day annual statement. Operating Expenses exclude capital (except as amortised under GAAP), leasing commissions, tenant-specific improvements and depreciation. Management fee is \\\\u201cnot to exceed a market-rate percentage\\\\u201d \\\\u2014 **no figure is given**. No cap on escalations. Tenant audit right, exercisable within 12 months of the annual statement; unlike the other commercial leases, there is no overcharge cost-shift in the tenant's favour.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(6) Renewal options\\\",\\n  \\\"**One** five-year option at **fair market rent \\\\u201cas reasonably determined by Landlord\\\\u201d**, with a three-appraiser arbitration fallback (average of the two closest). Notice **by 31 January 2028** (nine months before expiry); time of the essence. No further options. There is **no floor** and no reference to the final-year rent, so the Landlord's determination governs subject only to the arbitration right.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(7) Termination rights\\\",\\n  \\\"**Tenant early termination effective 31 October 2025** (end of Lease Year 4) on satisfaction of three conditions (\\\\u00a7 20.1): (a) written notice by **30 April 2025** (six months, time of the essence); (b) payment of a termination fee of **$40,657.14**, simultaneously with the notice \\\\u2014 comprising unamortised TI of $16,457.14 plus three months' Base Rent of $24,200.00; and (c) surrender under Article 17. Failure to deliver both notice and full payment renders the notice void. Landlord may terminate on default (Article 16), with damages discounted at 8%. Holdover **150%** of final rent, month-to-month. Casualty: if repair is estimated to exceed 180 days either party may terminate; if damage exceeds 50% of replacement cost Landlord may terminate regardless; rent abates proportionately. Condemnation: either party may terminate on a material taking; the award belongs to Landlord, with a separate claim available to the tenant for personal property, dental equipment, relocation and its own TI excess.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(8) Assignment and subletting\\\",\\n  \\\"Landlord's prior written consent required, **not to be unreasonably withheld, conditioned or delayed** (\\\\u00a7 11.1). Conditions: 30 days' prior notice, three years' financial statements, full copy of the proposed instrument, and evidence that the assignee is licensed and qualified to practise in North Carolina and will use the premises only for the Permitted Use. **No release** absent an express written release. Tenant reimburses Landlord's review costs including legal fees. Unconsented transfer is void **and an Event of Default**. No recapture right; no profit share.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(9) Security deposit / guaranty\\\",\\n  \\\"**No security deposit** (\\\\u201cSecurity Deposit: N/A\\\\u201d). Instead, a **continuing personal guaranty from Dr. Miriam Soto, individually** (Article 21): unconditional and irrevocable, a guaranty of payment and performance and not merely of collection, enforceable directly without first pursuing the tenant, and expressly unaffected by amendments, assignments, forbearance, release of the tenant or the tenant's bankruptcy. It runs throughout the initial term and **any Renewal Term, i.e. to 31 October 2033**.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(10) Tenant improvements\\\",\\n  \\\"TI Allowance **$12.00/RSF = $38,400.00**. Unused allowance is forfeited, not credited. Amortised straight-line over seven years at $5,485.71 per year, used only to compute the early-termination recapture. Improvements become Landlord's property on completion, other than trade fixtures, dental equipment and personal property. **No allowance in any Renewal Term.**\\\"),\\n (\\\"(11) Special provisions\\\",\\n  \\\"**Base Year 2022 falls inside the lease term** (commencement November 2021), so the tenant's recovery obligation starts from a base that already includes a full year of its own occupancy \\\\u2014 favourable to the tenant and a drag on recoveries. **Building area not stated**, so the recovery share cannot be verified. **SNDA:** Landlord to use commercially reasonable efforts to obtain an SNDA from any current or future mortgagee within 60 days of commencement or recording (\\\\u00a7 12.1) \\\\u2014 none on file. **Parking:** 12 dedicated spaces, no charge during the initial term. **Biohazard regime** with Landlord inspection and remediation rights (\\\\u00a7 5.2). Broker representation: \\\\u00a7 22.5 states that neither party dealt with a broker, which is inconsistent with Ridgeview Realty Brokers Inc. acting as listing broker on the other portfolio leases. Governing law: North Carolina, venue Wake County.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(12) Risk flags\\\",\\n  \\\"**R-05** early termination right with a 30 April 2025 notice deadline (high). **R-19** building area and therefore the recovery share cannot be verified. **R-09** no estoppel obligation in the lease. **R-10** SNDA only on commercially reasonable efforts. **R-26** Base Year 2022 falls within the term, depressing recoveries.\\\"),\\n], notes=[\\n \\\"Early-termination fee recomputed: $38,400.00 \\\\u00d7 3/7 = $16,457.14; $96,800.00 \\\\u00f7 12 \\\\u00d7 3 = $24,200.00; total **$40,657.14** \\\\u2014 agrees to the lease and to Exhibit D.\\\",\\n \\\"Rent schedule recomputed on a $0.75/RSF step: 28.00 / 28.75 / 29.50 / 30.25 / 31.00 / 31.75 / 32.50, all seven years agree, as do the annual amounts ($89,600 to $104,000) and monthly amounts.\\\",\\n \\\"Parking ratio recomputed: 3,200 \\\\u00d7 3.75 \\\\u00f7 1,000 = 12 spaces \\\\u2014 agrees.\\\",\\n \\\"**Deadline conflict to note:** the tenant's notice deadline of 30 April 2025 is 46 days after the target closing date of 15 March 2025, so Galleon inherits the right unexpired. The 2025 Lease Year base rent of $99,200.00 is also the rate used to compute the termination fee, which is only about five months' rent against three further years of term.\\\",\\n],\\nrisk_line=\\\"R-05 (high), R-09, R-10, R-19, R-26.\\\")\\n\\n# ---------- 4.3 BRIGHTPATH ----------\\nh2(doc, \\\"4.3  BrightPath Learning Centers LLC \\\\u2014 Millbrook Medical Plaza, Suite 100\\\")\\nsnapshot(doc, [\\n (\\\"Tenant\\\",\\\"BrightPath Learning Centers LLC, a North Carolina LLC\\\"),\\n (\\\"Premises\\\",\\\"Suite 100, ground floor, 5,800 RSF childcare facility\\\"),\\n (\\\"Landlord\\\",\\\"Thornfield Realty Holdings LP\\\"),\\n (\\\"Property\\\",\\\"1585 Millbrook Road, Raleigh, Wake Co., NC 27609\\\"),\\n (\\\"Lease date\\\",\\\"January 10, 2017\\\"),\\n (\\\"Source\\\",\\\"D5 \\\\u2014 Lease Agreement dated January 10, 2017\\\"),\\n (\\\"Current annual rent\\\",\\\"$150,220.00  ($12,518.33 / month)\\\"),\\n (\\\"Share of portfolio\\\",\\\"6.4%\\\"),\\n])\\nabstraction(doc, [\\n (\\\"(1) Tenant and premises\\\",\\n  \\\"BrightPath Learning Centers LLC, a North Carolina limited liability company. **Suite 100**, ground floor, approximately **5,800 RSF** childcare and early childhood education facility, with direct access to a ground-level courtyard and patio used as an outdoor play area. Measured under **BOMA 2010**, stipulated and expressly **not subject to remeasurement**. Pro rata share is 5,800 divided by total Building RSF \\\\u201cas reasonably determined by Landlord\\\\u201d, with Landlord to notify the share within 30 days of commencement \\\\u2014 **the Building area is not stated in the lease**. Permitted use: childcare, daycare and early childhood education, with licensing obligations to the NC Division of Child Development and Early Education.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(2) Term\\\",\\n  \\\"Lease Date 10 January 2017; Commencement **1 April 2017**; Expiration **31 March 2032**; **fifteen years**. Early access from 1 February 2017 for installation of fixtures and build-out, with no Base Rent or Additional Rent during that period. Three consecutive renewal terms of five years each, so the lease could run to 31 March 2047 if all options are exercised.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(3) Rent\\\",\\n  \\\"Year 1: **$22.00/RSF** = $127,600.00 per annum ($10,633.33 per month). Escalation **2.5% per annum compounded annually** on each anniversary of the Commencement Date. Current Lease Year 8 (1 April 2024 \\\\u2013 31 March 2025): **$25.90/RSF = $150,220.00 per annum ($12,518.33 per month)**. Year 15: $30.79/RSF = $178,582.00. Late charge 5%; interest 1.5% per month (18% per annum).\\\"),\\n (\\\"(4) Lease type\\\",\\n  \\\"**Triple net (NNN)** \\\\u2014 Article 5; tenant pays pro rata shares of Operating Expenses, Real Estate Taxes and Insurance Costs as Additional Rent.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(5) Operating expenses\\\",\\n  \\\"Tenant pays its pro rata share of Operating Expenses, Real Estate Taxes and Insurance Costs, by monthly estimate with a 90-day annual reconciliation statement and an audit right (commenced within 12 months). Excluded from Operating Expenses: capital expenditure (except law-mandated post-commencement capex, amortised over useful life with interest not exceeding 8%), leasing commissions, TI for other tenants, income and franchise taxes, depreciation, correction of original construction defects, and costs recovered from insurance, condemnation or other tenants. **Management fee capped at 5% of gross revenues from the Building.** Tax protest savings are credited through to the tenant. **No cap on controllable expenses.**\\\"),\\n (\\\"(6) Renewal options\\\",\\n  \\\"**Three consecutive five-year options** (to 2047). Notice **not less than 12 months** before expiry of the then-current term; failure to give timely notice waives that option **and all subsequent unexercised options**. Options are personal to BrightPath except in favour of a permitted affiliate. **First Renewal Term rent is the lesser of fair market rent and the Year 15 rent escalated at 3% per annum compounded** \\\\u2014 an effective cap in the tenant's favour. Second and Third Renewal Terms at fair market rent. FMR by agreement or a three-appraiser process using the average of the two closest appraisals; interim rent at the prior rate pending determination.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(7) Termination rights\\\",\\n  \\\"**No general early termination right for the tenant.** Landlord has a **recapture right** exercisable within 30 days of a request for consent to assign or sublet, which operates as a termination right in respect of the affected space (see category 8). Landlord may terminate on default (Article 16), including where the tenant's childcare licence is revoked, suspended or ineffective for more than 60 consecutive days. **Casualty:** Landlord to commence restoration within 60 days and complete within 180 days; if it determines restoration cannot be completed within 180 days, either party may terminate on 30 days' notice. Rent abates proportionately while untenantable. **Condemnation:** either party may terminate on a taking of 25% or more of the RSF; the award belongs to Landlord with a separate claim available to the tenant for trade fixtures, personal property, moving and business interruption. Holdover **150%**.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(8) Assignment and subletting\\\",\\n  \\\"Landlord's prior written consent required, on a reasonableness standard tied to the assignee's financial condition, creditworthiness, reputation, intended use and compatibility (\\\\u00a7 11.1). **Landlord recapture right:** within 30 days of receiving a complete request, Landlord may terminate the lease as to the proposed space (or the whole premises for an assignment) and re-let it to anyone on any terms with no liability to the tenant (\\\\u00a7 11.2). Conditions of consent include that the tenant remains primarily liable, 30 days' notice with audited financial statements, a business plan and references, and **payment to Landlord of 50% of any consideration above the rent payable under the lease**, net of the tenant's reasonable costs (\\\\u00a7 11.3(e)). **Affiliate transfers** permitted without consent on 15 days' notice, with assumption and continuing tenant liability (\\\\u00a7 11.4).\\\"),\\n (\\\"(9) Security deposit / guaranty\\\",\\n  \\\"**Security deposit of $25,440.00**, described in Article 1 and Article 6 as \\\\u201cequal to two (2) months of Base Rent\\\\u201d. Non-interest-bearing, need not be segregated, with a ten-day replenishment obligation and return within 30 days after expiry and surrender. **No guaranty.**\\\"),\\n (\\\"(10) Tenant improvements\\\",\\n  \\\"**No TI allowance** \\\\u2014 \\\\u201cTenant's Work shall be entirely self-funded by Tenant\\\\u201d (Exhibit D \\\\u00a7 3). Landlord delivers shell condition, including slab, exterior walls, MEP stubbed to the boundary, sprinklers and one ADA restroom. Improvements become Landlord's property except trade fixtures, personal property and movable equipment; Landlord may require removal of designated improvements on 60 days' notice before expiry, with restoration at the tenant's cost.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(11) Special provisions\\\",\\n  \\\"**Exclusive use (\\\\u00a7 7.2):** Landlord may not lease any space in Millbrook Medical Plaza for a childcare, daycare or early childhood education facility; the covenant runs with the property and binds successors; the tenant's remedy is injunctive relief plus actual damages. **Childcare licence revocation** for more than 60 consecutive days is an Event of Default (\\\\u00a7 16.1(e)). **Phase I ESA** prepared by Hanover Environmental Consultants Inc. dated 15 November 2016, with no RECs, CRECs or HRECs, and a Landlord representation of continued accuracy (\\\\u00a7 10.2). Access protocols coordinated with the on-site manager given the presence of children (\\\\u00a7 13). Outdoor play-area rights acknowledged (Exhibit C \\\\u00b6 8) and hours of operation 6:30 a.m. to 6:30 p.m. acknowledged. Governing law: North Carolina.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(12) Risk flags\\\",\\n  \\\"**R-13** Year 8 rate departs from the stated 2.5% escalation and the error propagates to the end of the term. **R-15** security deposit amount inconsistent with \\\\u201ctwo months of Base Rent\\\\u201d. **R-19** building area not stated. **R-09** no estoppel obligation in the lease. **R-16** landlord-favourable recapture and 50% profit share (not a risk to Galleon, noted for completeness).\\\"),\\n], notes=[\\n \\\"**Escalation integrity.** The Year 7 rate is $25.51. Applying 2.5% gives **$26.1477 \\\\u2192 $26.15** for Year 8, but Exhibit B states **$25.90**. The schedule then compounds from the erroneous figure ($25.90 \\\\u00d7 1.025 = $26.55, which is the stated Year 9 rate), so the shortfall carries through to Year 15 ($30.79 stated against $31.09 computed). Current-year understatement **$1,456.30**; cumulative over Years 8\\\\u201315 **$12,773.84**.\\\",\\n \\\"**Security deposit.** Two months of the current (Year 8) Base Rent is $150,220.00 \\\\u00f7 12 \\\\u00d7 2 = **$25,036.67**; two months of Year 1 rent would be $21,266.67. The stated $25,440.00 equals two months at $26.317/RSF, a rate that appears nowhere in the schedule. The amount held should be confirmed against the ledger and, if $25,440.00 is correct, treated as a closing proration.\\\",\\n \\\"Years 1 to 7 of the schedule agree with 2.5% compounding to the nearest cent; only Year 8 breaks the chain.\\\",\\n \\\"The document retains an unremoved Word field placeholder (\\\\u201cRight-click to update Table of Contents\\\\u201d) on the cover page \\\\u2014 an indicator that the lease was assembled from a template and that the remaining text should not be assumed to have been checked against a signed original.\\\",\\n],\\nrisk_line=\\\"R-13 (medium), R-15, R-19, R-09.\\\")\\nPYEOF\\necho ok\"}", "result": "ok\n"}
{"turn": 27, "role": "assistant", "text": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_ET_HiywI7xtfllkZfQ2wRnC6493", "name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && cat >> work/build.py <<'PYEOF'\\n\\n# ---------- 4.4 SE FIRE ----------\\nh2(doc, \\\"4.4  Southeastern Fire & Safety Equipment Co. \\\\u2014 Greystone Industrial Park, Unit 12\\\")\\nsnapshot(doc, [\\n (\\\"Tenant\\\",\\\"Southeastern Fire & Safety Equipment Co., a NC corporation\\\"),\\n (\\\"Premises\\\",\\\"Unit 12, 22,000 RSF industrial / flex\\\"),\\n (\\\"Landlord\\\",\\\"Thornfield Realty Holdings LP\\\"),\\n (\\\"Property\\\",\\\"770 Greystone Boulevard, Gastonia, Gaston Co., NC 28052\\\"),\\n (\\\"Lease date\\\",\\\"July 1, 2014\\\"),\\n (\\\"Source\\\",\\\"D6 \\\\u2014 Lease Agreement dated July 1, 2014\\\"),\\n (\\\"Current annual rent\\\",\\\"$305,250.00  ($25,437.50 / month, holdover)\\\"),\\n (\\\"Share of portfolio\\\",\\\"13.0%\\\"),\\n])\\nabstraction(doc, [\\n (\\\"(1) Tenant and premises\\\",\\n  \\\"Southeastern Fire & Safety Equipment Co., a North Carolina corporation. **Unit 12**, approximately **22,000 RSF** of industrial/flex space within Greystone Industrial Park, comprising warehouse area, a loading dock with two drive-in bays and office/flex area. The stated RSF is **conclusive and binding** for Base Rent and pro rata purposes (\\\\u00a7 2.2). Pro rata share is 22,000 divided by the rentable area of the Building or of Greystone Industrial Park as a whole \\\\u201cas reasonably determined by Landlord\\\\u201d \\\\u2014 **neither area is stated**. Permitted use: light industrial, warehousing, equipment storage and testing, and the service, repair, maintenance and reconditioning of fire safety equipment, plus ancillary office.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(2) Term\\\",\\n  \\\"Effective Date and Commencement **1 July 2014**; Expiration **30 June 2024**; **ten Lease Years**. **The term has expired.** The tenant has held over on a month-to-month basis since 1 July 2024. The single five-year Renewal Term (1 July 2024 \\\\u2013 30 June 2029) was **not exercised**: the notice deadline was **1 April 2024** and \\\\u00a7 3.3 provides that failure to give timely notice is an irrevocable waiver. **No renewal right remains.**\\\"),\\n (\\\"(3) Rent\\\",\\n  \\\"Year 1: **$7.50/RSF** = $165,000.00 per annum ($13,750.00 per month). Stated escalation **2% per annum**. Year 10 per the schedule: **$9.25/RSF** = $203,500.00 per annum ($16,958.33 per month) \\\\u2014 but see the verification note below; 2% compounding from Year 9 yields $8.97. **Holdover rent: 150% of the final month's Base Rent = $25,437.50 per month ($305,250.00 per annum)**, stated in both Article 13 and Exhibit B. Late charge 5%; interest 1.5% per month.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(4) Lease type\\\",\\n  \\\"**Triple net (NNN)** \\\\u2014 Article 5. Base Rent is \\\\u201cabsolutely net to Landlord\\\\u201d.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(5) Operating expenses\\\",\\n  \\\"Tenant pays its pro rata share of Operating Expenses, real estate taxes and insurance premiums, by monthly estimate with a 90-day annual reconciliation statement. Management fee not to exceed 5% of gross rental income. **No cap on recoveries and no tenant audit right** \\\\u2014 the lease provides for a reconciliation statement only.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(6) Renewal options\\\",\\n  \\\"**One** five-year option at fair market rental rate, determined in good faith by the parties or, failing agreement within 30 days, by a single mutually selected licensed appraiser whose determination is binding, with costs shared equally. Notice **no later than 1 April 2024** (90 days before expiry). **Lapsed unexercised \\\\u2014 no renewal rights remain.**\\\"),\\n (\\\"(7) Termination rights\\\",\\n  \\\"**During the holdover either party may terminate on 30 days' written notice** (Article 13); acceptance of holdover rent is not consent to a tenancy and does not waive the Landlord's right to recover possession. The tenant remains liable for holdover damages. Landlord may terminate on default (Article 12), with damages including the present value at 6% of the rent for the balance of the term. **Casualty:** Landlord may elect to restore within 180 days or to terminate within 60 days of the casualty; rent abates in proportion to the untenantable area. **Condemnation:** the lease terminates if substantially all of the premises is taken; awards belong to Landlord with a separate claim available to the tenant for trade fixtures, personal property and relocation.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(8) Assignment and subletting\\\",\\n  \\\"Landlord's prior written consent required, **withheld in the Landlord's sole and absolute discretion** (\\\\u00a7 9.1) \\\\u2014 the most restrictive standard in the portfolio. Unconsented transfer is void **and an Event of Default**. **No release** of the tenant (\\\\u00a7 9.2). **100% of any rent, consideration or other amounts received above the rent payable under the lease** must be paid over to Landlord (\\\\u00a7 9.3). Each transfer requires separate consent (\\\\u00a7 9.4).\\\"),\\n (\\\"(9) Security deposit / guaranty\\\",\\n  \\\"**None.** No security deposit, no guaranty and no letter of credit. A 13.0% share of aggregate rent is held by a holding-over tenant with no credit support and no remaining term.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(10) Tenant improvements\\\",\\n  \\\"**No TI allowance.** Non-structural alterations under $25,000 may be made without consent on 15 days' notice; structural alterations or work of $25,000 or more require consent with architect-prepared plans (\\\\u00a7 10.1\\\\u201310.2). Alterations become Landlord's property unless Landlord requires removal on notice given at least 30 days before expiry; trade fixtures and movable personal property remain the tenant's and must be removed with damage repaired (\\\\u00a7 10.3).\\\"),\\n (\\\"(11) Special provisions\\\",\\n  \\\"**Environmental (Article 14) \\\\u2014 the most significant environmental profile in the portfolio.** The tenant is expressly permitted to store, handle, use and transport fire suppressant chemicals, **aqueous film-forming foam (AFFF), foam concentrates, dry chemical agents and PFAS-containing materials** on the premises, subject to permits, a maintained inventory, annual provision of the inventory to Landlord and delivery of safety data sheets on request (\\\\u00a7 14.2). It must carry **Pollution Legal Liability insurance of $1,000,000 per occurrence** (\\\\u00a7 7.1(b)) and commercial general liability of $2,000,000 per occurrence / $5,000,000 aggregate. The environmental indemnity in \\\\u00a7 14.3 is broad, expressly covers AFFF, foam concentrates and PFAS, and **survives termination**; \\\\u00a7 14.4 imposes a remediation obligation; \\\\u00a7 14.5 imposes a compliance and notification regime. Landlord may conduct environmental testing at its own cost but is reimbursed if contamination attributable to the tenant is found. **Subordination (Article 16):** self-operative, with **no non-disturbance**, and the tenant irrevocably appoints Landlord as its attorney-in-fact to execute subordination documents. **Limitation of liability:** Landlord's liability is limited to its equity interest in the Building (\\\\u00a7 11.3). Governing law: North Carolina, venue Gaston or Mecklenburg County.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(12) Risk flags\\\",\\n  \\\"**R-04** expired lease, at-will holdover, no renewal right, no credit support \\\\u2014 13.0% of aggregate rent. **R-12** Year 10 rate departs from the stated 2% escalation and drives the holdover base. **R-25** AFFF/PFAS storage on premises with a survival indemnity but no security. **R-10** self-operative subordination with no non-disturbance. **R-21** no deposit or guaranty.\\\"),\\n], notes=[\\n \\\"**Escalation integrity \\\\u2014 this one matters.** Years 1 to 9 agree with 2% compounding to the nearest cent. Year 9 is $8.79; applying 2% gives **$8.9658 \\\\u2192 $8.97**, but the schedule states **$9.25**. Year 10 is therefore overstated by $203,500.00 \\\\u2212 $197,247.60 = **$6,252.40** per annum of base rent, and the holdover rent derived from it at 150% is overstated by roughly **$9,378.60** per annum ($305,250.00 against $295,871.40 on the corrected base).\\\",\\n \\\"**Which figure governs?** Section 4.1 provides that if the amounts in Section 4.1 conflict with Exhibit B, **Exhibit B controls**, and both state $9.25. The express rate is therefore arguably $9.25 notwithstanding the 2% formula. Because 13.0% of the aggregate rests on this figure, the rent actually billed for the final year should be confirmed from the billing ledger rather than resolved by construction (Risk R-12).\\\",\\n \\\"The 150% holdover calculation itself is correct on its stated base: $16,958.33 \\\\u00d7 1.5 = $25,437.50 per month.\\\",\\n \\\"Renewal deadline verified: 90 days before 30 June 2024 is 1 April 2024, as the lease states, and the Rent Roll correctly records the option as expired unexercised.\\\",\\n \\\"There is no TI allowance, and no estoppel, audit or non-disturbance protection for the Landlord or the tenant.\\\",\\n],\\nrisk_line=\\\"R-04 (high), R-12 (medium), R-25, R-10, R-21.\\\")\\n\\n# ---------- 4.5 VERDANA ----------\\nh2(doc, \\\"4.5  Verdana Software Solutions Inc. \\\\u2014 Concord Office Tower, 8th Floor\\\")\\nsnapshot(doc, [\\n (\\\"Tenant\\\",\\\"Verdana Software Solutions Inc., a Delaware corporation (GA-qualified)\\\"),\\n (\\\"Premises\\\",\\\"Entire 8th floor, 18,750 RSF Class A office\\\"),\\n (\\\"Landlord\\\",\\\"Thornfield Realty Holdings LP\\\"),\\n (\\\"Property\\\",\\\"300 Concord Plaza Drive, Atlanta, Fulton Co., GA 30309\\\"),\\n (\\\"Lease date\\\",\\\"February 28, 2022\\\"),\\n (\\\"Source\\\",\\\"D7 \\\\u2014 Office Lease Agreement dated February 28, 2022\\\"),\\n (\\\"Current annual rent\\\",\\\"$676,312.50  ($56,359.38 / month)\\\"),\\n (\\\"Share of portfolio\\\",\\\"28.8% \\\\u2014 largest tenant\\\"),\\n])\\nabstraction(doc, [\\n (\\\"(1) Tenant and premises\\\",\\n  \\\"Verdana Software Solutions Inc., a Delaware corporation qualified to do business in Georgia. The **entire 8th floor** of Concord Office Tower, approximately **18,750 RSF** of Class A office; the Building totals approximately **150,000 RSF** (stated in the lease), giving a pro rata share of **12.50%**. Measured under **BOMA Z65.1-2017** and conclusive absent written agreement. **Parking:** 56 unreserved spaces at no charge (2.99 per 1,000 RSF) plus **8 reserved executive spaces at $175.00 per space per month = $1,400.00 per month / $16,800.00 per year**, payable as Additional Rent and adjustable annually by not more than 5%. Permitted use: general office, software development and ancillary uses.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(2) Term\\\",\\n  \\\"Lease Date 28 February 2022; Commencement **1 July 2022**; Expiration **30 June 2032**; **ten years**. Early access from 1 April 2022 for construction, with no Base Rent and without affecting the Expiration Date. Renewal Terms: 1 July 2032 \\\\u2013 30 June 2037 and 1 July 2037 \\\\u2013 30 June 2042. Any Expansion Space is coterminous with the original premises, expiring 30 June 2032 (\\\\u00a7 13.05).\\\"),\\n (\\\"(3) Rent\\\",\\n  \\\"Year 1: **$34.00/RSF** = $637,500.00 per annum ($53,125.00 per month). Escalation **3% per annum compounded annually**. Current Lease Year 3 (1 July 2024 \\\\u2013 30 June 2025): **$36.07/RSF = $676,312.50 per annum ($56,359.38 per month)**. Year 10: $44.35/RSF = $831,562.50. Additional Rent includes the $16,800.00 reserved parking charge. Late fee 5%; interest 1.5% per month.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(4) Lease type\\\",\\n  \\\"**Full-service gross with a Base Year 2022 expense stop** \\\\u2014 Article V.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(5) Operating expenses\\\",\\n  \\\"Landlord pays all Operating Expenses; from 1 January 2023 the tenant pays its **12.50% pro rata share of the excess over calendar 2022** actuals, by monthly estimate with a 120-day annual statement. **Controllable operating expenses are capped at 5% per annum on a cumulative compounding basis** over the base-year amount, excluding taxes, insurance, utilities and snow/ice removal (\\\\u00a7 5.07) \\\\u2014 the only expense cap in the portfolio. **Gross-up to 95% occupancy** where the Building is less occupied (\\\\u00a7 5.08). Management fee capped at **4% of Building gross revenues**. Audit right; if an overcharge exceeds 5% Landlord pays the tenant's audit costs. Operating Expenses exclude capital except law-mandated or expense-reducing items amortised at 8%, debt service, income taxes, leasing commissions, other tenants' TI, and legal costs of tenant disputes.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(6) Renewal options\\\",\\n  \\\"**Two consecutive five-year options at 95% of fair market rent**, which must be exercised consecutively. Notice **not less than 12 months** before expiry \\\\u2014 first option by **30 June 2031**, second by 30 June 2036. No default condition at exercise or commencement. **No TI allowance in either Renewal Term** unless separately agreed. FMR by agreement or a three-MAI-appraiser process using the average of the two closest appraisals.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(7) Termination rights\\\",\\n  \\\"**No general early termination right for the tenant.** **Contraction right (\\\\u00a7 14):** at any time after the end of Lease Year 5 (i.e. on or after 1 July 2027) the tenant may, once, surrender up to **5,000 RSF** (26.7% of the premises) on **nine months' notice**, paying a contraction fee equal to the unamortised TI allowance allocable to that space (amortised at 7% over 120 months on $55.00/RSF) plus **six months' Base Rent** on the surrendered space; the premises, Base Rent, pro rata share and parking are then reduced proportionately. Landlord may terminate on default and may **accelerate** all remaining rent discounted at the Federal Reserve discount rate plus 1% (\\\\u00a7 20.02). **Casualty:** if Landlord determines repair will exceed **270 days**, either party may terminate; rent abates proportionately. **Condemnation:** termination on a total or disabling partial taking; awards to Landlord, with a separate claim for the tenant's moving costs, its own TI excess and business goodwill. Holdover **150%** plus damages.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(8) Assignment and subletting\\\",\\n  \\\"Assignment requires Landlord's consent, **not unreasonably withheld, conditioned or delayed**, and the assignor remains secondarily liable (\\\\u00a7 11.05). **No recapture right** \\\\u2014 \\\\u00a7 11.07 states expressly that Landlord has no recapture, termination or cancellation right in connection with any assignment or sublease. **Subletting up to 40% (7,500 RSF) is permitted without consent** subject to conditions: use consistent with the Permitted Use, no governmental entity, not an existing tenant or a prospect in active negotiation, and notice with a copy of the executed sublease within 10 business days (\\\\u00a7 11.02). Subletting above 40% requires consent within 20 business days, with **deemed consent on silence** (\\\\u00a7 11.03). **50% of Subletting Profits is payable to Landlord** (\\\\u00a7 11.04). **Affiliate transfers** permitted without consent subject to a tangible net-worth test measured against the tenant's net worth at the Lease Date and 15 days' notice (\\\\u00a7 11.06).\\\"),\\n (\\\"(9) Security deposit / guaranty\\\",\\n  \\\"**None.** Article I states \\\\u201cSecurity Deposit: None\\\\u201d and there is no guaranty. The largest tenancy in the portfolio (28.8% of aggregate rent) is supported only by the covenant of a Delaware corporation.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(10) Tenant improvements\\\",\\n  \\\"TI Allowance **$55.00/RSF = $1,031,250.00** (Exhibit C), drawn monthly against AIA G702/G703 applications and lien waivers with **10% retainage** released on substantial completion and certificate of occupancy. Unused allowance is **forfeited**, not credited. For recapture purposes the allowance is amortised at **7% per annum over 120 months** on a mortgage-style basis (\\\\u00a7 7.04). Improvements become Landlord's property; Landlord may designate non-standard improvements for removal at the time it approves plans. **Expansion Space allowance, if the option is exercised: $40.00/RSF \\\\u00d7 18,500 RSF = $740,000.00.**\\\"),\\n (\\\"(11) Special provisions\\\",\\n  \\\"**Expansion option (Article XIII) \\\\u2014 the principal encumbrance.** Verdana may require the Lessor to add the **entire 9th floor, approximately 18,500 RSF**, exercisable **at any time during Lease Years 3 to 5 (1 July 2024 \\\\u2013 30 June 2027)** on at least six months' notice. Expansion rent is **the same rate per RSF then in effect for the 8th floor** ($36.07/RSF in Year 3), escalating thereafter on the same 3% schedule, with a **$40.00/RSF allowance ($740,000.00)** and a term coterminous to 30 June 2032. The Lessor has no right to refuse. **Contraction right** (category 7). **Subordination:** subordination is expressly **conditioned** on the mortgagee delivering a commercially reasonable SNDA (\\\\u00a7 17.01), and the Landlord represented that **no mortgage encumbered the Building** as at 28 February 2022 (\\\\u00a7 17.02). **Estoppel:** either party within 15 business days, with deemed acknowledgment (\\\\u00a7 XXIV). After-hours HVAC $75.00 per hour per zone, adjustable. Alterations under $50,000 per project require no consent. Governing law: Georgia.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(12) Risk flags\\\",\\n  \\\"**R-06** 9th-floor expansion option at below-market fixed rent with a $740,000 allowance, window already open (high). **R-17** contraction right over up to 5,000 RSF. **R-21** no deposit or guaranty for the largest tenancy. **R-10** subordination conditional on an SNDA that does not exist; the no-mortgage representation is more than two years old. **R-09** estoppel exists but has not been obtained.\\\"),\\n], notes=[\\n \\\"Rent schedule recomputed on 3% compounding from $34.00 across all ten years: every stated rate and amount agrees to the nearest cent \\\\u2014 **the only lease in the portfolio with a fully conforming schedule**.\\\",\\n \\\"Pro rata share recomputed: 18,750 \\\\u00f7 150,000 = 12.50% \\\\u2014 correct. Parking ratio: 56 \\\\u00f7 18.75 = 2.99 per 1,000 RSF \\\\u2014 correct. Reserved parking: 8 \\\\u00d7 $175 \\\\u00d7 12 = $16,800.00 \\\\u2014 correct, and correctly excluded from the Rent Roll's base rent total (Rent Roll note 6).\\\",\\n \\\"TI allowance recomputed: 18,750 \\\\u00d7 $55.00 = $1,031,250.00 \\\\u2014 correct. Expansion allowance: 18,500 \\\\u00d7 $40.00 = $740,000.00 \\\\u2014 correct.\\\",\\n \\\"**Illustrative contraction fee.** Assuming contraction of the full 5,000 RSF effective 1 April 2028 (the earliest date consistent with notice given on 1 July 2027), the fee would be approximately $98,525 of Base Rent (six months at the Year 6 rate of $39.41/RSF \\\\u00d7 5,000 RSF) plus approximately $140,600 of unamortised TI allowance (7% mortgage-style amortisation of $275,000 over 120 months, after 69 months) \\\\u2014 in the order of **$239,000**. This is illustrative only: the fee depends on the contraction date and the rate then in effect.\\\",\\n \\\"Exhibit E contains a typographical error (\\\\u201cMartin Lueger King Jr. Day\\\\u201d). Cosmetic, noted for completeness of the document-integrity record.\\\",\\n],\\nrisk_line=\\\"R-06 (high), R-17, R-21, R-10, R-09.\\\")\\nPYEOF\\necho ok\"}"}], "input_tokens": 184292, "output_tokens": 4949, "finish_reason": "completed"}
{"turn": 27, "role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call_00_ET_HiywI7xtfllkZfQ2wRnC6493", "tool_name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && cat >> work/build.py <<'PYEOF'\\n\\n# ---------- 4.4 SE FIRE ----------\\nh2(doc, \\\"4.4  Southeastern Fire & Safety Equipment Co. \\\\u2014 Greystone Industrial Park, Unit 12\\\")\\nsnapshot(doc, [\\n (\\\"Tenant\\\",\\\"Southeastern Fire & Safety Equipment Co., a NC corporation\\\"),\\n (\\\"Premises\\\",\\\"Unit 12, 22,000 RSF industrial / flex\\\"),\\n (\\\"Landlord\\\",\\\"Thornfield Realty Holdings LP\\\"),\\n (\\\"Property\\\",\\\"770 Greystone Boulevard, Gastonia, Gaston Co., NC 28052\\\"),\\n (\\\"Lease date\\\",\\\"July 1, 2014\\\"),\\n (\\\"Source\\\",\\\"D6 \\\\u2014 Lease Agreement dated July 1, 2014\\\"),\\n (\\\"Current annual rent\\\",\\\"$305,250.00  ($25,437.50 / month, holdover)\\\"),\\n (\\\"Share of portfolio\\\",\\\"13.0%\\\"),\\n])\\nabstraction(doc, [\\n (\\\"(1) Tenant and premises\\\",\\n  \\\"Southeastern Fire & Safety Equipment Co., a North Carolina corporation. **Unit 12**, approximately **22,000 RSF** of industrial/flex space within Greystone Industrial Park, comprising warehouse area, a loading dock with two drive-in bays and office/flex area. The stated RSF is **conclusive and binding** for Base Rent and pro rata purposes (\\\\u00a7 2.2). Pro rata share is 22,000 divided by the rentable area of the Building or of Greystone Industrial Park as a whole \\\\u201cas reasonably determined by Landlord\\\\u201d \\\\u2014 **neither area is stated**. Permitted use: light industrial, warehousing, equipment storage and testing, and the service, repair, maintenance and reconditioning of fire safety equipment, plus ancillary office.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(2) Term\\\",\\n  \\\"Effective Date and Commencement **1 July 2014**; Expiration **30 June 2024**; **ten Lease Years**. **The term has expired.** The tenant has held over on a month-to-month basis since 1 July 2024. The single five-year Renewal Term (1 July 2024 \\\\u2013 30 June 2029) was **not exercised**: the notice deadline was **1 April 2024** and \\\\u00a7 3.3 provides that failure to give timely notice is an irrevocable waiver. **No renewal right remains.**\\\"),\\n (\\\"(3) Rent\\\",\\n  \\\"Year 1: **$7.50/RSF** = $165,000.00 per annum ($13,750.00 per month). Stated escalation **2% per annum**. Year 10 per the schedule: **$9.25/RSF** = $203,500.00 per annum ($16,958.33 per month) \\\\u2014 but see the verification note below; 2% compounding from Year 9 yields $8.97. **Holdover rent: 150% of the final month's Base Rent = $25,437.50 per month ($305,250.00 per annum)**, stated in both Article 13 and Exhibit B. Late charge 5%; interest 1.5% per month.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(4) Lease type\\\",\\n  \\\"**Triple net (NNN)** \\\\u2014 Article 5. Base Rent is \\\\u201cabsolutely net to Landlord\\\\u201d.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(5) Operating expenses\\\",\\n  \\\"Tenant pays its pro rata share of Operating Expenses, real estate taxes and insurance premiums, by monthly estimate with a 90-day annual reconciliation statement. Management fee not to exceed 5% of gross rental income. **No cap on recoveries and no tenant audit right** \\\\u2014 the lease provides for a reconciliation statement only.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(6) Renewal options\\\",\\n  \\\"**One** five-year option at fair market rental rate, determined in good faith by the parties or, failing agreement within 30 days, by a single mutually selected licensed appraiser whose determination is binding, with costs shared equally. Notice **no later than 1 April 2024** (90 days before expiry). **Lapsed unexercised \\\\u2014 no renewal rights remain.**\\\"),\\n (\\\"(7) Termination rights\\\",\\n  \\\"**During the holdover either party may terminate on 30 days' written notice** (Article 13); acceptance of holdover rent is not consent to a tenancy and does not waive the Landlord's right to recover possession. The tenant remains liable for holdover damages. Landlord may terminate on default (Article 12), with damages including the present value at 6% of the rent for the balance of the term. **Casualty:** Landlord may elect to restore within 180 days or to terminate within 60 days of the casualty; rent abates in proportion to the untenantable area. **Condemnation:** the lease terminates if substantially all of the premises is taken; awards belong to Landlord with a separate claim available to the tenant for trade fixtures, personal property and relocation.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(8) Assignment and subletting\\\",\\n  \\\"Landlord's prior written consent required, **withheld in the Landlord's sole and absolute discretion** (\\\\u00a7 9.1) \\\\u2014 the most restrictive standard in the portfolio. Unconsented transfer is void **and an Event of Default**. **No release** of the tenant (\\\\u00a7 9.2). **100% of any rent, consideration or other amounts received above the rent payable under the lease** must be paid over to Landlord (\\\\u00a7 9.3). Each transfer requires separate consent (\\\\u00a7 9.4).\\\"),\\n (\\\"(9) Security deposit / guaranty\\\",\\n  \\\"**None.** No security deposit, no guaranty and no letter of credit. A 13.0% share of aggregate rent is held by a holding-over tenant with no credit support and no remaining term.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(10) Tenant improvements\\\",\\n  \\\"**No TI allowance.** Non-structural alterations under $25,000 may be made without consent on 15 days' notice; structural alterations or work of $25,000 or more require consent with architect-prepared plans (\\\\u00a7 10.1\\\\u201310.2). Alterations become Landlord's property unless Landlord requires removal on notice given at least 30 days before expiry; trade fixtures and movable personal property remain the tenant's and must be removed with damage repaired (\\\\u00a7 10.3).\\\"),\\n (\\\"(11) Special provisions\\\",\\n  \\\"**Environmental (Article 14) \\\\u2014 the most significant environmental profile in the portfolio.** The tenant is expressly permitted to store, handle, use and transport fire suppressant chemicals, **aqueous film-forming foam (AFFF), foam concentrates, dry chemical agents and PFAS-containing materials** on the premises, subject to permits, a maintained inventory, annual provision of the inventory to Landlord and delivery of safety data sheets on request (\\\\u00a7 14.2). It must carry **Pollution Legal Liability insurance of $1,000,000 per occurrence** (\\\\u00a7 7.1(b)) and commercial general liability of $2,000,000 per occurrence / $5,000,000 aggregate. The environmental indemnity in \\\\u00a7 14.3 is broad, expressly covers AFFF, foam concentrates and PFAS, and **survives termination**; \\\\u00a7 14.4 imposes a remediation obligation; \\\\u00a7 14.5 imposes a compliance and notification regime. Landlord may conduct environmental testing at its own cost but is reimbursed if contamination attributable to the tenant is found. **Subordination (Article 16):** self-operative, with **no non-disturbance**, and the tenant irrevocably appoints Landlord as its attorney-in-fact to execute subordination documents. **Limitation of liability:** Landlord's liability is limited to its equity interest in the Building (\\\\u00a7 11.3). Governing law: North Carolina, venue Gaston or Mecklenburg County.\\\"),\\n (\\\"(12) Risk flags\\\",\\n  \\\"**R-04** expired lease, at-will holdover, no renewal right, no credit support \\\\u2014 13.0% of aggregate rent. **R-12** Year 10 rate departs from the stated 2% escalation and drives the holdover base. **R-25** AFFF/PFAS storage on premises with a survival indemnity but no security. **R-10** self-operative subordination with no non-disturbance. **R-21** no deposit or guaranty.\\\"),\\n], notes=[\\n \\\"**Escalation integrity \\\\u2014 this one matters.** Years 1 to 9 agree with 2% compounding to the nearest cent. Year 9 is $8.79; applying 2% gives **$8.9658 \\\\u2192 $8.97**, but the schedule states **$9.25**. Year 10 is therefore overstated by $203,500.00 \\\\u2212 $197,247.60 = **$6,252.40** per annum of base rent, and the holdover rent derived from it at 150% is overstated by roughly **$9,378.60** per annum ($305,250.00 against $295,871.40 on the corrected base).\\\",\\n \\\"**Which figure governs?** Section 4.1 provides that if the amounts in Section 4.1 conflict with Exhibit B, **Exhibit B controls**, and both state $9.25. The express rate is therefore arguably $9.25 notwithstanding the 2% formula. Because 13.0% of the aggregate rests on this figure, the rent actually billed for the final year should be confirmed from the billing ledger rather than resolved by construction (Risk R-12).\\\",\\n \\\"The 150% holdover calculation itself is correct on its stated base: $16,958.33 \\\\u00d7 1.5 = $25,437.50 per month.\\\",\\n \\\"Renewal deadline verified: 90 days before 30 June 2024 is 1 April 2024, as the lease states, and the Rent Roll correctly records the option as expired unexercised.\\\",\\n \\\"There is no TI allowance, and no estoppel, audit or non-disturbance protection for the Landlord or the tenant.\\\",\\n],\\nrisk_line=\\\"R-04 (high), R-12 (medium), R-25, R-10, R-21.\\\")\\n\\n# ---------- 4.5 VERDANA ----------\\nh2(doc, \\\"4.5  Verdana Software Solutions Inc. \\\\u2014 Concord Office Tower, 8th Floor\\\")\\nsnapshot(doc, [\\n (\\\"Tenant\\\",\\\"Verdana Software Solutions Inc., a Delaware corporation (GA-qualified)\\\"),\\n (\\\"Premises\\\",\\\"Entire 8th floor, 18,750 RSF Class A office\\\"),\\n (\\\"Landlord\\\",\\\"Thornfield Realty Holdings LP\\\"),\\n (\\\"Property\\\",\\\"300 Concord Plaza Drive, Atlanta, Fulton Co., GA 30309\\\"),\\n (\\\"Lease date\\\",\\\"February 28, 2022\\\"),\\n (\\\"Source\\\",\\\"D7 \\\\u2014 Office Lease Agreement dated February 28, 2022\\\"),\\n (\\\"Current annual rent\\\",\\\"$676,312.50  ($56,359.38 / month)\\\"),\\n (\\\"Share of portfolio\\\",\\\"28.8% \\\\u2014 largest tenant\\\"),\\n])\\nabstraction(doc, [\\n (\\\"(1) Tenant and premises\\\",\\n  \\\"Verdana Software Solutions Inc., a Delaware corpora