{"turn": 34, "role": "assistant", "text": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_zM3pEW6eo7mXboVpqWU74244", "name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && cat >> work/build.py <<'PYEOF'\\n\\n# ================= 6. VERIFICATION =================\\nh1(doc, \\\"SECTION 6\\\", \\\"Independent Verification of Rent Schedules and Dates\\\")\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"6.1  Method\\\", space_before=2)\\npara(doc, \\\"Section 2(c) of the Engagement Letter requires the firm to independently verify all rent escalation calculations. For each lease we took the stated starting rate per RSF, applied the stated escalation mechanism year by year using the lease's own rounding convention, and compared the result with the rate table in the lease. Because every one of these leases states a per-RSF rate from which the annual amount is derived by simple multiplication, the comparison at the per-RSF level isolates errors in the escalation mechanism from errors in the multiplication.\\\", size=9.8)\\npara(doc, \\\"Two measures are reported. The **current-year difference** is the effect on the rent payable in the Lease Year in effect on January 1, 2025, which is the figure that matters to current income. The **cumulative difference** is the aggregate effect across the remaining term, which is the figure that matters to a valuation done on contract rent. Where the effect is not the same in every year \\\\u2014 as with BrightPath, where the error compounds \\\\u2014 the year-by-year figures are in Appendix A.\\\", size=9.8)\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"6.2  Results by lease\\\")\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"Apex Fulfillment\\\",\\\"3% p.a. compounding\\\",\\\"Years 1\\\\u20134\\\",\\\"Years 5\\\\u201310\\\",\\\"\\\\u2212$525.00 (Year 6)\\\",\\\"\\\\u2212$3,500.00\\\",\\\"**Does not conform.** Year 5 stated $6.180 against $6.190 computed ($6.010 \\\\u00d7 1.03); the error then carries forward at roughly $0.006/RSF. Immaterial in amount but confirms the table was not generated from the stated formula.\\\"],\\n [\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto\\\",\\\"Fixed +$0.75/RSF p.a.\\\",\\\"All 7 years\\\",\\\"None\\\",\\\"nil\\\",\\\"nil\\\",\\\"**Conforms fully.** Every rate and amount agrees exactly.\\\"],\\n [\\\"BrightPath Learning\\\",\\\"2.5% p.a. compounding\\\",\\\"Years 1\\\\u20137\\\",\\\"Years 8\\\\u201315\\\",\\\"\\\\u2212$1,450.00 (Year 8)\\\",\\\"\\\\u2212$12,470.00\\\",\\\"**Does not conform.** Year 8 stated $25.90 against $26.15 computed ($25.51 \\\\u00d7 1.025); the error compounds through Year 15 and also lowers the Year 15 base from which the first renewal rent cap is calculated.\\\"],\\n [\\\"Southeastern Fire & Safety\\\",\\\"2% p.a. compounding\\\",\\\"Years 1\\\\u20139\\\",\\\"Year 10\\\",\\\"+$6,160.00 base  /  +$9,240.00 holdover\\\",\\\"+$6,160.00\\\",\\\"**Does not conform.** Year 10 stated $9.25 against $8.97 computed ($8.79 \\\\u00d7 1.02). This is the only departure with a material effect on current income, because the holdover rent is 150% of the Year 10 rate.\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana Software\\\",\\\"3% p.a. compounding\\\",\\\"All 10 years\\\",\\\"None\\\",\\\"nil\\\",\\\"nil\\\",\\\"**Conforms fully.** Every rate and amount agrees to the cent \\\\u2014 the most reliable rent table in the portfolio.\\\"],\\n [\\\"The Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"CPI-U, 2% floor / 4% cap\\\",\\\"Years 1\\\\u20135 within the band\\\",\\\"None apparent\\\",\\\"nil\\\",\\\"nil\\\",\\\"**Conforms to the mechanism** as far as it can be tested: the implied steps are +3.80%, +4.00% (cap), +2.50% and +2.00% (floor). Year 5 sits exactly on the floor, so the underlying CPI should be confirmed against BLS data.\\\"],\\n [\\\"United States (GSA)\\\",\\\"Flat in firm term; 2.5% in soft term\\\",\\\"Firm term and soft Years 6\\\\u20139\\\",\\\"Soft Year 10\\\",\\\"nil in firm term\\\",\\\"+$150.00 (Year 10 only)\\\",\\\"**Conforms in substance.** Year 10 is one cent per RSF above the chained figure. No economic significance, and the soft term is terminable in any event.\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Lease\\\",\\\"Mechanism as stated\\\",\\\"Conforming years\\\",\\\"Departing years\\\",\\\"Current-year difference\\\",\\\"Cumulative difference\\\",\\\"Assessment\\\"], rows,\\n          [0.85,0.95,0.72,0.62,0.83,0.72,2.01], size=7.2, head_size=7.0, align_center_cols=(2,3),\\n          row_fills=[WARN,None,WARN,WARN,None,None,None], keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"A negative difference means the lease states less rent than its own stated mechanism produces; a positive difference means the lease states more. Full year-by-year workings for all seven leases are at Appendix A. Shaded rows are the three leases whose tables do not conform.\\\")\\n\\nbox(doc, \\\"Why this matters, and why it is not simply a rounding question\\\",\\n    [\\\"The three non-conforming tables share a single pattern: **one year's rate departs from the stated mechanism, and the schedule then compounds forward from the erroneous figure**. That is a drafting or spreadsheet-control failure rather than rounding. The amounts are small in absolute terms \\\\u2014 the net effect on current income is an overstatement of **$7,265 per annum**, or 0.31% of the aggregate \\\\u2014 but three consequences follow:\\\",\\n     \\\"(a) the Rent Roll's statement that \\\\u201call figures [are] as stated in the underlying lease documents\\\\u201d is accurate as a description of the leases but cannot be relied on as a statement that the leases are correct; (b) each tenant's estoppel will certify **its own schedule**, so the certified rent may differ from the Rent Roll and from the correct figure, and Galleon should reconcile all three before closing; and (c) for Southeastern the discrepancy drives the holdover base and therefore 13.0% of aggregate rent, which is the one place where the amount is worth negotiating.\\\"],\\n    fill=AMBER, size=8.8)\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"6.3  Root-cause observations\\\")\\nbullets(doc, [\\n \\\"**The error is always a single year, never a systematic misapplication.** In Apex, BrightPath and Southeastern, every year except one follows the preceding year's stated rate times the stated factor, to the cent. This is consistent with a table built by formula and then manually overwritten in one cell, or built by hand and mis-keyed once.\\\",\\n \\\"**The error always runs in the landlord's disfavour except at Southeastern.** Apex and BrightPath state less rent than the mechanism produces (a tenant benefit); Southeastern states more (a landlord benefit, though one a tenant could dispute).\\\",\\n \\\"**Two leases contain provisions that make the question operative.** Apex \\\\u00a7 4.3 prescribes the calculation method in the body of the lease and states that the rate is \\\\u201ccalculated by multiplying the Base Rent per RSF for the immediately preceding Lease Year by 1.03\\\\u201d \\\\u2014 so the mechanism, not the table, arguably governs. Southeastern \\\\u00a7 4.1 does the opposite and provides that **Exhibit B controls** in the event of conflict \\\\u2014 so the table, not the mechanism, arguably governs there. The two leases therefore resolve the same type of discrepancy in opposite directions, which is a useful reminder that this is a drafting issue and not a data-entry one.\\\",\\n \\\"**No lease contains a reconciliation or true-up mechanism** that would allow either party to correct an error in the schedule after the fact. The remedy is an estoppel, an amendment, or an agreement at closing.\\\",\\n], size=9.2)\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"6.4  Date and notice-period verification\\\")\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"Commencement + 10 years = Expiration\\\",\\\"1 Jun 2019 + 10 yrs = 31 May 2029\\\",\\\"31 May 2029\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto\\\",\\\"Commencement + 7 years = Expiration\\\",\\\"1 Nov 2021 + 7 yrs = 31 Oct 2028\\\",\\\"31 Oct 2028\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"BrightPath\\\",\\\"Commencement + 15 years = Expiration\\\",\\\"1 Apr 2017 + 15 yrs = 31 Mar 2032\\\",\\\"31 Mar 2032\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Southeastern\\\",\\\"Commencement + 10 years = Expiration\\\",\\\"1 Jul 2014 + 10 yrs = 30 Jun 2024\\\",\\\"30 Jun 2024\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"Commencement + 10 years = Expiration\\\",\\\"1 Jul 2022 + 10 yrs = 30 Jun 2032\\\",\\\"30 Jun 2032\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"Commencement + 10 years = Expiration\\\",\\\"1 Oct 2020 + 10 yrs = 30 Sep 2030\\\",\\\"30 Sep 2030\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"GSA\\\",\\\"Firm term 5 years + soft term 5 years\\\",\\\"1 Jan 2021 + 5 = 31 Dec 2025; + 5 = 31 Dec 2030\\\",\\\"31 Dec 2025 / 31 Dec 2030\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"First renewal notice: 12 months before expiry\\\",\\\"31 May 2029 \\\\u2212 12 months = 31 May 2028\\\",\\\"31 May 2028 (stated)\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto\\\",\\\"Renewal notice: 9 months before expiry\\\",\\\"31 Oct 2028 \\\\u2212 9 months = 31 Jan 2028\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2028 (stated)\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto\\\",\\\"Early termination notice: 6 months before effective date\\\",\\\"31 Oct 2025 \\\\u2212 6 months = 30 Apr 2025\\\",\\\"30 Apr 2025 (stated)\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Southeastern\\\",\\\"Renewal notice: 90 days before expiry\\\",\\\"30 Jun 2024 \\\\u2212 90 days = 1 Apr 2024\\\",\\\"1 Apr 2024 (stated)\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"BrightPath\\\",\\\"First renewal notice: 12 months before expiry\\\",\\\"31 Mar 2032 \\\\u2212 12 months = 31 Mar 2031\\\",\\\"not stated\\\",\\\"Computed\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"First renewal notice: 12 months before expiry\\\",\\\"30 Jun 2032 \\\\u2212 12 months = 30 Jun 2031\\\",\\\"not stated\\\",\\\"Computed\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"First renewal notice: 9 months before expiry\\\",\\\"30 Sep 2030 \\\\u2212 9 months = 31 Dec 2029\\\",\\\"not stated\\\",\\\"Computed\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"Guaranty burn-off\\\",\\\"Earlier of 30 Sep 2025 or $2,000,000 TTM sales\\\",\\\"30 Sep 2025 (stated)\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"Expansion window: Lease Years 3 to 5\\\",\\\"1 Jul 2024 \\\\u2013 30 Jun 2027\\\",\\\"1 Jul 2024 \\\\u2013 30 Jun 2027 (stated)\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"Contraction: after Lease Year 5, 9 months' notice\\\",\\\"Notice available on/after 1 Jul 2027; earliest contraction 1 Apr 2028\\\",\\\"\\\\u201con or after 1 July 2027\\\\u201d (stated)\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"Pre-commencement period\\\",\\\"1 Mar 2019 \\\\u2013 31 May 2019 = 3 months\\\",\\\"3 months\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"Buildout Period\\\",\\\"15 May 2020 \\\\u2013 30 Sep 2020 = 4 months 16 days\\\",\\\"\\\\u201capproximately four and one-half months\\\\u201d\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"**Engagement Letter**\\\",\\\"**Due diligence period**\\\",\\\"Commences 16 Nov 2024; expires 31 Jan 2025 = **76 days elapsed** (77 counting both endpoints). 77 days runs from the **PSA date of 15 Nov 2024**\\\",\\\"**\\\\u201ca period of seventy-seven (77) days\\\\u201d**\\\",\\\"**\\\\u2717 inconsistent**\\\"],\\n [\\\"Engagement Letter\\\",\\\"Report delivery \\\\\\\"approximately six weeks\\\\\\\" before DD expiry\\\",\\\"20 Dec 2024 to 31 Jan 2025 = 42 days = 6.0 weeks\\\",\\\"\\\\u201capproximately six (6) weeks\\\\u201d\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Engagement Letter\\\",\\\"Lease files due 6 Dec 2024\\\",\\\"Letter dated 5 Dec 2024 \\\\u2014 one day after the letter\\\",\\\"6 Dec 2024\\\",\\\"Note: tight\\\"],\\n [\\\"PSA / closing\\\",\\\"DD expiry to target closing\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2025 to 15 Mar 2025 = 43 days\\\",\\\"15 Mar 2025\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Document\\\",\\\"Date or period checked\\\",\\\"Our recomputation\\\",\\\"Stated in document\\\",\\\"Result\\\"], rows,\\n          [0.85,1.55,2.1,1.35,0.85], size=7.4, head_size=7.2, align_center_cols=(4,),\\n          row_fills=[None]*19+[WARN,None,None,None], keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"One inconsistency was found, in the Engagement Letter rather than in any lease: a due diligence period that commences on 16 November 2024 and expires on 31 January 2025 is 76 days, not 77. A 77-day period runs from the PSA execution date of 15 November 2024. Because the due diligence expiry drives every deadline in Section 8, the contractual expiry should be confirmed against the PSA itself (Risk R-22).\\\")\\nPYEOF\\necho ok\"}"}], "input_tokens": 214289, "output_tokens": 4882, "finish_reason": "completed"}
