astern, every year except one follows the preceding year's stated rate times the stated factor, to the cent. This is consistent with a table built by formula and then manually overwritten in one cell, or built by hand and mis-keyed once.\\\",\\n \\\"**The error always runs in the landlord's disfavour except at Southeastern.** Apex and BrightPath state less rent than the mechanism produces (a tenant benefit); Southeastern states more (a landlord benefit, though one a tenant could dispute).\\\",\\n \\\"**Two leases contain provisions that make the question operative.** Apex \\\\u00a7 4.3 prescribes the calculation method in the body of the lease and states that the rate is \\\\u201ccalculated by multiplying the Base Rent per RSF for the immediately preceding Lease Year by 1.03\\\\u201d \\\\u2014 so the mechanism, not the table, arguably governs. Southeastern \\\\u00a7 4.1 does the opposite and provides that **Exhibit B controls** in the event of conflict \\\\u2014 so the table, not the mechanism, arguably governs there. The two leases therefore resolve the same type of discrepancy in opposite directions, which is a useful reminder that this is a drafting issue and not a data-entry one.\\\",\\n \\\"**No lease contains a reconciliation or true-up mechanism** that would allow either party to correct an error in the schedule after the fact. The remedy is an estoppel, an amendment, or an agreement at closing.\\\",\\n], size=9.2)\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"6.4  Date and notice-period verification\\\")\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"Commencement + 10 years = Expiration\\\",\\\"1 Jun 2019 + 10 yrs = 31 May 2029\\\",\\\"31 May 2029\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto\\\",\\\"Commencement + 7 years = Expiration\\\",\\\"1 Nov 2021 + 7 yrs = 31 Oct 2028\\\",\\\"31 Oct 2028\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"BrightPath\\\",\\\"Commencement + 15 years = Expiration\\\",\\\"1 Apr 2017 + 15 yrs = 31 Mar 2032\\\",\\\"31 Mar 2032\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Southeastern\\\",\\\"Commencement + 10 years = Expiration\\\",\\\"1 Jul 2014 + 10 yrs = 30 Jun 2024\\\",\\\"30 Jun 2024\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"Commencement + 10 years = Expiration\\\",\\\"1 Jul 2022 + 10 yrs = 30 Jun 2032\\\",\\\"30 Jun 2032\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"Commencement + 10 years = Expiration\\\",\\\"1 Oct 2020 + 10 yrs = 30 Sep 2030\\\",\\\"30 Sep 2030\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"GSA\\\",\\\"Firm term 5 years + soft term 5 years\\\",\\\"1 Jan 2021 + 5 = 31 Dec 2025; + 5 = 31 Dec 2030\\\",\\\"31 Dec 2025 / 31 Dec 2030\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"First renewal notice: 12 months before expiry\\\",\\\"31 May 2029 \\\\u2212 12 months = 31 May 2028\\\",\\\"31 May 2028 (stated)\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto\\\",\\\"Renewal notice: 9 months before expiry\\\",\\\"31 Oct 2028 \\\\u2212 9 months = 31 Jan 2028\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2028 (stated)\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto\\\",\\\"Early termination notice: 6 months before effective date\\\",\\\"31 Oct 2025 \\\\u2212 6 months = 30 Apr 2025\\\",\\\"30 Apr 2025 (stated)\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Southeastern\\\",\\\"Renewal notice: 90 days before expiry\\\",\\\"30 Jun 2024 \\\\u2212 90 days = 1 Apr 2024\\\",\\\"1 Apr 2024 (stated)\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"BrightPath\\\",\\\"First renewal notice: 12 months before expiry\\\",\\\"31 Mar 2032 \\\\u2212 12 months = 31 Mar 2031\\\",\\\"not stated\\\",\\\"Computed\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"First renewal notice: 12 months before expiry\\\",\\\"30 Jun 2032 \\\\u2212 12 months = 30 Jun 2031\\\",\\\"not stated\\\",\\\"Computed\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"First renewal notice: 9 months before expiry\\\",\\\"30 Sep 2030 \\\\u2212 9 months = 31 Dec 2029\\\",\\\"not stated\\\",\\\"Computed\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"Guaranty burn-off\\\",\\\"Earlier of 30 Sep 2025 or $2,000,000 TTM sales\\\",\\\"30 Sep 2025 (stated)\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"Expansion window: Lease Years 3 to 5\\\",\\\"1 Jul 2024 \\\\u2013 30 Jun 2027\\\",\\\"1 Jul 2024 \\\\u2013 30 Jun 2027 (stated)\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"Contraction: after Lease Year 5, 9 months' notice\\\",\\\"Notice available on/after 1 Jul 2027; earliest contraction 1 Apr 2028\\\",\\\"\\\\u201con or after 1 July 2027\\\\u201d (stated)\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"Pre-commencement period\\\",\\\"1 Mar 2019 \\\\u2013 31 May 2019 = 3 months\\\",\\\"3 months\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"Buildout Period\\\",\\\"15 May 2020 \\\\u2013 30 Sep 2020 = 4 months 16 days\\\",\\\"\\\\u201capproximately four and one-half months\\\\u201d\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"**Engagement Letter**\\\",\\\"**Due diligence period**\\\",\\\"Commences 16 Nov 2024; expires 31 Jan 2025 = **76 days elapsed** (77 counting both endpoints). 77 days runs from the **PSA date of 15 Nov 2024**\\\",\\\"**\\\\u201ca period of seventy-seven (77) days\\\\u201d**\\\",\\\"**\\\\u2717 inconsistent**\\\"],\\n [\\\"Engagement Letter\\\",\\\"Report delivery \\\\\\\"approximately six weeks\\\\\\\" before DD expiry\\\",\\\"20 Dec 2024 to 31 Jan 2025 = 42 days = 6.0 weeks\\\",\\\"\\\\u201capproximately six (6) weeks\\\\u201d\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n [\\\"Engagement Letter\\\",\\\"Lease files due 6 Dec 2024\\\",\\\"Letter dated 5 Dec 2024 \\\\u2014 one day after the letter\\\",\\\"6 Dec 2024\\\",\\\"Note: tight\\\"],\\n [\\\"PSA / closing\\\",\\\"DD expiry to target closing\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2025 to 15 Mar 2025 = 43 days\\\",\\\"15 Mar 2025\\\",\\\"\\\\u2713\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Document\\\",\\\"Date or period checked\\\",\\\"Our recomputation\\\",\\\"Stated in document\\\",\\\"Result\\\"], rows,\\n          [0.85,1.55,2.1,1.35,0.85], size=7.4, head_size=7.2, align_center_cols=(4,),\\n          row_fills=[None]*19+[WARN,None,None,None], keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"One inconsistency was found, in the Engagement Letter rather than in any lease: a due diligence period that commences on 16 November 2024 and expires on 31 January 2025 is 76 days, not 77. A 77-day period runs from the PSA execution date of 15 November 2024. Because the due diligence expiry drives every deadline in Section 8, the contractual expiry should be confirmed against the PSA itself (Risk R-22).\\\")\\nPYEOF\\necho ok\"}", "result": "ok\n"}
{"turn": 35, "role": "assistant", "text": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_jzEA2tznfY6tzJJnIFyP6228", "name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && cat >> work/build.py <<'PYEOF'\\n\\n# ================= 7. RISK REGISTER =================\\nh1(doc, \\\"SECTION 7\\\", \\\"Risk Register\\\")\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"7.1  Rating scales\\\", space_before=2)\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"**Critical**\\\",\\\"Threatens the transaction itself or a material portion of value; requires resolution before the due diligence period expires.\\\",\\\"Immediate\\\",\\\"Action required now, without waiting for the Report.\\\"],\\n [\\\"**High**\\\",\\\"Material effect on value, closing mechanics or lender requirements; requires a negotiated protection or documented position before closing.\\\",\\\"Pre-DD expiry\\\",\\\"Before 31 January 2025.\\\"],\\n [\\\"**Medium**\\\",\\\"Requires verification, documentation or a conservative assumption; modest value effect.\\\",\\\"Pre-closing\\\",\\\"Before 15 March 2025.\\\"],\\n [\\\"**Low**\\\",\\\"Presentational, administrative, immaterial in amount, or matters to be monitored after closing.\\\",\\\"Post-closing\\\",\\\"On an ongoing basis once complete.\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Severity\\\",\\\"Meaning\\\",\\\"Timing band\\\",\\\"Meaning\\\"], rows, [0.85,2.9,0.85,2.1], size=7.8, head_size=7.6, keep_rows=True)\\npara(doc, \\\"Twenty-six items are registered. One is Critical, nine are High, nine are Medium and seven are Low. Severity is our assessment of the effect on Galleon's position; the timing band indicates when the item must be actioned, not how serious it is \\\\u2014 several High items fall into the pre-closing band because the closing is the last opportunity to obtain the protection.\\\", size=9.8, space_before=4)\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"7.2  Critical and High severity items\\\")\\ndef risk_table(doc, rows):\\n    add_table(doc, [\\\"ID\\\",\\\"Finding and consequence\\\",\\\"Severity\\\",\\\"Timing\\\",\\\"Required action\\\"], rows,\\n              [0.42,2.86,0.66,0.74,2.02], size=7.3, head_size=7.2,\\n              align_center_cols=(0,2,3),\\n              row_fills=[WARN if r[2]==\\\"Critical\\\" else AMBER for r in rows], keep_rows=True)\\n\\nrisk_table(doc, [\\n [\\\"R-01\\\",\\\"**Apex ROFR over Building C may have been triggered by this acquisition.** Article XIII requires the Seller, before accepting or executing any agreement with a third party, to deliver a ROFR Notice where the offer covers Building C \\\\u2014 expressly including a sale as part of a portfolio transaction. The PSA was executed on 15 November 2024 for a portfolio containing Building C. If triggered and unwaived, Apex has 30 days to elect to buy Building C at an allocable price set by the Seller in good faith (disputable before an MAI appraiser), and the ROFR reinstates if the Seller does not close within 180 days. A memorandum may have been recorded.\\\",\\\"Critical\\\",\\\"Immediate\\\",\\\"Obtain: (i) any ROFR Notice delivered and Apex's response; (ii) a written waiver and estoppel from Apex; (iii) a Mecklenburg County search for a recorded memorandum of ROFR; (iv) a Seller representation and specific indemnity in the PSA. Confirm the deal structure \\\\u2013 an equity transfer may not constitute a sale of Building C.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-02\\\",\\\"**GSA lease cannot be assigned and is senior to any mortgage.** Section 8 bars the Lessor from assigning or delegating without the Contracting Officer's prior written consent and requires 30 days' notice of any building transfer and a written assumption. Section 16 provides the lease is **not** subordinate to any mortgage and bars the Lessor from granting a priority mortgage without federal consent.\\\",\\\"High\\\",\\\"Immediate\\\",\\\"Confirm structure. If asset-level, open a consent/novation dialogue with GSA Region 4 now and make it a closing condition. Require Fieldstone to confirm the lending approach to Section 16 before the financing commitment; obtain a Government SNDA if required.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-03\\\",\\\"**20.1% of aggregate rent has only twelve months of firm term.** The GSA firm term ends 31 December 2025; thereafter the Government may terminate on 120 days' notice with no fee or penalty. Soft-term rent of $2,546,100 is expressly contingent on continued occupancy. The Rent Roll nevertheless includes the full $472,500 in the aggregate.\\\",\\\"High\\\",\\\"Pre-DD expiry\\\",\\\"Value the GSA tenancy on 12 months of firm rent plus a probability-weighted soft term; do not capitalise soft-term rent. Ask Seller for any GSA renewal, expansion or relocation signal, and for recent Contracting Officer correspondence.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-04\\\",\\\"**Southeastern holds over at will \\\\u2014 13.0% of aggregate rent.** The term expired on 30 June 2024 and the renewal option lapsed on 1 April 2024. Either party may terminate on 30 days' notice. There is no deposit, guaranty or letter of credit.\\\",\\\"High\\\",\\\"Pre-closing\\\",\\\"Obtain a new lease or a holdover acknowledgement fixing a 12 to 24 month term, contractual rent and a restriction on termination; establish the tenant's intention to remain. If not obtained, value the space on a short-term at-will basis with a re-letting and downtime allowance.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-05\\\",\\\"**Dr. Soto early termination \\\\u2014 net exposure approximately $264,143.** Notice must be given by **30 April 2025**, 46 days after the target closing date, with a $40,657.14 payment, for a termination effective 31 October 2025. Remaining rent at risk is $304,800.\\\",\\\"High\\\",\\\"Pre-DD expiry\\\",\\\"Obtain an estoppel confirming no termination notice has been delivered and no present intention to terminate. Seek a PSA covenant and indemnity from Seller, a closing holdback, or a direct waiver or amendment with the tenant before closing.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-06\\\",\\\"**Verdana expansion option encumbers the 9th floor.** 18,500 RSF (12.3% of the building) at the then-current 8th-floor rate \\\\u2014 $36.07/RSF in Year 3, escalating 3% \\\\u2014 with a $740,000 allowance and a term coterminous to 30 June 2032. The window is open from 1 July 2024 to 30 June 2027 on 6 months' notice, and the Lessor has no right to refuse.\\\",\\\"High\\\",\\\"Pre-DD expiry\\\",\\\"Obtain an estoppel confirming the option has not been exercised and any notice given; confirm the 9th floor is vacant and deliverable (if it is leased to a third party the Lessor may be unable to perform); quantify the below-market exposure and seek a price adjustment or a negotiated waiver.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-07\\\",\\\"**Pint & Platter co-tenancy right cannot be tested.** If occupancy of the 62,000 RSF centre falls below 70% of leasable area for more than 180 consecutive days, the tenant may reduce Base Rent to 75% or terminate on 60 days' notice. Occupancy of the centre as a whole is not disclosed in the documents provided.\\\",\\\"High\\\",\\\"Pre-DD expiry\\\",\\\"Obtain the full Haywood Village Shops rent roll and an occupancy certificate as at closing, plus an estoppel confirming that no Co-Tenancy Failure has occurred, is continuing, or has been waived.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-08\\\",\\\"**Exclusive-use covenants restrict re-letting across three properties.** Apex bars any logistics, distribution or warehouse user from Buildings A, B **and** C until 2029 (plus renewals); BrightPath bars a second childcare operator at Millbrook Medical Plaza; Pint & Platter bars another full-service restaurant above 2,000 RSF at Haywood Village Shops.\\\",\\\"High\\\",\\\"Pre-DD expiry\\\",\\\"Obtain the Distribution Center and Haywood rent rolls to test present compliance (a current breach would give the tenant leverage). Factor each restriction into the business plan and any re-letting assumption; consider whether a waiver is commercially available.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-09\\\",\\\"**Five of seven leases impose no estoppel obligation.** Only Apex (10 business days, with deemed acknowledgment) and Verdana (15 business days) require an estoppel. For Soto, BrightPath, Southeastern, Pint & Platter and GSA, Galleon has no contractual right to one.\\\",\\\"High\\\",\\\"Pre-DD expiry\\\",\\\"Make estoppels from all seven tenants an express PSA closing condition, in the form set out in Section 9, with a Seller cure obligation and a purchase price remedy for non-delivery.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-25\\\",\\\"**AFFF and PFAS materials are expressly permitted on the Southeastern premises.** Article 14 allows storage, handling and use of aqueous film-forming foam, foam concentrates and PFAS-containing materials; requires $1,000,000 pollution legal liability cover; and gives a broad indemnity that survives termination \\\\u2014 but no security for it.\\\",\\\"High\\\",\\\"Immediate\\\",\\\"Refer Unit 12 to Hanover for a targeted assessment, including PFAS sampling if a Phase I identifies a recognised environmental condition. Obtain the tenant's pollution legal liability certificate, the historical inventory and safety data sheets. Seek a Seller environmental indemnity with a survival period and an escrow, and consider a tenant guaranty for the indemnity.\\\"],\\n])\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"7.3  Medium severity items\\\")\\nrisk_table(doc, [\\n [\\\"R-10\\\",\\\"**No SNDA on file for any lease, and three leases are structurally incompatible with customary lender requirements.** Apex and Southeastern are self-operative subordination with no non-disturbance. Verdana's subordination is expressly conditioned on delivery of an SNDA. The GSA lease is senior to any mortgage.\\\",\\\"Medium\\\",\\\"Pre-closing\\\",\\\"Have Fieldstone confirm required lender deliverables before commitment. Obtain SNDAs where needed from any existing lender and, for Apex and Southeastern, a tripartite non-disturbance from the new lender. Re-test Verdana \\\\u00a7 17.02 (no mortgage as at February 2022).\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-11\\\",\\\"**Weighted average remaining term overstated by approximately 0.4 years.** Rent Roll states ~5.7 years (soft) and ~4.6 years (firm); recomputation gives **5.25** and **4.25** years.\\\",\\\"Medium\\\",\\\"Pre-DD expiry\\\",\\\"Use the recomputed figures in the valuation and hold-period model; ask the property manager to explain the methodology so the discrepancy is documented.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-12\\\",\\\"**Southeastern Year 10 rate departs from the stated 2% mechanism** \\\\u2014 $9.25 stated against $8.97 computed. Base rent overstated by $6,160 and holdover rent by $9,240 per annum. Section 4.1 makes Exhibit B controlling, so $9.25 probably governs, but the tenant could argue the formula.\\\",\\\"Medium\\\",\\\"Pre-closing\\\",\\\"Reconcile to the 2023\\\\u201324 billing ledger and the holdover invoices; resolve by estoppel or amendment. Because this drives 13.0% of aggregate rent, the actual billed figure should be established rather than resolved by construction.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-13\\\",\\\"**BrightPath Year 8 rate departs from the stated 2.5% mechanism** \\\\u2014 $25.90 against $26.15 \\\\u2014 and the error compounds to the end of the term. Current year understated by $1,450; cumulative $12,470. It also lowers the Year 15 base from which the first renewal rent cap is calculated.\\\",\\\"Medium\\\",\\\"Pre-closing\\\",\\\"Reconcile to current billing; correct by amendment or reflect the correct figure in the estoppel; adjust the renewal cap assumption in the model.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-14\\\",\\\"**Pint & Platter percentage-rent breakpoint conflict.** Section 3.3 and Exhibit B fix the Breakpoint at $1,350,000; Article 1 defines a Natural Breakpoint of Base Rent \\\\u00f7 6%, which is $1,489,767 in Year 5 \\\\u2014 a $139,767 difference in sales and roughly $8,386 per annum at the margin.\\\",\\\"Medium\\\",\\\"Pre-closing\\\",\\\"Estoppel confirming the breakpoint applied in practice, together with the percentage rent actually paid for Lease Years 2 to 5 and the certified gross sales statements.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-16\\\",\\\"**GSA holdover and re-letting risk.** Holdover continues at the base rent with no premium, and the Lessor expressly waives holdover rent and damages. The Government may remove improvements within 60 days and has no restoration obligation beyond structural damage; SCIF space cannot be inspected; abandoned improvements may be unusable.\\\",\\\"Medium\\\",\\\"Pre-closing\\\",\\\"Obtain a condition report on the premises within SCIF access limits; budget for re-letting and restoration; seek a Seller indemnity for post-closing restoration and a termination-right notice obligation.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-17\\\",\\\"**Verdana contraction option over up to 5,000 RSF (26.7% of the premises).** Available after Lease Year 5 on 9 months' notice; the fee is roughly $239,000 on an illustrative basis against a rent loss of about $197,000 per annum.\\\",\\\"Medium\\\",\\\"Post-closing\\\",\\\"Model the option in the downside case; estoppel confirming no notice has been given; consider whether the fee adequately compensates for the rent loss and re-letting cost.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-19\\\",\\\"**Four leases do not state the denominator for the recovery share** (Soto, BrightPath, Southeastern, GSA), and the two Millbrook leases use different measurement standards (BOMA 2017 against BOMA 2010) in the same building. Recovery percentages for those tenants could not be verified.\\\",\\\"Medium\\\",\\\"Pre-DD expiry\\\",\\\"Obtain building and park RSF confirmations and the base-year statements; reconcile 2024 recoveries tenant by tenant; confirm the GSA share (10.00% if the building is 150,000 RSF) and the 2021 GSA base-year statement due by 31 March 2022.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-21\\\",\\\"**Credit support is absent where concentration is highest.** Apex (23.7%) and Verdana (28.8%) have no deposit, letter of credit or guaranty; Southeastern (13.0%) likewise. The Pint & Platter guaranty burns off on the earlier of 30 September 2025 or $2,000,000 trailing-twelve-month sales.\\\",\\\"Medium\\\",\\\"Pre-closing\\\",\\\"Obtain current financial statements for Apex, Verdana and Southeastern; obtain certified trailing-twelve-month gross sales and any release for Pint & Platter. Consider a guaranty, letter of credit or escrow as a closing requirement, or a corresponding price adjustment.\\\"],\\n])\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"7.4  Low severity items\\\")\\nrisk_table(doc, [\\n [\\\"R-15\\\",\\\"**BrightPath security deposit amount is unexplained.** $25,440 is described as two months' Base Rent but equals $25,036.67 at the current rate and $21,266.67 at the Year 1 rate; it corresponds to a rate of $26.317/RSF, which appears nowhere in the schedule.\\\",\\\"Low\\\",\\\"Pre-closing\\\",\\\"Obtain the deposit ledger; confirm the amount held; arrange transfer to Galleon or a purchase price credit as a closing proration.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-18\\\",\\\"**Apex renewal options are lost together.** Failure to give the first notice by 31 May 2028 forfeits the second option as well, and both options are personal to Apex and void on assignment.\\\",\\\"Low\\\",\\\"Post-closing\\\",\\\"Diarise 31 May 2028; reflect the renewal structure in the hold-period model; note the options would be lost on any assignment of the Apex lease.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-20\\\",\\\"**Apex Year 5 rate departs from the stated 3% mechanism** \\\\u2014 $6.180 against $6.190 \\\\u2014 carrying forward at about $0.006/RSF. Understates current rent by $525 and the term by $3,500.\\\",\\\"Low\\\",\\\"Post-closing\\\",\\\"Record in the reconciliation; no economic action required.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-22\\\",\\\"**Engagement Letter due diligence period stated as 77 days** but is 76 days measured from the stated commencement date of 16 November 2024 (77 days runs from the PSA date of 15 November 2024).\\\",\\\"Low\\\",\\\"Immediate\\\",\\\"Confirm the contractual due diligence expiry against the PSA and diarise every deadline in Section 8 against the confirmed date.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-23\\\",\\\"**Lease-file completeness and document hygiene.** No amendments, side letters, commencement date memoranda, estoppels or SNDAs were provided for any lease. The BrightPath document retains a Word field placeholder; the Verdana rules contain a typographical error; the Apex rounding note does not match its figures.\\\",\\\"Low\\\",\\\"Pre-closing\\\",\\\"Obtain a Seller certification that each lease file is complete and that no side letter, amendment or unrecorded agreement exists; obtain the commencement date memoranda that the Verdana lease required under \\\\u00a7 3.04, and any others that exist.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-24\\\",\\\"**The Apex lease contains no casualty or condemnation article.** There is no express rent abatement, repair obligation or termination right on damage or taking.\\\",\\\"Low\\\",\\\"Pre-DD expiry\\\",\\\"Confirm with Seller whether an amendment supplies these provisions; otherwise note that North Carolina law and the PSA govern, and disclose the position to the lender if it requires casualty provisions.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-26\\\",\\\"**The Soto Base Year of calendar 2022 falls inside the lease term**, so the tenant's recovery obligation begins from a base that already reflects a full year of its own occupancy \\\\u2014 a drag on recoveries relative to a pre-commencement base year.\\\",\\\"Low\\\",\\\"Pre-closing\\\",\\\"Obtain the 2022 base-year operating expense statement and model recoveries on the true incremental basis.\\\"],\\n])\\nPYEOF\\necho ok\"}"}], "input_tokens": 219185, "output_tokens": 7113, "finish_reason": "completed"}
{"turn": 35, "role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call_00_jzEA2tznfY6tzJJnIFyP6228", "tool_name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && cat >> work/build.py <<'PYEOF'\\n\\n# ================= 7. RISK REGISTER =================\\nh1(doc, \\\"SECTION 7\\\", \\\"Risk Register\\\")\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"7.1  Rating scales\\\", space_before=2)\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"**Critical**\\\",\\\"Threatens the transaction itself or a material portion of value; requires resolution before the due diligence period expires.\\\",\\\"Immediate\\\",\\\"Action required now, without waiting for the Report.\\\"],\\n [\\\"**High**\\\",\\\"Material effect on value, closing mechanics or lender requirements; requires a negotiated protection or documented position before closing.\\\",\\\"Pre-DD expiry\\\",\\\"Before 31 January 2025.\\\"],\\n [\\\"**Medium**\\\",\\\"Requires verification, documentation or a conservative assumption; modest value effect.\\\",\\\"Pre-closing\\\",\\\"Before 15 March 2025.\\\"],\\n [\\\"**Low**\\\",\\\"Presentational, administrative, immaterial in amount, or matters to be monitored after closing.\\\",\\\"Post-closing\\\",\\\"On an ongoing basis once complete.\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Severity\\\",\\\"Meaning\\\",\\\"Timing band\\\",\\\"Meaning\\\"], rows, [0.85,2.9,0.85,2.1], size=7.8, head_size=7.6, keep_rows=True)\\npara(doc, \\\"Twenty-six items are registered. One is Critical, nine are High, nine are Medium and seven are Low. Severity is our assessment of the effect on Galleon's position; the timing band indicates when the item must be actioned, not how serious it is \\\\u2014 several High items fall into the pre-closing band because the closing is the last opportunity to obtain the protection.\\\", size=9.8, space_before=4)\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"7.2  Critical and High severity items\\\")\\ndef risk_table(doc, rows):\\n    add_table(doc, [\\\"ID\\\",\\\"Finding and consequence\\\",\\\"Severity\\\",\\\"Timing\\\",\\\"Required action\\\"], rows,\\n              [0.42,2.86,0.66,0.74,2.02], size=7.3, head_size=7.2,\\n              align_center_cols=(0,2,3),\\n              row_fills=[WARN if r[2]==\\\"Critical\\\" else AMBER for r in rows], keep_rows=True)\\n\\nrisk_table(doc, [\\n [\\\"R-01\\\",\\\"**Apex ROFR over Building C may have been triggered by this acquisition.** Article XIII requires the Seller, before accepting or executing any agreement with a third party, to deliver a ROFR Notice where the offer covers Building C \\\\u2014 expressly including a sale as part of a portfolio transaction. The PSA was executed on 15 November 2024 for a portfolio containing Building C. If triggered and unwaived, Apex has 30 days to elect to buy Building C at an allocable price set by the Seller in good faith (disputable before an MAI appraiser), and the ROFR reinstates if the Seller does not close within 180 days. A memorandum may have been recorded.\\\",\\\"Critical\\\",\\\"Immediate\\\",\\\"Obtain: (i) any ROFR Notice delivered and Apex's response; (ii) a written waiver and estoppel from Apex; (iii) a Mecklenburg County search for a recorded memorandum of ROFR; (iv) a Seller representation and specific indemnity in the PSA. Confirm the deal structure \\\\u2013 an equity transfer may not constitute a sale of Building C.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-02\\\",\\\"**GSA lease cannot be assigned and is senior to any mortgage.** Section 8 bars the Lessor from assigning or delegating without the Contracting Officer's prior written consent and requires 30 days' notice of any building transfer and a written assumption. Section 16 provides the lease is **not** subordinate to any mortgage and bars the Lessor from granting a priority mortgage without federal consent.\\\",\\\"High\\\",\\\"Immediate\\\",\\\"Confirm structure. If asset-level, open a consent/novation dialogue with GSA Region 4 now and make it a closing condition. Require Fieldstone to confirm the lending approach to Section 16 before the financing commitment; obtain a Government SNDA if required.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-03\\\",\\\"**20.1% of aggregate rent has only twelve months of firm term.** The GSA firm term ends 31 December 2025; thereafter the Government may terminate on 120 days' notice with no fee or penalty. Soft-term rent of $2,546,100 is expressly contingent on continued occupancy. The Rent Roll nevertheless includes the full $472,500 in the aggregate.\\\",\\\"High\\\",\\\"Pre-DD expiry\\\",\\\"Value the GSA tenancy on 12 months of firm rent plus a probability-weighted soft term; do not capitalise soft-term rent. Ask Seller for any GSA renewal, expansion or relocation signal, and for recent Contracting Officer correspondence.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-04\\\",\\\"**Southeastern holds over at will \\\\u2014 13.0% of aggregate rent.** The term expired on 30 June 2024 and the renewal option lapsed on 1 April 2024. Either party may terminate on 30 days' notice. There is no deposit, guaranty or letter of credit.\\\",\\\"High\\\",\\\"Pre-closing\\\",\\\"Obtain a new lease or a holdover acknowledgement fixing a 12 to 24 month term, contractual rent and a restriction on termination; establish the tenant's intention to remain. If not obtained, value the space on a short-term at-will basis with a re-letting and downtime allowance.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-05\\\",\\\"**Dr. Soto early termination \\\\u2014 net exposure approximately $264,143.** Notice must be given by **30 April 2025**, 46 days after the target closing date, with a $40,657.14 payment, for a termination effective 31 October 2025. Remaining rent at risk is $304,800.\\\",\\\"High\\\",\\\"Pre-DD expiry\\\",\\\"Obtain an estoppel confirming no termination notice has been delivered and no present intention to terminate. Seek a PSA covenant and indemnity from Seller, a closing holdback, or a direct waiver or amendment with the tenant before closing.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-06\\\",\\\"**Verdana expansion option encumbers the 9th floor.** 18,500 RSF (12.3% of the building) at the then-current 8th-floor rate \\\\u2014 $36.07/RSF in Year 3, escalating 3% \\\\u2014 with a $740,000 allowance and a term coterminous to 30 June 2032. The window is open from 1 July 2024 to 30 June 2027 on 6 months' notice, and the Lessor has no right to refuse.\\\",\\\"High\\\",\\\"Pre-DD expiry\\\",\\\"Obtain an estoppel confirming the option has not been exercised and any notice given; confirm the 9th floor is vacant and deliverable (if it is leased to a third party the Lessor may be unable to perform); quantify the below-market exposure and seek a price adjustment or a negotiated waiver.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-07\\\",\\\"**Pint & Platter co-tenancy right cannot be tested.** If occupancy of the 62,000 RSF centre falls below 70% of leasable area for more than 180 consecutive days, the tenant may reduce Base Rent to 75% or terminate on 60 days' notice. Occupancy of the centre as a whole is not disclosed in the documents provided.\\\",\\\"High\\\",\\\"Pre-DD expiry\\\",\\\"Obtain the full Haywood Village Shops rent roll and an occupancy certificate as at closing, plus an estoppel confirming that no Co-Tenancy Failure has occurred, is continuing, or has been waived.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-08\\\",\\\"**Exclusive-use covenants restrict re-letting across three properties.** Apex bars any logistics, distribution or warehouse user from Buildings A, B **and** C until 2029 (plus renewals); BrightPath bars a second childcare operator at Millbrook Medical Plaza; Pint & Platter bars another full-service restaurant above 2,000 RSF at Haywood Village Shops.\\\",\\\"High\\\",\\\"Pre-DD expiry\\\",\\\"Obtain the Distribution Center and Haywood rent rolls to test present compliance (a current breach would give the tenant leverage). Factor each restriction into the business plan and any re-letting assumption; consider whether a waiver is commercially available.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-09\\\",\\\"**Five of seven leases impose no estoppel obligation.** Only Apex (10 business days, with deemed acknowledgment) and Verdana (15 business days) require an estoppel. For Soto, BrightPath, Southeastern, Pint & Platter and GSA, Galleon has no contractual right to one.\\\",\\\"High\\\",\\\"Pre-DD expiry\\\",\\\"Make estoppels from all seven tenants an express PSA closing condition, in the form set out in Section 9, with a Seller cure obligation and a purchase price remedy for non-delivery.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-25\\\",\\\"**AFFF and PFAS materials are expressly permitted on the Southeastern premises.** Article 14 allows storage, handling and use of aqueous film-forming foam, foam concentrates and PFAS-containing materials; requires $1,000,000 pollution legal liability cover; and gives a broad indemnity that survives termination \\\\u2014 but no security for it.\\\",\\\"High\\\",\\\"Immediate\\\",\\\"Refer Unit 12 to Hanover for a targeted assessment, including PFAS sampling if a Phase I identifies a recognised environmental condition. Obtain the tenant's pollution legal liability certificate, the historical inventory and safety data sheets. Seek a Seller environmental indemnity with a survival period and an escrow, and consider a tenant guaranty for the indemnity.\\\"],\\n])\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"7.3  Medium severity items\\\")\\nrisk_table(doc, [\\n [\\\"R-10\\\",\\\"**No SNDA on file for any lease, and three leases are structurally incompatible with customary lender requirements.** Apex and Southeastern are self-operative subordination with no non-disturbance. Verdana's subordination is expressly conditioned on delivery of an SNDA. The GSA lease is senior to any mortgage.\\\",\\\"Medium\\\",\\\"Pre-closing\\\",\\\"Have Fieldstone confirm required lender deliverables before commitment. Obtain SNDAs where needed from any existing lender and, for Apex and Southeastern, a tripartite non-disturbance from the new lender. Re-test Verdana \\\\u00a7 17.02 (no mortgage as at February 2022).\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-11\\\",\\\"**Weighted average remaining term overstated by approximately 0.4 years.** Rent Roll states ~5.7 years (soft) and ~4.6 years (firm); recomputation gives **5.25** and **4.25** years.\\\",\\\"Medium\\\",\\\"Pre-DD expiry\\\",\\\"Use the recomputed figures in the valuation and hold-period model; ask the property manager to explain the methodology so the discrepancy is documented.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-12\\\",\\\"**Southeastern Year 10 rate departs from the stated 2% mechanism** \\\\u2014 $9.25 stated against $8.97 computed. Base rent overstated by $6,160 and holdover rent by $9,240 per annum. Section 4.1 makes Exhibit B controlling, so $9.25 probably governs, but the tenant could argue the formula.\\\",\\\"Medium\\\",\\\"Pre-closing\\\",\\\"Reconcile to the 2023\\\\u201324 billing ledger and the holdover invoices; resolve by estoppel or amendment. Because this drives 13.0% of aggregate rent, the actual billed figure should be established rather than resolved by construction.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-13\\\",\\\"**BrightPath Year 8 rate departs from the stated 2.5% mechanism** \\\\u2014 $25.90 against $26.15 \\\\u2014 and the error compounds to the end of the term. Current year understated by $1,450; cumulative $12,470. It also lowers the Year 15 base from which the first renewal rent cap is calculated.\\\",\\\"Medium\\\",\\\"Pre-closing\\\",\\\"Reconcile to current billing; correct by amendment or reflect the correct figure in the estoppel; adjust the renewal cap assumption in the model.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-14\\\",\\\"**Pint & Platter percentage-rent breakpoint conflict.** Section 3.3 and Exhibit B fix the Breakpoint at $1,350,000; Article 1 defines a Natural Breakpoint of Base Rent \\\\u00f7 6%, which is $1,489,767 in Year 5 \\\\u2014 a $139,767 difference in sales and roughly $8,386 per annum at the margin.\\\",\\\"Medium\\\",\\\"Pre-closing\\\",\\\"Estoppel confirming the breakpoint applied in practice, together with the percentage rent actually paid for Lease Years 2 to 5 and the certified gross sales statements.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-16\\\",\\\"**GSA holdover and re-letting risk.** Holdover continues at the base rent with no premium, and the Lessor expressly waives holdover rent and damages. The Government may remove improvements within 60 days and has no restoration obligation beyond structural damage; SCIF space cannot be inspected; abandoned improvements may be unusable.\\\",\\\"Medium\\\",\\\"Pre-closing\\\",\\\"Obtain a condition report on the premises within SCIF access limits; budget for re-letting and restoration; seek a Seller indemnity for post-closing restoration and a termination-right notice obligation.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-17\\\",\\\"**Verdana contraction option over up to 5,000 RSF (26.7% of the premises).** Available after Lease Year 5 on 9 months' notice; the fee is roughly $239,000 on an illustrative basis against a rent loss of about $197,000 per annum.\\\",\\\"Medium\\\",\\\"Post-closing\\\",\\\"Model the option in the downside case; estoppel confirming no notice has been given; consider whether the fee adequately compensates for the rent loss and re-letting cost.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-19\\\",\\\"**Four leases do not state the denominator for the recovery share** (Soto, BrightPath, Southeastern, GSA), and the two Millbrook leases use different measurement standards (BOMA 2017 against BOMA 2010) in the same building. Recovery percentages for those tenants could not be verified.\\\",\\\"Medium\\\",\\\"Pre-DD expiry\\\",\\\"Obtain building and park RSF confirmations and the base-year statements; reconcile 2024 recoveries tenant by tenant; confirm the GSA share (10.00% if the building is 150,000 RSF) and the 2021 GSA base-year statement due by 31 March 2022.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-21\\\",\\\"**Credit support is absent where concentration is highest.** Apex (23.7%) and Verdana (28.8%) have no deposit, letter of credit or guaranty; Southeastern (13.0%) likewise. The Pint & Platter guaranty burns off on the earlier of 30 September 2025 or $2,000,000 trailing-twelve-month sales.\\\",\\\"Medium\\\",\\\"Pre-closing\\\",\\\"Obtain current financial statements for Apex, Verdana and Southeastern; obtain certified trailing-twelve-month gross sales and any release for Pint & Platter. Consider a guaranty, letter of credit or escrow as a closing requirement, or a corresponding price adjustment.\\\"],\\n])\\n\\nh2(doc, \\\"7.4  Low severity items\\\")\\nrisk_table(doc, [\\n [\\\"R-15\\\",\\\"**BrightPath security deposit amount is unexplained.** $25,440 is described as two months' Base Rent but equals $25,036.67 at the current rate and $21,266.67 at the Year 1 rate; it corresponds to a rate of $26.317/RSF, which appears nowhere in the schedule.\\\",\\\"Low\\\",\\\"Pre-closing\\\",\\\"Obtain the deposit ledger; confirm the amount held; arrange transfer to Galleon or a purchase price credit as a closing proration.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-18\\\",\\\"**Apex renewal options are lost together.** Failure to give the first notice by 31 May 2028 forfeits the second option as well, and both options are personal to Apex and void on assignment.\\\",\\\"Low\\\",\\\"Post-closing\\\",\\\"Diarise 31 May 2028; reflect the renewal structure in the hold-period model; note the options would be lost on any assignment of the Apex lease.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-20\\\",\\\"**Apex Year 5 rate departs from the stated 3% mechanism** \\\\u2014 $6.180 against $6.190 \\\\u2014 carrying forward at about $0.006/RSF. Understates current rent by $525 and the term by $3,500.\\\",\\\"Low\\\",\\\"Post-closing\\\",\\\"Record in the reconciliation; no economic action required.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-22\\\",\\\"**Engagement Letter due diligence period stated as 77 days** but is 76 days measured from the stated commencement date of 16 November 2024 (77 days runs from the PSA date of 15 November 2024).\\\",\\\"Low\\\",\\\"Immediate\\\",\\\"Confirm the contractual due diligence expiry against the PSA and diarise every deadline in Section 8 against the confirmed date.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-23\\\",\\\"**Lease-file completeness and document hygiene.** No amendments, side letters, commencement date memoranda, estoppels or SNDAs were provided for any lease. The BrightPath document retains a Word field placeholder; the Verdana rules contain a typographical error; the Apex rounding note does not match its figures.\\\",\\\"Low\\\",\\\"Pre-closing\\\",\\\"Obtain a Seller certification that each lease file is complete and that no side letter, amendment or unrecorded agreement exists; obtain the commencement date memoranda that the Verdana lease required under \\\\u00a7 3.04, and any others that exist.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-24\\\",\\\"**The Apex lease contains no casualty or condemnation article.** There is no express rent abatement, repair obligation or termination right on damage or taking.\\\",\\\"Low\\\",\\\"Pre-DD expiry\\\",\\\"Confirm with Seller whether an amendment supplies these provisions; otherwise note that North Carolina law and the PSA govern, and disclose the position to the lender if it requires casualty provisions.\\\"],\\n [\\\"R-26\\\",\\\"**The Soto Base Year of calendar 2022 falls inside the lease term**, so the tenant's recovery obligation begins from a base that already reflects a full year of its own occupancy \\\\u2014 a drag on recoveries relative to a pre-commencement base year.\\\",\\\"Low\\\",\\\"Pre-closing\\\",\\\"Obtain the 2022 base-year operating expense statement and model recoveries on the true incremental basis.\\\"],\\n])\\nPYEOF\\necho ok\"}", "result": "ok\n"}
{"turn": 36, "role": "assistant", "text": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_ET_oUoSTrCVtqCy3Bobv2Pi5845", "name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && cat >> work/build.py <<'PYEOF'\\n\\n# ================= 8. ACTIONS =================\\nh1(doc, \\\"SECTION 8\\\", \\\"Recommended Pre-Closing Actions\\\")\\n\\npara(doc, \\\"The actions below are sequenced against the engagement timetable: due diligence expires on **31 January 2025**, the target closing date is **15 March 2025**, and the Report is delivered on **20 December 2024**. Deadlines shown as \\\\\\\"31 Jan 2025\\\\\\\" assume the due diligence expiry is confirmed against the PSA (Risk R-22). Responsible parties are identified by reference to the parties named in the Engagement Letter; Galleon is assumed to instruct each of its advisors directly.\\\", size=9.8)\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"1\\\",\\\"Confirm the acquisition structure \\\\u2014 asset purchase or transfer of entity interests \\\\u2014 and instruct counsel accordingly.\\\",\\\"R-01, R-02\\\",\\\"Galleon (Aldaine) / B&H\\\",\\\"Immediate\\\"],\\n [\\\"2\\\",\\\"Obtain from Seller any ROFR Notice delivered to Apex, Apex's response, and any waiver; obtain a fresh written waiver and estoppel from Apex.\\\",\\\"R-01\\\",\\\"B&H via Seller\\\",\\\"10 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"3\\\",\\\"Commission a Mecklenburg County search for any recorded memorandum of ROFR or memorandum of lease affecting Building C; add to Stonebridge's title scope.\\\",\\\"R-01\\\",\\\"Stonebridge / B&H\\\",\\\"10 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"4\\\",\\\"Add to the PSA: a ROFR representation, a specific ROFR indemnity, and a closing condition that no ROFR has been validly exercised.\\\",\\\"R-01\\\",\\\"Galleon / B&H\\\",\\\"Before signing any amendment\\\"],\\n [\\\"5\\\",\\\"Open a GSA consent/novation dialogue with Region 4 if the structure is asset-level; obtain the full GSA lease file including any supplemental lease agreements and Contracting Officer correspondence.\\\",\\\"R-02, R-03\\\",\\\"B&H via Seller\\\",\\\"Immediate\\\"],\\n [\\\"6\\\",\\\"Require Fieldstone to confirm, before the financing commitment, how the lender will address the GSA anti-subordination clause and the absence of SNDAs at Apex and Southeastern.\\\",\\\"R-02, R-10\\\",\\\"Galleon / Fieldstone\\\",\\\"Before commitment\\\"],\\n [\\\"7\\\",\\\"Issue estoppel requests to all seven tenants in the Section 9 form, as a PSA closing condition with a Seller cure obligation.\\\",\\\"R-09, R-05, R-06, R-07\\\",\\\"B&H via Seller\\\",\\\"17 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"8\\\",\\\"Obtain the Haywood Village Shops full rent roll and an occupancy certificate to test the 70% co-tenancy threshold.\\\",\\\"R-07\\\",\\\"Seller / Karen Osgood\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"9\\\",\\\"Obtain the Distribution Center rent roll for Buildings A and B to test the Apex exclusive-use covenant.\\\",\\\"R-08\\\",\\\"Seller / Karen Osgood\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"10\\\",\\\"Confirm whether the 9th floor at Concord Office Tower is vacant, leased, or subject to any other right; quantify the Verdana expansion exposure and seek a price adjustment or waiver.\\\",\\\"R-06\\\",\\\"Seller / B&H\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"11\\\",\\\"Negotiate a new lease, or a holdover acknowledgement with a fixed term and termination restriction, with Southeastern Fire & Safety.\\\",\\\"R-04\\\",\\\"Seller (pre-closing)\\\",\\\"28 Feb 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"12\\\",\\\"Obtain the Southeastern pollution legal liability certificate, historical AFFF/PFAS inventory and safety data sheets; instruct Hanover to assess Unit 12 specifically.\\\",\\\"R-25\\\",\\\"Galleon / Hanover\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"13\\\",\\\"Negotiate a PSA covenant, holdback or direct waiver with Dr. Soto to neutralise the 30 April 2025 termination right.\\\",\\\"R-05\\\",\\\"B&H / Galleon\\\",\\\"28 Feb 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"14\\\",\\\"Reconcile 2024 billing ledgers, holdover invoices and percentage rent statements against the Rent Roll and the lease schedules; correct the Apex, BrightPath and Southeastern figures.\\\",\\\"R-12, R-13, R-14, R-20\\\",\\\"B&H / Crestline\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"15\\\",\\\"Obtain 2021\\\\u20132024 operating expense statements and base-year certifications per property, and confirm the building and park RSF denominators.\\\",\\\"R-19, R-26\\\",\\\"Seller / Crestline\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"16\\\",\\\"Obtain the security deposit ledger and transfer/credit mechanics for BrightPath ($25,440) and Pint & Platter ($19,800); obtain the guaranty originals for Soto and Pint & Platter.\\\",\\\"R-15, R-21\\\",\\\"Seller\\\",\\\"28 Feb 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"17\\\",\\\"Obtain certified trailing-twelve-month gross sales for Pint & Platter and any guaranty release executed under Exhibit D \\\\u00a7 2.\\\",\\\"R-21\\\",\\\"Seller\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"18\\\",\\\"Obtain current financial statements for Apex, Verdana and Southeastern; consider credit enhancement or a price adjustment for the unsecured 65.5% of aggregate rent.\\\",\\\"R-21\\\",\\\"Galleon / Crestline\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"19\\\",\\\"Obtain a Seller certification that the lease files are complete, that no side letters or amendments exist, and that all commencement date memoranda have been delivered.\\\",\\\"R-23, R-24\\\",\\\"Seller\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"20\\\",\\\"Confirm the due diligence expiry date against the PSA and re-diarise every deadline in Section 3.6 and this table.\\\",\\\"R-22\\\",\\\"B&H\\\",\\\"Immediate\\\"],\\n [\\\"21\\\",\\\"Re-run the valuation model on firm rent only (WALT 4.25 years), with the GSA soft term and the Southeastern holdover probability-weighted, the Verdana expansion encumbrance reflected, and the Soto termination modelled.\\\",\\\"R-03, R-04, R-05, R-06, R-11\\\",\\\"Galleon / Crestline\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"#\\\",\\\"Action\\\",\\\"Risk(s)\\\",\\\"Responsible\\\",\\\"Deadline\\\"], rows, [0.3,3.5,0.95,1.1,0.85], size=7.6, head_size=7.4,\\n          align_center_cols=(0,3,4), keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"Section 2(d) of the Engagement Letter requires the firm to flag time-sensitive items without waiting for the delivery of this Report. Two items meet that description and were raised on delivery: the Apex ROFR question (R-01) and the GSA structural issues (R-02), both of which affect whether and how the transaction can close.\\\")\\n\\n# ================= 9. CHECKLIST =================\\nh1(doc, \\\"SECTION 9\\\", \\\"Estoppel and Document Request Checklist\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"Because five of the seven leases contain no tenant estoppel obligation, the certifications below will only be obtained if they are made PSA conditions. Each is included because a specific provision in the corresponding lease makes the point material.\\\", size=9.8)\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"Lease in full force and effect; no amendments or side letters\\\",\\\"All\\\",\\\"Confirms the file is complete, which no lease can compel (R-23)\\\"],\\n [\\\"No default by landlord or tenant; no outstanding landlord obligations, unpaid allowances or reimbursements\\\",\\\"All\\\",\\\"Apex, BrightPath and Verdana had TI allowances; confirm final draws and release of Verdana's 10% retainage (R-23)\\\"],\\n [\\\"No prepaid rent; current rent, additional rent and estimated operating expense charges\\\",\\\"All\\\",\\\"Reconciles the Rent Roll against billing (R-12, R-13, R-20)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Correct current annual and monthly base rent per the tenant's own schedule\\\",\\\"All\\\",\\\"Tenants will certify their own schedule, which may differ from the correct figure (R-12, R-13, R-20)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Security deposit amount held by landlord\\\",\\\"BrightPath, Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"BrightPath's stated amount is inconsistent (R-15)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Renewal options unexercised and no notice delivered\\\",\\\"Apex, Soto, BrightPath, Verdana, Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"Five tenants hold options (R-18)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Expansion option not exercised; no notice given\\\",\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"9th-floor option window is open (R-06)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Contraction option not exercised; no notice given\\\",\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"Contraction right after Year 5 (R-17)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Early termination right not exercised and no notice or intention to terminate\\\",\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto\\\",\\\"30 April 2025 deadline (R-05)\\\"],\\n [\\\"**ROFR over Building C waived as to this transaction; no ROFR Notice received, or received and waived**\\\",\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"Critical item (R-01)\\\"],\\n [\\\"No exclusive-use breach; confirmation of the current occupant mix in Buildings A and B\\\",\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"Exclusive use across all three buildings (R-08)\\\"],\\n [\\\"No co-tenancy failure has occurred, is continuing, or is unwaived\\\",\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"70% test on 62,000 RSF (R-07)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Percentage rent actually paid for Lease Years 2 to 5; breakpoint applied in practice\\\",\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"Fixed vs Natural Breakpoint conflict (R-14)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Guaranty status and whether any release has been executed\\\",\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto, Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"Pint & Platter burn-off (R-21)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Childcare licence in force; no revocation or suspension proceeding\\\",\\\"BrightPath\\\",\\\"Licence revocation is an Event of Default (R-23)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Holdover acknowledged; intention to remain; rent currently payable\\\",\\\"Southeastern\\\",\\\"At-will tenancy (R-04)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Environmental condition of the premises; pollution legal liability cover in force\\\",\\\"Southeastern\\\",\\\"AFFF/PFAS (R-25)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Confirmation of lease status, firm term and any termination notice\\\",\\\"United States (GSA)\\\",\\\"Arranged through the Contracting Officer in lieu of a contractual estoppel (R-02, R-03)\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Certification required\\\",\\\"Tenant\\\",\\\"Reason it is required\\\"], rows, [3.1,1.5,2.1], size=7.9, head_size=7.7, keep_rows=True)\\npara(doc, \\\"**Ancillary documents to be requested at the same time:**\\\", size=9.8, space_before=6)\\nbullets(doc, [\\n \\\"All amendments, side letters, letter agreements, commencement date memoranda and guaranties for each of the seven leases.\\\",\\n \\\"Any subleases or licence agreements currently in effect, and notice of any pending assignment or sublease request.\\\",\\n \\\"Copies of all SNDAs, subordination agreements and mortgages affecting each property, for coordination with Stonebridge's title review.\\\",\\n \\\"Current certificates of insurance for all seven tenants, and confirmation that any required additional-insured endorsements are in place.\\\",\\n \\\"The 2021 GSA Base Year operating expense statement (required to have been delivered by 31 March 2022) and the 2022 base-year statements for Millbrook Medical Plaza.\\\",\\n \\\"The 2024 billing ledgers, aged receivables and percentage rent statements for all seven tenants.\\\",\\n \\\"Any notice, correspondence or claim from a tenant relating to options, exclusive use, co-tenancy, CAM reconciliation or default.\\\",\\n \\\"Confirmation of the ROFR Notice position for Apex and any recorded memorandum affecting Building C (to be obtained through Stonebridge).\\\",\\n], size=9.2)\\nPYEOF\\necho ok\"}"}], "input_tokens": 226312, "output_tokens": 2539, "finish_reason": "completed"}
{"turn": 36, "role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call_00_ET_oUoSTrCVtqCy3Bobv2Pi5845", "tool_name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && cat >> work/build.py <<'PYEOF'\\n\\n# ================= 8. ACTIONS =================\\nh1(doc, \\\"SECTION 8\\\", \\\"Recommended Pre-Closing Actions\\\")\\n\\npara(doc, \\\"The actions below are sequenced against the engagement timetable: due diligence expires on **31 January 2025**, the target closing date is **15 March 2025**, and the Report is delivered on **20 December 2024**. Deadlines shown as \\\\\\\"31 Jan 2025\\\\\\\" assume the due diligence expiry is confirmed against the PSA (Risk R-22). Responsible parties are identified by reference to the parties named in the Engagement Letter; Galleon is assumed to instruct each of its advisors directly.\\\", size=9.8)\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"1\\\",\\\"Confirm the acquisition structure \\\\u2014 asset purchase or transfer of entity interests \\\\u2014 and instruct counsel accordingly.\\\",\\\"R-01, R-02\\\",\\\"Galleon (Aldaine) / B&H\\\",\\\"Immediate\\\"],\\n [\\\"2\\\",\\\"Obtain from Seller any ROFR Notice delivered to Apex, Apex's response, and any waiver; obtain a fresh written waiver and estoppel from Apex.\\\",\\\"R-01\\\",\\\"B&H via Seller\\\",\\\"10 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"3\\\",\\\"Commission a Mecklenburg County search for any recorded memorandum of ROFR or memorandum of lease affecting Building C; add to Stonebridge's title scope.\\\",\\\"R-01\\\",\\\"Stonebridge / B&H\\\",\\\"10 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"4\\\",\\\"Add to the PSA: a ROFR representation, a specific ROFR indemnity, and a closing condition that no ROFR has been validly exercised.\\\",\\\"R-01\\\",\\\"Galleon / B&H\\\",\\\"Before signing any amendment\\\"],\\n [\\\"5\\\",\\\"Open a GSA consent/novation dialogue with Region 4 if the structure is asset-level; obtain the full GSA lease file including any supplemental lease agreements and Contracting Officer correspondence.\\\",\\\"R-02, R-03\\\",\\\"B&H via Seller\\\",\\\"Immediate\\\"],\\n [\\\"6\\\",\\\"Require Fieldstone to confirm, before the financing commitment, how the lender will address the GSA anti-subordination clause and the absence of SNDAs at Apex and Southeastern.\\\",\\\"R-02, R-10\\\",\\\"Galleon / Fieldstone\\\",\\\"Before commitment\\\"],\\n [\\\"7\\\",\\\"Issue estoppel requests to all seven tenants in the Section 9 form, as a PSA closing condition with a Seller cure obligation.\\\",\\\"R-09, R-05, R-06, R-07\\\",\\\"B&H via Seller\\\",\\\"17 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"8\\\",\\\"Obtain the Haywood Village Shops full rent roll and an occupancy certificate to test the 70% co-tenancy threshold.\\\",\\\"R-07\\\",\\\"Seller / Karen Osgood\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"9\\\",\\\"Obtain the Distribution Center rent roll for Buildings A and B to test the Apex exclusive-use covenant.\\\",\\\"R-08\\\",\\\"Seller / Karen Osgood\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"10\\\",\\\"Confirm whether the 9th floor at Concord Office Tower is vacant, leased, or subject to any other right; quantify the Verdana expansion exposure and seek a price adjustment or waiver.\\\",\\\"R-06\\\",\\\"Seller / B&H\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"11\\\",\\\"Negotiate a new lease, or a holdover acknowledgement with a fixed term and termination restriction, with Southeastern Fire & Safety.\\\",\\\"R-04\\\",\\\"Seller (pre-closing)\\\",\\\"28 Feb 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"12\\\",\\\"Obtain the Southeastern pollution legal liability certificate, historical AFFF/PFAS inventory and safety data sheets; instruct Hanover to assess Unit 12 specifically.\\\",\\\"R-25\\\",\\\"Galleon / Hanover\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"13\\\",\\\"Negotiate a PSA covenant, holdback or direct waiver with Dr. Soto to neutralise the 30 April 2025 termination right.\\\",\\\"R-05\\\",\\\"B&H / Galleon\\\",\\\"28 Feb 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"14\\\",\\\"Reconcile 2024 billing ledgers, holdover invoices and percentage rent statements against the Rent Roll and the lease schedules; correct the Apex, BrightPath and Southeastern figures.\\\",\\\"R-12, R-13, R-14, R-20\\\",\\\"B&H / Crestline\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"15\\\",\\\"Obtain 2021\\\\u20132024 operating expense statements and base-year certifications per property, and confirm the building and park RSF denominators.\\\",\\\"R-19, R-26\\\",\\\"Seller / Crestline\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"16\\\",\\\"Obtain the security deposit ledger and transfer/credit mechanics for BrightPath ($25,440) and Pint & Platter ($19,800); obtain the guaranty originals for Soto and Pint & Platter.\\\",\\\"R-15, R-21\\\",\\\"Seller\\\",\\\"28 Feb 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"17\\\",\\\"Obtain certified trailing-twelve-month gross sales for Pint & Platter and any guaranty release executed under Exhibit D \\\\u00a7 2.\\\",\\\"R-21\\\",\\\"Seller\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"18\\\",\\\"Obtain current financial statements for Apex, Verdana and Southeastern; consider credit enhancement or a price adjustment for the unsecured 65.5% of aggregate rent.\\\",\\\"R-21\\\",\\\"Galleon / Crestline\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"19\\\",\\\"Obtain a Seller certification that the lease files are complete, that no side letters or amendments exist, and that all commencement date memoranda have been delivered.\\\",\\\"R-23, R-24\\\",\\\"Seller\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n [\\\"20\\\",\\\"Confirm the due diligence expiry date against the PSA and re-diarise every deadline in Section 3.6 and this table.\\\",\\\"R-22\\\",\\\"B&H\\\",\\\"Immediate\\\"],\\n [\\\"21\\\",\\\"Re-run the valuation model on firm rent only (WALT 4.25 years), with the GSA soft term and the Southeastern holdover probability-weighted, the Verdana expansion encumbrance reflected, and the Soto termination modelled.\\\",\\\"R-03, R-04, R-05, R-06, R-11\\\",\\\"Galleon / Crestline\\\",\\\"31 Jan 2025\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"#\\\",\\\"Action\\\",\\\"Risk(s)\\\",\\\"Responsible\\\",\\\"Deadline\\\"], rows, [0.3,3.5,0.95,1.1,0.85], size=7.6, head_size=7.4,\\n          align_center_cols=(0,3,4), keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"Section 2(d) of the Engagement Letter requires the firm to flag time-sensitive items without waiting for the delivery of this Report. Two items meet that description and were raised on delivery: the Apex ROFR question (R-01) and the GSA structural issues (R-02), both of which affect whether and how the transaction can close.\\\")\\n\\n# ================= 9. CHECKLIST =================\\nh1(doc, \\\"SECTION 9\\\", \\\"Estoppel and Document Request Checklist\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"Because five of the seven leases contain no tenant estoppel obligation, the certifications below will only be obtained if they are made PSA conditions. Each is included because a specific provision in the corresponding lease makes the point material.\\\", size=9.8)\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"Lease in full force and effect; no amendments or side letters\\\",\\\"All\\\",\\\"Confirms the file is complete, which no lease can compel (R-23)\\\"],\\n [\\\"No default by landlord or tenant; no outstanding landlord obligations, unpaid allowances or reimbursements\\\",\\\"All\\\",\\\"Apex, BrightPath and Verdana had TI allowances; confirm final draws and release of Verdana's 10% retainage (R-23)\\\"],\\n [\\\"No prepaid rent; current rent, additional rent and estimated operating expense charges\\\",\\\"All\\\",\\\"Reconciles the Rent Roll against billing (R-12, R-13, R-20)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Correct current annual and monthly base rent per the tenant's own schedule\\\",\\\"All\\\",\\\"Tenants will certify their own schedule, which may differ from the correct figure (R-12, R-13, R-20)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Security deposit amount held by landlord\\\",\\\"BrightPath, Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"BrightPath's stated amount is inconsistent (R-15)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Renewal options unexercised and no notice delivered\\\",\\\"Apex, Soto, BrightPath, Verdana, Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"Five tenants hold options (R-18)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Expansion option not exercised; no notice given\\\",\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"9th-floor option window is open (R-06)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Contraction option not exercised; no notice given\\\",\\\"Verdana\\\",\\\"Contraction right after Year 5 (R-17)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Early termination right not exercised and no notice or intention to terminate\\\",\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto\\\",\\\"30 April 2025 deadline (R-05)\\\"],\\n [\\\"**ROFR over Building C waived as to this transaction; no ROFR Notice received, or received and waived**\\\",\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"Critical item (R-01)\\\"],\\n [\\\"No exclusive-use breach; confirmation of the current occupant mix in Buildings A and B\\\",\\\"Apex\\\",\\\"Exclusive use across all three buildings (R-08)\\\"],\\n [\\\"No co-tenancy failure has occurred, is continuing, or is unwaived\\\",\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"70% test on 62,000 RSF (R-07)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Percentage rent actually paid for Lease Years 2 to 5; breakpoint applied in practice\\\",\\\"Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"Fixed vs Natural Breakpoint conflict (R-14)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Guaranty status and whether any release has been executed\\\",\\\"Dr. Miriam Soto, Pint & Platter\\\",\\\"Pint & Platter burn-off (R-21)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Childcare licence in force; no revocation or suspension proceeding\\\",\\\"BrightPath\\\",\\\"Licence revocation is an Event of Default (R-23)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Holdover acknowledged; intention to remain; rent currently payable\\\",\\\"Southeastern\\\",\\\"At-will tenancy (R-04)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Environmental condition of the premises; pollution legal liability cover in force\\\",\\\"Southeastern\\\",\\\"AFFF/PFAS (R-25)\\\"],\\n [\\\"Confirmation of lease status, firm term and any termination notice\\\",\\\"United States (GSA)\\\",\\\"Arranged through the Contracting Officer in lieu of a contractual estoppel (R-02, R-03)\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"Certification required\\\",\\\"Tenant\\\",\\\"Reason it is required\\\"], rows, [3.1,1.5,2.1], size=7.9, head_size=7.7, keep_rows=True)\\npara(doc, \\\"**Ancillary documents to be requested at the same time:**\\\", size=9.8, space_before=6)\\nbullets(doc, [\\n \\\"All amendments, side letters, letter agreements, commencement date memoranda and guaranties for each of the seven leases.\\\",\\n \\\"Any subleases or licence agreements currently in effect, and notice of any pending assignment or sublease request.\\\",\\n \\\"Copies of all SNDAs, subordination agreements and mortgages affecting each property, for coordination with Stonebridge's title review.\\\",\\n \\\"Current certificates of insurance for all seven tenants, and confirmation that any required additional-insured endorsements are in place.\\\",\\n \\\"The 2021 GSA Base Year operating expense statement (required to have been delivered by 31 March 2022) and the 2022 base-year statements for Millbrook Medical Plaza.\\\",\\n \\\"The 2024 billing ledgers, aged receivables and percentage rent statements for all seven tenants.\\\",\\n \\\"Any notice, correspondence or claim from a tenant relating to options, exclusive use, co-tenancy, CAM reconciliation or default.\\\",\\n \\\"Confirmation of the ROFR Notice position for Apex and any recorded memorandum affecting Building C (to be obtained through Stonebridge).\\\",\\n], size=9.2)\\nPYEOF\\necho ok\"}", "result": "ok\n"}
{"turn": 37, "role": "assistant", "text": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_ET_8I3TtieBstza8EjwSkfZ7576", "name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && cat >> work/build.py <<'PYEOF'\\n\\n# ================= 10. OPEN ITEMS =================\\nh1(doc, \\\"SECTION 10\\\", \\\"Open Items and Information Gaps\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"The following matters could not be resolved from the nine documents provided. Each is stated together with its effect on the analysis, so that the reader can see which conclusions in this Report are qualified.\\\", size=9.8)\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"1\\\",\\\"**Acquisition structure** \\\\u2014 whether Galleon is acquiring assets or entity interests.\\\",\\\"Determines whether the Apex ROFR is triggered at all (R-01) and whether GSA consent or a novation is required (R-02). Two of the three most significant conclusions in this Report depend on it.\\\",\\\"PSA / Galleon\\\"],\\n [\\\"2\\\",\\\"**Any ROFR Notice delivered to Apex, and Apex's response.**\\\",\\\"The single most consequential open question (R-01). If a notice was delivered and the 30-day period has run without exercise, the position is materially better than if no notice was given.\\\",\\\"Seller / Apex\\\"],\\n [\\\"3\\\",\\\"**Full Haywood Village Shops rent roll and occupancy certificate.**\\\",\\\"Without it the Pint & Platter co-tenancy right cannot be tested, and the 25% rent reduction or termination right cannot be valued (R-07).\\\",\\\"Seller / Karen Osgood\\\"],\\n [\\\"4\\\",\\\"**Buildings A and B occupancy at Thornfield Distribution Center.**\\\",\\\"Without it the Apex exclusive-use covenant cannot be tested; a current breach would give Apex leverage and would depress the value of A and B (R-08).\\\",\\\"Seller / Karen Osgood\\\"],\\n [\\\"5\\\",\\\"**Status of the 9th floor at Concord Office Tower.**\\\",\\\"Determines whether the Verdana expansion option can be performed, and therefore the value of the encumbrance (R-06).\\\",\\\"Seller\\\"],\\n [\\\"6\\\",\\\"**Amendments, side letters and commencement memoranda for all seven leases.**\\\",\\\"No conclusion in this Report can exclude the possibility that a term has been varied. The Verdana lease required a commencement date memorandum that has not been produced (R-23).\\\",\\\"Seller\\\"],\\n [\\\"7\\\",\\\"**Billing ledgers, aged receivables and percentage rent statements.**\\\",\\\"Necessary to reconcile the Rent Roll and to resolve the three escalation discrepancies against actual billing rather than by construction (R-12, R-13, R-14, R-20).\\\",\\\"Seller / Crestline\\\"],\\n [\\\"8\\\",\\\"**Operating expense base-year statements and reconciliation statements.**\\\",\\\"The recovery income of all seven leases, and the base-year effect at Millbrook and Concord Office Tower, cannot be quantified without them (R-19, R-26).\\\",\\\"Seller / Crestline\\\"],\\n [\\\"9\\\",\\\"**Building and park rentable areas for four properties.**\\\",\\\"The recovery shares for Soto, BrightPath, Southeastern and GSA are unverifiable as drafted (R-19).\\\",\\\"Seller\\\"],\\n [\\\"10\\\",\\\"**Amount of the two security deposits actually held, and status of the Pint & Platter guaranty.**\\\",\\\"The BrightPath figure is internally inconsistent, and the Pint & Platter guaranty may already have burned off (R-15, R-21).\\\",\\\"Seller\\\"],\\n [\\\"11\\\",\\\"**Current financial statements for Apex, Verdana and Southeastern.**\\\",\\\"65.5% of aggregate rent is unsecured; no view on credit quality is possible on the documents provided (R-21).\\\",\\\"Seller / tenants\\\"],\\n [\\\"12\\\",\\\"**Any SNDAs, subordination agreements and existing mortgages.**\\\",\\\"Needed to reconcile Verdana \\\\u00a7 17.02 (no mortgage at February 2022) with the current position, and to plan the lender's deliverables (R-10).\\\",\\\"Seller / Stonebridge\\\"],\\n [\\\"13\\\",\\\"**Environmental information for Unit 12 (Greystone).**\\\",\\\"AFFF/PFAS are expressly permitted on the premises; the indemnity survives termination but is unsecured (R-25).\\\",\\\"Hanover / Seller\\\"],\\n [\\\"14\\\",\\\"**Whether any lease amendment supplies casualty and condemnation provisions for the Apex lease.**\\\",\\\"The lease has none, which is unusual for an NNN industrial lease of this size (R-24).\\\",\\\"Seller\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"#\\\",\\\"Open item\\\",\\\"Effect on this analysis\\\",\\\"To be obtained from\\\"], rows, [0.3,2.3,3.0,1.1], size=7.7, head_size=7.5,\\n          align_center_cols=(0,), keep_rows=True)\\n\\n# ================= 11. LIMITATIONS =================\\nh1(doc, \\\"SECTION 11\\\", \\\"Limitations and Reliance\\\")\\nlimits = [\\n \\\"**Basis of the Report.** This Report has been prepared for Galleon Capital Advisors LLC and its authorized representatives for the sole purpose of evaluating the acquisition of the Portfolio. It may not be relied upon by any other person, including any lender (including Fieldstone Capital Markets LLC in its capacity as debt placement agent), title company, insurer or other adviser, without the prior written consent of Birchwood & Hale LLP.\\\",\\n \\\"**Documents only.** The analysis is based solely on the nine documents listed in Section 2.2 and Appendix B, as provided to the firm. We have not verified any fact, representation or condition beyond the four corners of those documents, and we have not inspected any property, met any tenant, or reviewed any Seller book or record. Where a document was incomplete or internally inconsistent, we have said so rather than resolving the inconsistency in Galleon's favour.\\\",\\n \\\"**Matters outside scope.** Title, survey, zoning, environmental, structural and building condition review; the financial and accounting review of Seller's books and records; debt placement and financing; brokerage; and tax advice are all outside the scope of this engagement and are being handled by the parties identified in Section 2 of the Engagement Letter. Where this Report identifies an issue in one of those areas \\\\u2014 for example the AFFF/PFAS regime at Unit 12 (R-25) or the priority of the GSA lease against a mortgage (R-02) \\\\u2014 it does so only to refer the matter, not to opine on it.\\\",\\n \\\"**Not a valuation, and not a guarantee.** This Report does not value the Portfolio, any property or any lease. Rental figures are contractual rent as verified from the leases, not net operating income, and no opinion is expressed on capitalisation rates, market rent, discount rates or investment merit. Nothing in this Report guarantees the enforceability of any lease provision, the creditworthiness or financial condition of any tenant, or the accuracy of any representation made by the Seller, the property manager or any third party.\\\",\\n \\\"**Forward-looking statements and deadlines.** Option deadlines, notice periods and expiration dates have been computed from the leases as drafted. They assume no notice has been given, no renewal exercised and no amendment executed, and they are subject to confirmation against the PSA, the lease files and actual correspondence \\\\u2014 in particular the due diligence expiry date noted at R-22.\\\",\\n \\\"**Estimates and illustrations.** Where figures are described as illustrative \\\\u2014 the Building C allocable ROFR price at Section 1.4 and the Verdana contraction fee at Section 4.5 \\\\u2014 they are arithmetical indications built on stated assumptions and are not valuations or predictions. They should not be used as negotiation positions without further work.\\\",\\n \\\"**Currency and date.** All amounts are in United States dollars. The Report is stated as at December 20, 2024 and takes the rent, term and option position as at January 1, 2025. We have no obligation to update the Report for events after its date.\\\",\\n \\\"**Professional responsibility.** This Report sets out legal analysis based on the documents provided. It is not tax advice, and Galleon should consult its tax advisers. Galleon is encouraged to verify independently all financial information and to conduct such additional due diligence as it considers appropriate.\\\",\\n]\\nfor i,t in enumerate(limits,1):\\n    p = doc.add_paragraph()\\n    pf = p.paragraph_format\\n    pf.left_indent = Inches(0.3); pf.first_line_indent = Inches(-0.3)\\n    pf.space_after = Pt(5); pf.line_spacing = 1.09\\n    r = p.add_run(f\\\"({i})  \\\"); r.font.size=Pt(9.2); r.bold=True; r.font.color.rgb = NAVY\\n    for k,part in enumerate(t.split(\\\"**\\\")):\\n        if not part: continue\\n        rr = p.add_run(part); rr.font.size=Pt(9.2); rr.bold = (k%2==1)\\n\\ndoc.add_paragraph().paragraph_format.space_after = Pt(14)\\npara(doc, \\\"Respectfully submitted,\\\", size=9.8, space_after=16)\\npara(doc, \\\"**BIRCHWOOD & HALE LLP**\\\", size=10, space_after=1)\\npara(doc, \\\"Lydia Chen, Partner          Devon Pratt, Senior Associate\\\", size=9.5, space_after=1, color=GREY)\\npara(doc, \\\"December 20, 2024\\\", size=9.5, color=GREY)\\nPYEOF\\necho ok\"}"}], "input_tokens": 228865, "output_tokens": 1998, "finish_reason": "completed"}
{"turn": 37, "role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call_00_ET_8I3TtieBstza8EjwSkfZ7576", "tool_name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && cat >> work/build.py <<'PYEOF'\\n\\n# ================= 10. OPEN ITEMS =================\\nh1(doc, \\\"SECTION 10\\\", \\\"Open Items and Information Gaps\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"The following matters could not be resolved from the nine documents provided. Each is stated together with its effect on the analysis, so that the reader can see which conclusions in this Report are qualified.\\\", size=9.8)\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"1\\\",\\\"**Acquisition structure** \\\\u2014 whether Galleon is acquiring assets or entity interests.\\\",\\\"Determines whether the Apex ROFR is triggered at all (R-01) and whether GSA consent or a novation is required (R-02). Two of the three most significant conclusions in this Report depend on it.\\\",\\\"PSA / Galleon\\\"],\\n [\\\"2\\\",\\\"**Any ROFR Notice delivered to Apex, and Apex's response.**\\\",\\\"The single most consequential open question (R-01). If a notice was delivered and the 30-day period has run without exercise, the position is materially better than if no notice was given.\\\",\\\"Seller / Apex\\\"],\\n [\\\"3\\\",\\\"**Full Haywood Village Shops rent roll and occupancy certificate.**\\\",\\\"Without it the Pint & Platter co-tenancy right cannot be tested, and the 25% rent reduction or termination right cannot be valued (R-07).\\\",\\\"Seller / Karen Osgood\\\"],\\n [\\\"4\\\",\\\"**Buildings A and B occupancy at Thornfield Distribution Center.**\\\",\\\"Without it the Apex exclusive-use covenant cannot be tested; a current breach would give Apex leverage and would depress the value of A and B (R-08).\\\",\\\"Seller / Karen Osgood\\\"],\\n [\\\"5\\\",\\\"**Status of the 9th floor at Concord Office Tower.**\\\",\\\"Determines whether the Verdana expansion option can be performed, and therefore the value of the encumbrance (R-06).\\\",\\\"Seller\\\"],\\n [\\\"6\\\",\\\"**Amendments, side letters and commencement memoranda for all seven leases.**\\\",\\\"No conclusion in this Report can exclude the possibility that a term has been varied. The Verdana lease required a commencement date memorandum that has not been produced (R-23).\\\",\\\"Seller\\\"],\\n [\\\"7\\\",\\\"**Billing ledgers, aged receivables and percentage rent statements.**\\\",\\\"Necessary to reconcile the Rent Roll and to resolve the three escalation discrepancies against actual billing rather than by construction (R-12, R-13, R-14, R-20).\\\",\\\"Seller / Crestline\\\"],\\n [\\\"8\\\",\\\"**Operating expense base-year statements and reconciliation statements.**\\\",\\\"The recovery income of all seven leases, and the base-year effect at Millbrook and Concord Office Tower, cannot be quantified without them (R-19, R-26).\\\",\\\"Seller / Crestline\\\"],\\n [\\\"9\\\",\\\"**Building and park rentable areas for four properties.**\\\",\\\"The recovery shares for Soto, BrightPath, Southeastern and GSA are unverifiable as drafted (R-19).\\\",\\\"Seller\\\"],\\n [\\\"10\\\",\\\"**Amount of the two security deposits actually held, and status of the Pint & Platter guaranty.**\\\",\\\"The BrightPath figure is internally inconsistent, and the Pint & Platter guaranty may already have burned off (R-15, R-21).\\\",\\\"Seller\\\"],\\n [\\\"11\\\",\\\"**Current financial statements for Apex, Verdana and Southeastern.**\\\",\\\"65.5% of aggregate rent is unsecured; no view on credit quality is possible on the documents provided (R-21).\\\",\\\"Seller / tenants\\\"],\\n [\\\"12\\\",\\\"**Any SNDAs, subordination agreements and existing mortgages.**\\\",\\\"Needed to reconcile Verdana \\\\u00a7 17.02 (no mortgage at February 2022) with the current position, and to plan the lender's deliverables (R-10).\\\",\\\"Seller / Stonebridge\\\"],\\n [\\\"13\\\",\\\"**Environmental information for Unit 12 (Greystone).**\\\",\\\"AFFF/PFAS are expressly permitted on the premises; the indemnity survives termination but is unsecured (R-25).\\\",\\\"Hanover / Seller\\\"],\\n [\\\"14\\\",\\\"**Whether any lease amendment supplies casualty and condemnation provisions for the Apex lease.**\\\",\\\"The lease has none, which is unusual for an NNN industrial lease of this size (R-24).\\\",\\\"Seller\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"#\\\",\\\"Open item\\\",\\\"Effect on this analysis\\\",\\\"To be obtained from\\\"], rows, [0.3,2.3,3.0,1.1], size=7.7, head_size=7.5,\\n          align_center_cols=(0,), keep_rows=True)\\n\\n# ================= 11. LIMITATIONS =================\\nh1(doc, \\\"SECTION 11\\\", \\\"Limitations and Reliance\\\")\\nlimits = [\\n \\\"**Basis of the Report.** This Report has been prepared for Galleon Capital Advisors LLC and its authorized representatives for the sole purpose of evaluating the acquisition of the Portfolio. It may not be relied upon by any other person, including any lender (including Fieldstone Capital Markets LLC in its capacity as debt placement agent), title company, insurer or other adviser, without the prior written consent of Birchwood & Hale LLP.\\\",\\n \\\"**Documents only.** The analysis is based solely on the nine documents listed in Section 2.2 and Appendix B, as provided to the firm. We have not verified any fact, representation or condition beyond the four corners of those documents, and we have not inspected any property, met any tenant, or reviewed any Seller book or record. Where a document was incomplete or internally inconsistent, we have said so rather than resolving the inconsistency in Galleon's favour.\\\",\\n \\\"**Matters outside scope.** Title, survey, zoning, environmental, structural and building condition review; the financial and accounting review of Seller's books and records; debt placement and financing; brokerage; and tax advice are all outside the scope of this engagement and are being handled by the parties identified in Section 2 of the Engagement Letter. Where this Report identifies an issue in one of those areas \\\\u2014 for example the AFFF/PFAS regime at Unit 12 (R-25) or the priority of the GSA lease against a mortgage (R-02) \\\\u2014 it does so only to refer the matter, not to opine on it.\\\",\\n \\\"**Not a valuation, and not a guarantee.** This Report does not value the Portfolio, any property or any lease. Rental figures are contractual rent as verified from the leases, not net operating income, and no opinion is expressed on capitalisation rates, market rent, discount rates or investment merit. Nothing in this Report guarantees the enforceability of any lease provision, the creditworthiness or financial condition of any tenant, or the accuracy of any representation made by the Seller, the property manager or any third party.\\\",\\n \\\"**Forward-looking statements and deadlines.** Option deadlines, notice periods and expiration dates have been computed from the leases as drafted. They assume no notice has been given, no renewal exercised and no amendment executed, and they are subject to confirmation against the PSA, the lease files and actual correspondence \\\\u2014 in particular the due diligence expiry date noted at R-22.\\\",\\n \\\"**Estimates and illustrations.** Where figures are described as illustrative \\\\u2014 the Building C allocable ROFR price at Section 1.4 and the Verdana contraction fee at Section 4.5 \\\\u2014 they are arithmetical indications built on stated assumptions and are not valuations or predictions. They should not be used as negotiation positions without further work.\\\",\\n \\\"**Currency and date.** All amounts are in United States dollars. The Report is stated as at December 20, 2024 and takes the rent, term and option position as at January 1, 2025. We have no obligation to update the Report for events after its date.\\\",\\n \\\"**Professional responsibility.** This Report sets out legal analysis based on the documents provided. It is not tax advice, and Galleon should consult its tax advisers. Galleon is encouraged to verify independently all financial information and to conduct such additional due diligence as it considers appropriate.\\\",\\n]\\nfor i,t in enumerate(limits,1):\\n    p = doc.add_paragraph()\\n    pf = p.paragraph_format\\n    pf.left_indent = Inches(0.3); pf.first_line_indent = Inches(-0.3)\\n    pf.space_after = Pt(5); pf.line_spacing = 1.09\\n    r = p.add_run(f\\\"({i})  \\\"); r.font.size=Pt(9.2); r.bold=True; r.font.color.rgb = NAVY\\n    for k,part in enumerate(t.split(\\\"**\\\")):\\n        if not part: continue\\n        rr = p.add_run(part); rr.font.size=Pt(9.2); rr.bold = (k%2==1)\\n\\ndoc.add_paragraph().paragraph_format.space_after = Pt(14)\\npara(doc, \\\"Respectfully submitted,\\\", size=9.8, space_after=16)\\npara(doc, \\\"**BIRCHWOOD & HALE LLP**\\\", size=10, space_after=1)\\npara(doc, \\\"Lydia Chen, Partner          Devon Pratt, Senior Associate\\\", size=9.5, space_after=1, color=GREY)\\npara(doc, \\\"December 20, 2024\\\", size=9.5, color=GREY)\\nPYEOF\\necho ok\"}", "result": "ok\n"}
{"turn": 38, "role": "assistant", "text": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_lsiszcKwn9ipVMuPVIOG1302", "name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && cat >> work/build.py <<'PYEOF'\\n\\n# ================= APPENDIX A =================\\nfrom decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP\\nimport calendar\\nMN = [\\\"Jan\\\",\\\"Feb\\\",\\\"Mar\\\",\\\"Apr\\\",\\\"May\\\",\\\"Jun\\\",\\\"Jul\\\",\\\"Aug\\\",\\\"Sep\\\",\\\"Oct\\\",\\\"Nov\\\",\\\"Dec\\\"]\\ndef q(x,n):\\n    return Decimal(str(x)).quantize(Decimal('1.'+'0'*n), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP)\\ndef periods(y,m,n,thismonth_is_first=True):\\n    out=[]\\n    for i in range(n):\\n        mm = m + i*12\\n        sy = y + (mm-1)//12; sm = (mm-1)%12 + 1\\n        em = sm + 11\\n        ey = sy + (em-1)//12; emm = (em-1)%12 + 1\\n        last = calendar.monthrange(ey, emm)[1]\\n        out.append(f\\\"{MN[sm-1]} 1, {sy} \\\\u2013 {MN[emm-1]} {last}, {ey}\\\")\\n    return out\\n\\ndef appx_table(doc, name, y1, rate, stated, rsf, dp, start_y, start_m, note_map=None, intro=None):\\n    h2(doc, name, space_before=10)\\n    if intro: para(doc, intro, size=8.8, space_after=3)\\n    per = periods(start_y, start_m, len(stated))\\n    rows=[]; cur=q(y1,dp); fills=[]\\n    for i,s in enumerate(stated,1):\\n        s=q(s,dp); d=cur-s; da=d*rsf\\n        note = (note_map or {}).get(i,\\\"\\\")\\n        rows.append([str(i), per[i-1], f\\\"{cur}\\\", f\\\"{s}\\\", (f\\\"{d}\\\" if d!=0 else \\\"\\\\u2014\\\"),\\n                     f\\\"{s*rsf:,.2f}\\\", f\\\"{cur*rsf:,.2f}\\\", note])\\n        fills.append(WARN if d!=0 else None)\\n        cur = q(cur*(1+Decimal(str(rate))), dp)\\n    add_table(doc, [\\\"Yr\\\",\\\"Lease Year period\\\",\\\"Contract\\\",\\\"Stated\\\",\\\"Diff/RSF\\\",\\\"Stated annual ($)\\\",\\\"Contract annual ($)\\\",\\\"Note\\\"], rows,\\n              [0.3,1.62,0.62,0.55,0.55,0.85,0.9,1.31], size=7.0, head_size=6.9,\\n              align_center_cols=(0,2,3,4,5,6), row_fills=fills, keep_rows=True)\\n    tot = sum((q(y1,dp))*0 for _ in [0])\\nh1(doc, \\\"APPENDIX A\\\", \\\"Escalation Schedule Recomputation\\\")\\npara(doc, \\\"Each table below recomputes the rent schedule from the lease's own starting rate and stated escalation mechanism, applying the lease's rounding convention at each step (to the nearest $0.001 per RSF for Apex, which states rates to three decimals; to the nearest cent elsewhere). The \\\\u201cContract\\\\u201d column is what the mechanism produces; the \\\\u201cStated\\\\u201d column is what the lease actually says. Shaded rows are departures. A negative difference means the lease states less than its own mechanism produces.\\\", size=9.2)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"Where a departure occurs, the following year's \\\\u201cContract\\\\u201d figure is computed from the corrected rate rather than from the stated rate, so that the effect of the error on the remainder of the term is shown. \\\\u201cStated annual\\\\u201d is the product of the stated rate and the stated rentable area; every stated annual and monthly amount in all seven leases recomputes exactly on that basis, so the tables do not repeat the monthly check.\\\")\\n\\nappx_table(doc, \\\"A.1  Apex Fulfillment Services \\\\u2014 3% compounding, $5.500/RSF, 87,500 RSF\\\", 5.500, 0.03,\\n [\\\"5.500\\\",\\\"5.665\\\",\\\"5.835\\\",\\\"6.010\\\",\\\"6.180\\\",\\\"6.370\\\",\\\"6.561\\\",\\\"6.758\\\",\\\"6.961\\\",\\\"7.170\\\"], 87500, 3, 2019, 6,\\n note_map={5:\\\"Root error: $6.010 \\\\u00d7 1.03 = $6.190, stated $6.180\\\",6:\\\"Carry-forward; brief departs from current rate\\\",9:\\\"\\\",10:\\\"\\\"},\\n intro=\\\"Departures at Years 5 and 6 only. Cumulative effect across Years 5\\\\u201310: \\\\u2212$3,500.00. Current-year (Year 6) effect: \\\\u2212$525.00.\\\")\\nappx_table(doc, \\\"A.2  Dr. Miriam Soto, DDS \\\\u2014 fixed +$0.750/RSF per annum, $28.000/RSF, 3,200 RSF\\\", 28.00, 0.0,\\n [\\\"28.00\\\",\\\"28.75\\\",\\\"29.50\\\",\\\"30.25\\\",\\\"31.00\\\",\\\"31.75\\\",\\\"32.50\\\"], 3200, 2, 2021, 11,\\n intro=\\\"Fixed step rather than a percentage escalation, so the mechanism is additive: $28.00 + $0.75 \\\\u00d7 (year \\\\u2212 1). All seven years conform exactly; no departures.\\\")\\nappx_table(doc, \\\"A.3  BrightPath Learning Centers \\\\u2014 2.5% compounding, $22.00/RSF, 5,800 RSF\\\", 22.00, 0.025,\\n [\\\"22.00\\\",\\\"22.55\\\",\\\"23.11\\\",\\\"23.69\\\",\\\"24.28\\\",\\\"24.89\\\",\\\"25.51\\\",\\\"25.90\\\",\\\"26.55\\\",\\\"27.21\\\",\\\"27.89\\\",\\\"28.59\\\",\\\"29.30\\\",\\\"30.04\\\",\\\"30.79\\\"], 5800, 2, 2017, 4,\\n note_map={8:\\\"Root error: $25.51 \\\\u00d7 1.025 = $26.15, stated $25.90\\\",15:\\\"Error compounded throughout; $0.30/RSF by Year 15\\\"},\\n intro=\\\"Departure at Year 8 which then compounds to the end of the term. Cumulative effect across Years 8\\\\u201315: \\\\u2212$12,470.00. Current-year (Year 8) effect: \\\\u2212$1,450.00. The lower Year 15 base also reduces the cap on the first Renewal Term rent.\\\")\\nappx_table(doc, \\\"A.4  Southeastern Fire & Safety \\\\u2014 2% compounding, $7.50/RSF, 22,000 RSF\\\", 7.50, 0.02,\\n [\\\"7.50\\\",\\\"7.65\\\",\\\"7.80\\\",\\\"7.96\\\",\\\"8.12\\\",\\\"8.28\\\",\\\"8.45\\\",\\\"8.62\\\",\\\"8.79\\\",\\\"9.25\\\"], 22000, 2, 2014, 7,\\n note_map={10:\\\"Root error: $8.79 \\\\u00d7 1.02 = $8.97, stated $9.25 \\\\u2014 drives holdover at 150%\\\"},\\n intro=\\\"Departure at Year 10 only \\\\u2014 the final year of the term, which sets the holdover rent. Base rent overstated by $6,160.00 for that year; holdover rent overstated by $9,240.00 per annum ($305,250.00 stated against $296,010.00 on the corrected base).\\\")\\nappx_table(doc, \\\"A.5  Verdana Software Solutions \\\\u2014 3% compounding, $34.00/RSF, 18,750 RSF\\\", 34.00, 0.03,\\n [\\\"34.00\\\",\\\"35.02\\\",\\\"36.07\\\",\\\"37.15\\\",\\\"38.26\\\",\\\"39.41\\\",\\\"40.59\\\",\\\"41.81\\\",\\\"43.06\\\",\\\"44.35\\\"], 18750, 2, 2022, 7,\\n intro=\\\"All ten years conform exactly to the stated mechanism. No departures.\\\")\\nappx_table(doc, \\\"A.6  The Pint & Platter \\\\u2014 CPI-U with 2% floor / 4% cap, $18.000/RSF, 4,400 RSF\\\", 18.000, 0.0,\\n [\\\"18.000\\\",\\\"18.684\\\",\\\"19.431\\\",\\\"19.917\\\",\\\"20.315\\\"], 4400, 3, 2020, 10,\\n note_map={2:\\\"+3.80% \\\\u2014 within band\\\",3:\\\"+4.00% \\\\u2014 at cap\\\",4:\\\"+2.50% \\\\u2014 within band\\\",5:\\\"+2.00% \\\\u2014 at floor\\\"},\\n intro=\\\"The mechanism is index-linked, so this table compares each stated rate with the prior stated rate and shows the implied annual movement against the 2% floor and 4% cap. All movements fall within the band. Because Year 5 sits exactly on the floor, the underlying CPI-U movement should be confirmed against Bureau of Labor Statistics data.\\\")\\nappx_table(doc, \\\"A.7  United States of America (GSA) \\\\u2014 flat in firm term, 2.5% compounding in soft term, 15,000 RSF\\\", 31.50, 0.025,\\n [\\\"31.50\\\",\\\"31.50\\\",\\\"31.50\\\",\\\"31.50\\\",\\\"31.50\\\",\\\"32.29\\\",\\\"33.10\\\",\\\"33.93\\\",\\\"34.78\\\",\\\"35.64\\\"], 15000, 2, 2021, 1,\\n note_map={10:\\\"$34.78 \\\\u00d7 1.025 = $35.65, stated $35.64 \\\\u2014 one cent, immaterial\\\"},\\n intro=\\\"Firm-term rows are flat by design, so the shaded rows there reflect the deliberate absence of escalation rather than an error; the mechanism is applied only from Year 6. One one-cent departure at Year 10, with no economic significance, and the soft term is terminable on 120 days' notice in any event.\\\")\\n\\n# ================= APPENDIX B =================\\nh1(doc, \\\"APPENDIX B\\\", \\\"Source Document Index\\\")\\nrows = [\\n [\\\"D1\\\",\\\"portfolio-rent-roll.xlsx\\\",\\\"Rent Roll sheet (7 lease rows + total) and Summary sheet (aggregate statistics, concentration, WALT methodology notes, 9 numbered notes)\\\",\\\"Prepared by Karen Osgood, Property Manager, dated 1 December 2024. States that figures are \\\\u201cas stated in underlying lease documents\\\\u201d and have not been independently verified.\\\"],\\n [\\\"D2\\\",\\\"engagement-letter.docx\\\",\\\"Engagement terms: purpose, scope 2(a)\\\\u2013(f), 12 abstraction categories, deliverables, $45,000 fee cap, timeline, client responsibilities, limitations\\\",\\\"Dates the due diligence period and the PSA. Source of the $2,347,843.50 estimate and the 156,650 RSF scope.\\\"],\\n [\\\"D3\\\",\\\"apex-fulfillment-lease.docx\\\",\\\"Articles I\\\\u2013XX (definitions, premises, term, rent, NNN, use and exclusive use, assignment, subordination, TI, maintenance, insurance, renewal, ROFR, holdover, default, indemnity, estoppel, notices, miscellaneous, parking); Exhibits A\\\\u2013D\\\",\\\"Full lease text reviewed. No amendments or guaranty.\\\"],\\n [\\\"D4\\\",\\\"soto-dds-lease.docx\\\",\\\"Articles 1\\\\u201322 (definitions and basic lease provisions, premises, term, rent, use, utilities, insurance, TI, maintenance, parking, assignment, subordination, indemnity, casualty, condemnation, default, surrender, notices, renewal, early termination, personal guaranty, miscellaneous); Exhibits A\\\\u2013D\\\",\\\"Full lease text reviewed, including the Exhibit D early termination worksheet.\\\"],\\n [\\\"D5\\\",\\\"brightpath-lease.docx\\\",\\\"Articles 1\\\\u201319 (basic information, premises, term, rent, NNN provisions, security deposit, use and exclusive use, maintenance, insurance, environmental, assignment and recapture, renewal, access, casualty, condemnation, default, subordination, notices, miscellaneous); Exhibits A\\\\u2013D\\\",\\\"Full lease text reviewed. No TI allowance (Exhibit D \\\\u00a7 3).\\\"],\\n [\\\"D6\\\",\\\"se-fire-safety-lease.docx\\\",\\\"Articles 1\\\\u201318 (definitions, premises, term and renewal, rent, NNN, use, insurance, maintenance, assignment, alterations, indemnity, default, holdover, hazardous materials, casualty and condemnation, subordination, notices, miscellaneous); Exhibits A\\\\u2013B\\\",\\\"Full lease text reviewed, including the Article 14 environmental regime.\\\"],\\n [\\\"D7\\\",\\\"verdana-software-lease.docx\\\",\\\"Articles I\\\\u2013XXVIII (basic information through miscellaneous, limitation of liability, exhibits), including Article XIII expansion, Article XIV contraction, Article XV parking, Article XVII subordination, Article XXIV estoppel; Exhibits A\\\\u2013E\\\",\\\"Full lease text reviewed. Landlord represented no mortgage on the building as at 28 February 2022 (\\\\u00a7 17.02).\\\"],\\n [\\\"D8\\\",\\\"pint-platter-lease.docx\\\",\\\"Articles 1\\\\u201318 (definitions, premises and term, rent and CPI escalation and percentage rent, security deposit, use and exclusive use and radius restriction, operating expenses, maintenance, insurance, assignment, co-tenancy, renewal, SNDA, indemnity, default, casualty and condemnation, surrender, notices, miscellaneous); Exhibits A\\\\u2013D incl. Personal Guaranty\\\",\\\"Full lease text reviewed, including the Exhibit D guaranty burn-off.\\\"],\\n [\\\"D9\\\",\\\"gsa-lease.docx\\\",\\\"Sections 1\\\\u201320 (lease information summary, premises, term, rent, operating expenses, services, TI, assignment, insurance, security and SCIF, telecommunications, lessor alterations, casualty and condemnation, default, quiet enjoyment, subordination and non-disturbance, environmental, notices, miscellaneous, parking); Exhibits A\\\\u2013C\\\",\\\"Full lease text reviewed. No renewal option; no amendments or supplemental lease agreements provided.\\\"],\\n]\\nadd_table(doc, [\\\"ID\\\",\\\"File reviewed\\\",\\\"Contents reviewed\\\",\\\"Completeness notes\\\"], rows, [0.3,1.35,2.9,2.15], size=7.4, head_size=7.2,\\n          align_center_cols=(0,), keep_rows=True)\\nsource_note(doc, \\\"No document in the file identifies itself as an amendment, side letter, estoppel certificate, SNDA, sublease or commencement date memorandum. The absence should be confirmed by Seller certification rather than assumed (Risk R-23).\\\")\\n\\n# ================= APPENDIX C ======