{"turn": 46, "role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call_00_gSYvv9fzTdwKoTDk7X282355", "tool_name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && for i in 9 10 11 31 38 40 42; do echo \\\"=========== PAGE $i ===========\\\"; pdftotext -f $i -l $i -layout work/pdf/lease-abstraction-report.pdf - | head -40; done\"}", "result": "=========== PAGE 9 ===========\nBIRCHWOOD & HALE LLP | Lease Abstraction Report — Thornfield Realty Holdings LP Portfolio | Privileged &\nConfidential / Attorney Work Product\n\n\n ID    Document                            Forma    Parties / addressee             Date     Scope of document reviewed\n                                             t\n\n D9    GSA Lease No. GS-04B-15678           DOCX    Lessor: Thornfield Realty      30 Sep    5th Floor, Concord Office\n       (Form L201D)                                 Holdings LP / Lessee: USA       2020     Tower; Ex. A–C\n                                                    (GSA Region 4)\n\nNo amendments, side letters, guaranties (other than the Pint & Platter guaranty at Exhibit D to D8 and the Soto guaranty at\nArticle 21 of D4), SNDAs, estoppel certificates, subleases, commencement date memoranda, or operating expense\nreconciliations were provided. See Section 10.\n\n\n2.3 Method\n    • Inventory and control. All nine documents were inventoried before analysis and are listed in\n      Section 2.2 and Appendix B. The Engagement Letter was treated as the controlling instruction for\n      the form and content of this Report.\n    • Full-text review. Each lease was read in full, including recitals and exhibits, rather than relying\n      on the Rent Roll's summary. Facts were extracted with section citations and recorded in a source-\n      to-issue log.\n    • Independent recomputation. Every rent schedule was recomputed year by year from the stated\n      starting rent, the stated escalation mechanism and the stated rentable area, and compared with\n      the rate table in the lease and with the Rent Roll (Section 6 and Appendix A). Every percentage\n      share, allowance, amortisation and fee was recomputed from first principles.\n    • Date arithmetic. Commencement and expiration dates, option notice deadlines and notice\n      periods were recomputed from the operative clauses rather than accepted as stated, including the\n      Engagement Letter's own due diligence period.\n    • Reconciliation and flagging. Differences were classified by cause (rounding, drafting error in a\n      single year, error propagating through the term, or a genuine conflict between provisions). Where\n      a conflict exists between two provisions of the same lease, the conflict is described and the\n      probable controlling provision identified; where it cannot be resolved on the documents, it is\n      flagged for follow-up rather than silently resolved.\n    • Separation of fact from judgement. Extracted facts are presented in the abstraction tables; our\n      characterisation and conclusions appear in Sections 1, 3 and 7; open questions are collected in\n      Section 10. Risk ratings are our assessment and are explained in Section 7.1.\n\n2.4 Conventions and limitations\n=========== PAGE 10 ===========\nBIRCHWOOD & HALE LLP | Lease Abstraction Report — Thornfield Realty Holdings LP Portfolio | Privileged &\nConfidential / Attorney Work Product\n\n\n   • No verification of tenant assertions. Nothing in this Report verifies any fact stated in a lease by\n     a tenant, or the truth of any representation made by the Seller or the Rent Roll. See Section 11.\n\n\n\n\n                        Galleon Capital Advisors LLC · December 20, 2024 · Page 10 of 50\n\f=========== PAGE 11 ===========\nBIRCHWOOD & HALE LLP | Lease Abstraction Report — Thornfield Realty Holdings LP Portfolio | Privileged &\nConfidential / Attorney Work Product\n\n\nSECTION 3\n\nPortfolio-Level Analysis\n\n3.1 Rent-at-risk: what is and is not firm\nThree of the seven tenancies are not firm beyond twelve months. Each fails in a different way, and\neach requires a different remedy, so they are analysed separately rather than aggregated.\n\nSoutheastern Fire & Safety — expired lease, at-will holdover\nThe ten-year term expired on June 30, 2024. The tenant's single five-year renewal option required\nwritten notice by April 1, 2024 and lapsed unexercised, so no renewal right remains. Since July\n1, 2024 the tenant has occupied month-to-month at 150% of the final month's rent — $25,437.50\nper month, $305,250 per annum — and either party may terminate on 30 days' written notice\n(Article 13). There is no security deposit, no guaranty and no letter of credit. The tenant is\ntherefore paying a 50% premium but can leave at any time, and the Landlord can require it to\nleave at any time on 30 days' notice. For a purchaser this is 13.0% of aggregate rent that is both\nterminable at will by the tenant and unsupported by credit enhancement. It is also the tenancy that\ncarries the most significant environmental exposure in the portfolio, since the permitted use\nexpressly includes storage and handling of aqueous film-forming foam, foam concentrates and\nPFAS-containing materials (Article 14).\n\nGSA — twelve months of firm term, then terminable at will\nThe firm term runs from January 1, 2021 to December 31, 2025. After the firm term expiration date\nthe lease continues for a five-year soft term during which the Government may terminate at any\ntime on not less than 120 calendar days' written notice, with no termination fee, penalty or\nliquidated damages (§ 3.2). The lease states expressly that soft-term rent is “contingent upon the\nGovernment's continued occupancy and is not guaranteed beyond the Firm Term Expiration Date”.\nThe Rent Roll nonetheless includes the full $472,500 in the aggregate. In substance Galleon is\nbuying twelve months of government rent with an option over the following five years at the\nGovernment's sole election.\n\nDr. Miriam Soto — contractual but terminable on payment of a modest fee\nThe term runs to October 31, 2028, but Article 20 gives the tenant a right to terminate effective\nOctober 31, 2025 on 60 days' notice (deliverable by April 30, 2025) and payment of $40,657.14. We\nrecomputed the fee: unamortised TI allowance of $38,400 × 3/7 = $16,457.14, plus three months'\nbase rent of $96,800 ÷ 4 = $24,200.00, total $40,657.14 — consistent with the lease and with\n=========== PAGE 31 ===========\nBIRCHWOOD & HALE LLP | Lease Abstraction Report — Thornfield Realty Holdings LP Portfolio | Privileged &\nConfidential / Attorney Work Product\n\n\n5.6 The Rent Roll's weighted average term and implied cap rate\nWeighted average remaining term is dealt with at Section 1.5: the stated figures of ~5.7 and\n~4.6 years are not reproducible, and the independently computed figures are 5.25 years (GSA soft\nterm included) and 4.25 years (GSA firm term only). The Rent Roll's own methodology note\nacknowledges that the treatment of the Southeastern holdover and of the GSA firm versus soft\nterm “materially affects the calculation”, but does not explain the ~0.4 year gap.\nImplied cap rate of ~1.25%. The Rent Roll correctly flags that this figure reflects annual rent of\n$2,347,843.50 over the full portfolio purchase price of $187,500,000 and that it is not indicative of\nthe portfolio cap rate. We agree, and would go further: the figure has no analytical value and\nshould not be carried into any internal Galleon material, because (i) it uses rent rather than net\noperating income, so it ignores recoveries and expenses entirely; and (ii) it sets the rent of seven\nleases against the price of twelve properties. For reference only, the acquisition price equates to\n$769.55 per RSF across the whole portfolio (243,650 RSF) and $1,196.94 per RSF if notionally\nallocated to the 156,650 RSF covered by these seven leases. Neither figure is a valuation\nconclusion.\n\n\n\n\n                        Galleon Capital Advisors LLC · December 20, 2024 · Page 31 of 50\n\f=========== PAGE 38 ===========\nBIRCHWOOD & HALE LLP | Lease Abstraction Report — Thornfield Realty Holdings LP Portfolio | Privileged &\nConfidential / Attorney Work Product\n\n\n  ID    Finding and consequence                                   Severity    Timing       Required action\n\n R-22   Engagement Letter due diligence period stated as            Low      Immediate     Confirm the contractual due diligence\n        77 days but is 76 days measured from the stated                                    expiry against the PSA and diarise\n        commencement date of 16 November 2024 (77 days                                     every deadline in Section 8 against\n        runs from the PSA date of 15 November 2024).                                       the confirmed date.\n\n R-23   Lease-file completeness and document hygiene.               Low      Pre-closing   Obtain a Seller certification that each\n        No amendments, side letters, commencement date                                     lease file is complete and that no side\n        memoranda, estoppels or SNDAs were provided for                                    letter, amendment or unrecorded\n        any lease. The BrightPath document retains a Word                                  agreement exists; obtain the\n        field placeholder; the Verdana rules contain a                                     commencement date memoranda that\n        typographical error; the Apex rounding note does not                               the Verdana lease required under §\n        match its figures.                                                                 3.04, and any others that exist.\n\n R-24   The Apex lease contains no casualty or                      Low       Pre-DD       Confirm with Seller whether an\n        condemnation article. There is no express rent                        expiry       amendment supplies these provisions;\n        abatement, repair obligation or termination right on                               otherwise note that North Carolina\n        damage or taking.                                                                  law and the PSA govern, and disclose\n                                                                                           the position to the lender if it requires\n                                                                                           casualty provisions.\n\n R-26   The Soto Base Year of calendar 2022 falls inside            Low      Pre-closing   Obtain the 2022 base-year operating\n        the lease term, so the tenant's recovery obligation                                expense statement and model\n        begins from a base that already reflects a full year of                            recoveries on the true incremental\n        its own occupancy — a drag on recoveries relative to a                             basis.\n        pre-commencement base year.\n\n\n\n\n                            Galleon Capital Advisors LLC · December 20, 2024 · Page 38 of 50\n\f=========== PAGE 40 ===========\nBIRCHWOOD & HALE LLP | Lease Abstraction Report — Thornfield Realty Holdings LP Portfolio | Privileged &\nConfidential / Attorney Work Product\n\n\n  #   Action                                                             Risk(s)             Responsible         Deadline\n\n 16   Obtain the security deposit ledger and transfer/credit             R-15, R-21              Seller         28 Feb 2025\n      mechanics for BrightPath ($25,440) and Pint & Platter\n      ($19,800); obtain the guaranty originals for Soto and Pint &\n      Platter.\n\n 17   Obtain certified trailing-twelve-month gross sales for Pint &      R-21                    Seller         31 Jan 2025\n      Platter and any guaranty release executed under Exhibit D § 2.\n\n 18   Obtain current financial statements for Apex, Verdana and          R-21             Galleon / Crestline   31 Jan 2025\n      Southeastern; consider credit enhancement or a price\n      adjustment for the unsecured 65.5% of aggregate rent.\n\n 19   Obtain a Seller certification that the lease files are complete,   R-23, R-24              Seller         31 Jan 2025\n      that no side letters or amendments exist, and that all\n      commencement date memoranda have been delivered.\n\n 20   Confirm the due diligence expiry date against the PSA and re-      R-22                    B&H             Immediate\n      diarise every deadline in Section 3.6 and this table.\n\n 21   Re-run the valuation model on firm rent only (WALT 4.25            R-03, R-04,      Galleon / Crestline   31 Jan 2025\n      years), with the GSA soft term and the Southeastern holdover       R-05, R-06,\n      probability-weighted, the Verdana expansion encumbrance            R-11\n      reflected, and the Soto termination modelled.\n\nSection 2(d) of the Engagement Letter requires the firm to flag time-sensitive items without waiting for the delivery of this\nReport. Two items meet that description and were raised on delivery: the Apex ROFR question (R-01) and the GSA structural\nissues (R-02), both of which affect whether and how the transaction can close.\n\n\n\n\n                            Galleon Capital Advisors LLC · December 20, 2024 · Page 40 of 50\n\f=========== PAGE 42 ===========\nBIRCHWOOD & HALE LLP | Lease Abstraction Report — Thornfield Realty Holdings LP Portfolio | Privileged &\nConfidential / Attorney Work Product\n\n\n   • Copies of all SNDAs, subordination agreements and mortgages affecting each property, for\n     coordination with Stonebridge's title review.\n   • Current certificates of insurance for all seven tenants, and confirmation that any required\n     additional-insured endorsements are in place.\n   • The 2021 GSA Base Year operating expense statement (required to have been delivered by 31\n     March 2022) and the 2022 base-year statements for Millbrook Medical Plaza.\n   • The 2024 billing ledgers, aged receivables and percentage rent statements for all seven tenants.\n   • Any notice, correspondence or claim from a tenant relating to options, exclusive use, co-tenancy,\n     CAM reconciliation or default.\n   • Confirmation of the ROFR Notice position for Apex and any recorded memorandum affecting\n     Building C (to be obtained through Stonebridge).\n\n\n\n\n                        Galleon Capital Advisors LLC · December 20, 2024 · Page 42 of 50\n\f"}
