arranged through the                                  mortgage without consent; SNDA only if the\n                  Contracting Officer                                       Government requests (Art. 16)\n\nConsequence: for five of the seven leases Galleon has no contractual right to an estoppel at all, and for none of the seven is\nthere a non-disturbance agreement in place. The PSA should therefore carry an express estoppel condition covering each\ntenant, and the lender's SNDA requirements should be tested against the Apex, Southeastern and GSA provisions before the\nfinancing commitment is finalised.\n\n\n3.6 Option and notice deadlines\nThe following dates are computed from the operative notice provisions. Dates marked “open now”\nhave already begun to run and require immediate attention.\n Lease            Right or obligation            Notice period                 Key date                                      Risk\n\n Apex             ROFR over Building C           30 days from delivery of a    On any triggering offer — may have            R-01\n                                                 ROFR Notice                   been triggered by the PSA (15 Nov\n                                                                               2024)\n\n Apex             Renewal option 1 / option      12 months before expiry       31 May 2028 / 31 May 2033                     R-18\n                  2\n\n Dr. Miriam       Early termination notice       6 months before effective     30 April 2025 — 46 days after target          R-05\n Soto                                            date                          closing\n\n Dr. Miriam       Renewal option                 9 months before expiry        31 January 2028\n Soto\n\n BrightPath       Renewal option 1               12 months before expiry       31 March 2031\n\n Southeastern     Renewal option                 90 days before expiry         Lapsed — 1 April 2024; no renewal             R-04\n                     