{"turn": 62, "role": "assistant", "text": "All checks pass. Let me write the summary note.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_48x3CuRW6DRBu15ZOUuy0737", "name": "write", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"response.md\", \"content\": \"# Lease Abstraction Report — Thornfield Portfolio (7 leases)\\n\\n**Deliverable:** `lease-abstraction-report.docx` — 49 pages, ~26,400 words, 53 tables. Validated against the ECMA-376 WordprocessingML schema.\\n\\n## What was done\\n\\nRead all nine source documents in full (seven leases, the rent roll, the engagement letter), built a source-to-issue log with article/section citations, and **independently recomputed** every rent schedule, percentage share, allowance, amortisation, fee and date rather than relying on the rent roll's summary. The report follows the engagement letter's required structure: twelve-category abstractions per lease (§2(e)), rent roll cross-check (§2(b)), escalation verification (§2(c)), risk matrix by severity and time-sensitivity (§2(d)), executive summary (§2(f)) and pre-closing actions (§3).\\n\\n**Structure:** cover → contents → §1 Executive Summary → §2 Scope & Method → §3 Portfolio Analysis → §4 Seven Lease Abstractions → §5 Rent Roll Cross-Check → §6 Schedule & Date Verification → §7 Risk Register (26 items) → §8 Pre-Closing Actions → §9 Estoppel Checklist → §10 Open Items → §11 Limitations → Appendices A (year-by-year recomputation for all seven leases), B (source index), C (abbreviations).\\n\\n## Headline findings\\n\\n- **Aggregate rent ties exactly:** $2,347,843.50 reconciles to both the rent roll and the engagement letter; all 16 data fields checked per lease agree except one.\\n- **WALT overstated.** Rent roll states ~5.7 / ~4.6 years; recomputation on the rent roll's own stated method gives **5.25 / 4.25 years** — not reproducible on any alternative weighting basis.\\n- **37.2% of rent is not firm:** Southeastern at-will holdover (13.0%), GSA with 12 months of firm term then 120-day cancellation (20.1%), Soto option expiring 30 Apr 2025 (4.1%). Firm rent excluding the two at-will tenancies is $1,570,093.50 (66.9%).\\n- **Critical: Apex ROFR.** Article XIII is triggered by a *portfolio* sale and requires notice *before* the seller executes — the PSA was signed 15 Nov 2024 over a portfolio containing Building C.\\n- **GSA lease is senior to any mortgage and cannot be assigned without federal consent** — obstacles to financing and to an asset-level closing.\\n- **Verdana expansion option** fixes below-market rent on a further 18,500 RSF with a $740,000 allowance; the window is already open.\\n- **Three rent schedules break their own escalation formulas** (Apex Yr 5, BrightPath Yr 8, Southeastern Yr 10). Net current-year overstatement **$7,265**, concentrated in the Southeastern holdover ($9,240). Verdana, Soto and GSA conform.\\n- **Only 2 of 7 leases oblige a tenant estoppel; no SNDA exists for any lease.**\\n- Minor date inconsistency in the engagement letter itself (77-day DD period is 76 days from the stated start date).\\n\\nEach finding is tied to a numbered risk (R-01…R-26) with a severity, timing band, and an assigned action and deadline in §8, sequenced against the 31 Jan 2025 due-diligence expiry and 15 Mar 2025 target closing.\\n\"}"}], "input_tokens": 313669, "output_tokens": 874, "finish_reason": "completed"}
